- 35.7.9/8.7.18/8.5.8 — Computronium worktree 4 — sample from 2012 — closed — complete 2026-11-16. COMPLETE 2026-11-16 (~07:36 CST), hub ~/chromium-census/worktree-2012/ (STATE.md + PROVENANCE.md). Provenance: last commit of calendar 2012 — src c9523469b743 (2012-12-31, svn trunk r174787), Chrome 26.0.1374.0 dev trunk; census clone was depth-1 so the tree was fetched by exact SHA from github.com/chromium/chromium and hash-verified (HEAD^{tree} 4858b1850… matches the API record). WebKit DEPS pin r138552 acquired EXACTLY (e52cd1bfca39). v8 pin r13282 unreachable (svn-era) — substituted on the record: bleeding_edge@13291, last v8 commit of 2012. skia r6910 not acquired (svn hosts gone); in-tree skia glue only. Sizes: src 45,808 files / 9,686,972 physical lines / 6,048,731 code; combined (src+WebKit+v8) 251,010 files / 22,615,923 physical / 10,046,426 code — the whole 2012 browser is ~10M code lines, 2x the 5M budget before dedup (vs 140.6M today). Encode round-trip: 251,011/251,011 scrolls verified, 0 mismatches. Build: 288,095 function instances → 157,657 canonical + 130,438 standoffs; lines avoided 841,308 (16.8% of function-body lines); resolved 21,905,053 physical lines — function dedup alone does not reach 5M on 2012 either; the mass is non-function content (LayoutTests 185,581 files). Cross-stratum: 2,773 behavior groups span repos (454 in all three strata). Caveat: normalized-body identity collapses all empty bodies into one group — standoff counts are dominated by trivial bodies; avoided lines is the meaningful figure. Types extracted (54,224 in src), not deduplicated per the needless-structure ruling.
