Notes:
- Issued in PH: DevSecOps chat 2026-11-15 23:51 CST, immediately after all deployment activity was consolidated into that chat (DEPLOYMENT-CONTEXT.md).
- Verified current state: qexo's signed channel today carries exactly one artifact — qexo itself. Fleet 19/19 ranch nodes on v1.5.0 via the signed channel (first channel-clean rollout, 2026-11-14); signer is aletheia-core (fingerprint A4E7277FB3EB0E589604BE5B506DBE3FC209E755); releases are GPG-signed manifest scrolls served on :8484, accepted only on signature + strictly-newer version + hash match (+ platform stamp v1.6.2/PR #27 v1.7.1); atomic swap, qexo.prev kept, doctor post-check, receipt scroll either way; auto timers OFF fleet-wide (Will's call to light).
- Gap: generalizing to arbitrary service artifacts (phext-lattice, markdown-wizard, SQ, register, etc.) requires a multi-artifact manifest in qexo — not present in the current design as recorded. awsbox is not a qexo node (fleet = 19 ranch nodes + Will's laptop) — standardizing awsbox publishing behind qexo requires enrolling awsbox. Both are named in the DevSecOps spec draft, staged one stage at a time.
- Correction pass 2026-11-15 (qexo chat coordination flag, verified against the record): base tree is quarterexo exo 609bab65 (v1.7.1 merge via PR #27 https://github.com/wbic16/quarterexo/pull/27); PR #25 (v1.6.2) closed superseded. Manifest grammar already carries artifact: stanzas under one signature (APK bundling, task 34.8.11/8.7.11/7.7.9) — Stage 1 EXTENDS that grammar (name/install action/service), no parallel format. Serve route serves only qexo-<version> names — naming/route generalization is Stage 1/2 scope. Fleet also reached v1.6.1 via the signed channel 2026-11-14 (19/19), first release signed by qexo's internal OpenPGP. Spec QEXO-DEPLOY-STANDARD.md updated in PH: DevSecOps files.
