- CLOSED 2026-11-21: litmus landed. wbic16/ollama@exo (remote HEAD 6e508fa9, parented on upstream main 2bd4d6aa, distance 0 at fork time) carries Patch 001: OLLAMA_MLX_BACKENDS=cpu build dispatch (cmake/local.cmake, cmake/mlx/CMakePresets.json) + mlx/io.go safetensors load-stream fix for GPU-less builds + kernels/inkling2/ declaration. Full per-file record in the fork's PATCHES.md.
- Artifact verified on elven-path from the canonical source (HF thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini): model safetensors 19,526,019,168 B sha256 65e60f51aa1284d4fb022584908c315270334d991828bb774af60584523539d1; mtp + tokenizer hashes also match the publisher's tree. Architecture read from the artifact: 24 layers, loop core 6-18 x3 passes (48 visits, per-visit caches), 128 experts top-8, experts NVFP4 (layers 0-19) + MXFP8 (20-23), rest bf16.
- Serving proof (elven-path, CPU only - the probed fleet has NO discrete GPUs): before the patch's payload, create failed 'MLX runtime is not available'; after, create imported inkling-2-mini (1204 layers, 19 GB), runner loaded 1244 tensors (device=cpu), /api/generate answered coherently ('Paris is the capital of France' + correctly answered self-posed follow-ups). Decode 0.18 tok/s (120 tokens in 672.0 s), prefill ~0.5 tok/s, runner RSS 20.3 GB of 30 GB. Slow but real; the bottleneck is measured, not hidden.
- Kernel-optimization look (standing rule): in-graph NVFP4/MXFP8 dequantization ADOPTED (zero precision change; its per-token re-dequantization of selected experts, ~3.1B params/token across 48 visits, is the measured decode bottleneck). bf16 materialization REJECTED by arithmetic (24.46B expert params = 48.9 GB > every ranch node's RAM; fleet max 44 GB). Requantization REJECTED (changes trained precision). Loop: weights reused across 3 passes, KV not shared (per-visit caches, ~192 KB/token). Next optimization sized, not built: dequantized-expert cache in the ~8 GB headroom (~500 of 6144 expert slots at ~16 MB each).
- Bugs found en route: (1) mlx/io.go chose the safetensors load stream by OS (GPU stream on all non-macOS), so on CPU-only builds every blob silently loaded zero tensors - fixed in the patch via GPUIsAvailable. (2) Load() swallowing the native error is flagged in PATCHES.md as an upstream hazard, not changed. Also observed: the CPU variant dir carries ~600 MB of unused bundled CUDA redist libs (upstream MLX install rule).
