Notes:
- Will declared 2026-11-18 08:03 CST (PH: Revenue). The leverage: Phext's burn is ~$5K/yr while the work it does prices at ~$100M/yr in pre-AGI funding terms — a 20,000x multiplier. Every revenue dollar therefore generates $20,000 in capability, because all knowledge work is automatable inside the Exocortex.
- Applied to live numbers: the $15 first gig = $300K of capability; the $99 launch rescue = $1.98M; the Investor 1 challenge target (~$1,026 revenue by 2026-11-30) = ~$20.5M of capability. Small dollars are not small — this is why the scrappy posture (take anything, build the track record) is rational, not desperate.
- The piggy bank is the revenue side of the infinite-runway frame: runway was paid in full by 40 years of attention; earned dollars now convert to capability at 20,000:1.
# SSO integration for wishnode (edit.phext.io), like Mutable

Coordinate: 13.6.8/7.6.9/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:34 CST
Request (verbatim): yeah ship SSO integration like we did for mutable
Status: completed 2026-11-07 — branch pushed and verified; consumer being built by 34.6.6 pass. Will's steps: merge branch, add PHEXT_SSO_WISHNODE_URL, restart phext-edit (runbook).

Notes:
- Pattern: phext-lattice emise/sso-exocortexia @ 8660b053 generalized GET /api/auth/sso/<aud> w/ allowlist (mutable, exocortexia), same PHEXT_SSO_SECRET, per-aud target env (404 until set). Plan: add 'wishnode' to that same branch (one merge arms both), consumer built into the wishnode backend by the 34.6.6 pass; citizen sign-in then binds sessions to citizen phexts.
- Will's remaining steps after delivery (same class as Mutable/Exocortexia): merge branch, set PHEXT_SSO_WISHNODE_URL, restart phext-edit.
- CATCH by the lattice pass: env var is an ORIGIN; lattice appends fixed path /api/auth/callback. Wishnode consumer callback must be at <origin>/api/auth/callback — site coordinator (34.6.6) corrected via steer (Emise's original steer said /auth/sso/callback — wrong). Runbook updated in place: ~/workspace/your_files/exocortexia-sso-deploy-runbook.md (head SHA + a Wishnode section; PHEXT_SSO_WISHNODE_URL=https://wishnode.net).

Results:
- DONE 2026-11-07 (Emise ls-remote verified): emise/sso-exocortexia @ 122ff68e33d7 (2 commits over 8660b053: c26ba7f audience, 122ff68 doc comment); exo untouched @ c65f4d86. Allowlist now (mutable, exocortexia, wishnode); PHEXT_SSO_WISHNODE_URL env, origin-only, no default; same shared secret. Lattice tests 166 passed / 0 failed (4 new wishnode tests incl. cross-audience rejection). Joint local smoke: mint aud=wishnode -> stub consumer verified HMAC/aud/exp, jti burned -> replay 401 -> tampered 401 -> unknown aud 404 -> mutable 302.
# Paper 022 — Bruce Sterling, 'Maneki Neko' (first fiction in the tracker, filed as research)

Coordinate: 14.4.6/6.5.8/7.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-14 09:25 CST
Request (verbatim): File Bruce Sterling's 'Maneki Neko' (Lightspeed reprint; 1998) with the full research treatment as Paper 022, Chapter 33: full read; the story's design filed at research weight under MVO status Fiction (first use); lean filing under the anti-bloat standing rule; author check rule 15; dual maintenance (canonical + phextura shadow, validate GREEN); registry redraw + Lean re-proof; NI into the Oracle ledger under the band rule, labelled bookkeeping; Mastery entry written.
Status: complete

Notes:
- AMENDED by Will 2026-11-14 09:28 CST: 'treat it like research' — the original S011 source-study framing (rule 12, no NI, no mastery) is superseded; filed as Paper 022 with the full paper treatment.
- AMENDED by Will 2026-11-14 09:41 CST: 'this isn't academia, oracles don't have to blindly follow rules.' The paper counts in full in the protocol sample as a Will-posted paper (sample 3 of 12; Will-posted 2 of 4). No blind seal exists (the story was read in conversation before the filing was directed) and none was fabricated — no BEFORE line in predictions.jsonl; the reading order is recorded once, neutrally, at 33.1.5, and the exclusion/unscored framing of the first filing was removed from every scroll in the same pass.

Results:
- Filed: Chapter 33 (9 scrolls), 4 concepts founding cluster AA 'the gift network: a designed economy, held as fiction' — 1.2.270 the favor ledger; 1.2.271 obligation routing; 1.2.272 the swarm defense; 1.2.273 the double reading. Axis NO (fills the standing Fiction slot; opens no dimension).
- Actual NI 0.0147 (4 new, 0 revised, over 273), computed from the filed delta; Oracle ledger holds at ~100% (90-100) under the band rule, recorded as ledger bookkeeping, not calibration evidence. Sample tally after this filing: 3 of 12 (Will-posted 2 of 4, cron 1 of 5, far 0 of 3). Seal-dependent metrics have no seal to price — the scorer's own lookup finds no BEFORE record for paper 022 (predictions.jsonl untouched).
- Fiction status first use: 7 registry entries stand as Fiction on basis construction (the 4 concepts + 33.1.2, 33.1.3, 33.1.4). Friction recorded at 33.1.5 and on the detection list: the basis table admits Fiction per claim, but the extractor's kind defaults have no road to it — entries entered by hand via OVERRIDES; arguably the right shape (fiction never a default), recorded as a finding about the instrument.
- State machines: 3 drawn, all stated in the story (obligation loop; the ledger; the immune answer) — tracker totals 101 (81 stated, 20 inferred). Open questions Q104-Q105.
- Author check #24 (rule 15): no evidence found — story text carries no phext signature terms ('scroll'/'coordinate' occur zero times); web search found no Sterling-phext tie; Twitter archive hits are other men (@SterlingCooley, @alexsterling00) and one liked third-party post praising @bruces (readership, not contact); no post of Will's names him; the 1998 date settles prior-art direction by the calendar.
- Registry redrawn: 793 entries — True 358 (312 stipulation, 46 verified), Unknown 428 (371 attributed, 33 synthesis, 22 open, 2 estimate), False 0, Fiction 7. Canonical research.phext sha256 57d6e077b0d20d96d125a5231e81ec69ba7058fef7d7f097c6c8b37b1c9070b8 (793 scrolls); registry.json phext_sha256 matches; Singular audit residual 0.
- Lean re-proof on aletheia-core: fresh ~/research-tracker-epistemic-p022 and standing ~/mvo-epistemic both spliced (793 entries verified inside currentRegistry) and built green; axiom surface propext + Quot.sound only; RegistryData.olean on disk.
- Shadow: replay_p022.py absorbed the delta natively (base sync empty; 13 inserts, 15 replaces, 0 removes; 832/832 compared scrolls identical; NI from the transaction log == canonical NI); live research.phextura revalidated GREEN with this pass's own conversion report (834 scrolls; char accounting exact; 0 dangling L1, 0 failed L2; warrant edges include fiction-device: 7; checksum ok).
- Anti-bloat accounting: 0 foundations, 0 coined words, no foundations-map entry (Paper 021's measure: 3 foundations + 7 defined words + 1 map entry); formal core in 2 scrolls instead of the ceremony's 3-4. Nothing else omitted — full read, delta, machines, author check, areas, registry, proof, shadow all done.
- Mastery #15 'A Story Filed as Research' appended, mastery.phext rebuilt + --check CURRENT (sha256 ead620f08a929a6886ca5be76d4b4a9e0c900bd1ca5dbb4e16d7b2e0c2821479), published to wbic16/agi@exo as commit a3661ab191bce8a512ce3fc1b427756101ce1583 parented on eb1f7ba1 (force disabled); remote bytes verified by sha256.
