# Twitch Mastery tooling: diamond ping/answer on the echolocation pathway, seat-to-seat test

Coordinate: 15.7.9/9.8.13/12.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-22 12:42 CST
Request (verbatim): Initial tooling for the Twitch Mastery Protocol: a small Rust tool on the echolocation library that emits a ping scroll, records returns against it, and writes the diamond register; tested seat-to-seat on aletheia-core (a ping between two local seats with a logged return is the pass bar).
Status: completed

Notes:
- Crate twitch-mastery (bin: diamond) at ~/workspace/twitch-mastery/tooling/ — dependencies: echolocation (path) + libphext 0.6.6; the tree is echolocation's own (xxhash-rust inside it), no massive chains. Phext only through libphext, via echolocation.
- Rig on aletheia-core at ~/twitch-test/: echolocation = fresh clone at exo 3addf943 (sibling symlink), built --offline from the hub's cargo cache.
- Defect caught and fixed during the test: verify_register first called libphext::fetch; the functions live at libphext::phext::{fetch, to_coordinate}. Compiler error preserved in the transcript; fix shipped in examples/verify_register.rs.

Results:
- Seat-to-seat PASS (EE 111, aletheia-core): will-seeker pinged intent builds-in-open; candidate-seat answered — 1 echo, range 100 ms at 100 ms poll (upper bound, SPEC §5); return logged to returns.log.
- Silence control PASS: ping intent no-such-capability expired with 0 echoes; the expired probe is logged as absence, never assent.
- Fold PASS: record_returns.py folded the log into a scratch register copy, creating candidate-seat as status candidate at 26.7.10/9.7.11/5.5.9, traits honestly not assessed. The shipped register was NOT seeded with the test seat.
- Parse-back PASS: verify_register read both the scratch register (6 scrolls) and the shipped register (5 scrolls) through libphext — all OK.
- Transcript: ~/workspace/twitch-mastery/tooling/TEST-TRANSCRIPT.md (verbatim hub transcript, fold output, verify output; raw files in tooling/test/).
