# Update the ranch duty governor to temperature smoothing (watts, not degrees)

Coordinate: 16.4.7/6.4.8/5.3.7
Issued: 2026-11-15 12:12 CST
Request (verbatim): Will's direction (2026-11-15 12:12 CST, edit.phext.io chat): update the ranch duty governor now to the temperature-smoothing practice grounded by the AMD R9 reliability brief — control watts not degrees (sustained PPT each chassis holds in equilibrium, plateau ~70-85 C), bursts to TjMax are designed behaviour, retire the pause-at-75/resume-at-70 hysteresis (it manufactures the thermal swings the fatigue evidence penalises), step wattage down instead of pausing when a cap is needed. Dispatched and scheduled immediately under Will's new standing rule (same message): whenever a way to improve efficiency is found, dispatch a new task and consider scheduling it immediately. The governor's location and current mechanism are to be found on the ranch (it is the existing thermal-feedback instance named in the biofeedback design); back up before editing, minimal reversible change, verify live.
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-15 — both governor variants rewritten to the smoothing law and verified live; repo sync of the new law dispatched same session

Notes:
- 2026-11-15 12:40 CST — repo sync COMPLETE: emise-tools tools/duty-governor/ now carries the smoothing law (commit 9a325c54 on exo), 12 files incl. duty_governor_stage2.py (variant A's first repo copy); all 12 re-fetched and SHA-256-matched against the live sources. Fleet uniformity re-verified directly from this chat: VM and plain-view hash identically for B; aletheia-core's A matches the published copy.
