# Duty-cycle management for the ranch: governed bursts inside the thermal band

Coordinate: 18.4.11/8.5.12/6.4.7
Issued: 2026-11-15 02:32 CST
Request (verbatim): Will's direction after the per-node soak sweep (task 24.5.7/7.6.11/6.6.8) showed every node breaches 75 C within ~2-3 min at any full-tilt count: sustained ranch work is managed as DUTY CYCLES. Build a per-node duty-cycle governor: it runs a workload as a process group and holds Tctl inside the band by SIGSTOP/SIGCONT (pause at 73 C, resume at <=70 C, Tctl sampled every few seconds from k10temp resolved by name — the die moves in seconds, the per-minute log is too slow to govern by). It complements the existing between-job policy (pause starts >=75, resume <=70, off-time to <=65 after an 80 C crossing; ranch-batchq, 2026-11-04) by governing INSIDE a job; work is never killed or throttled, only frozen and resumed. Test on three representative nodes (plain-view = worst, free-fall = closest to the line, one 8945HS) with the NLE bench, 30 min governed per node at 4 and at 8 instances: success = no Tctl sample >=75 anywhere in the run; deliverables per node = duty fraction, effective sustained steps/s, Tctl band stats, and the chosen scheduled profile (instances x duty) by effective rate. Extend node-limits.md with the duty-cycled sustained rates; publish the tool to wbic16/emise-tools in the same session (exec bit verified). First workload: the NetHack solver campaigns (Stage 2 steered to govern its search the same way).
Status: open

