# SMOL round 2 — introduce the harsh reality of predators

Coordinate: 19.5.9/6.6.9/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-17 07:44 CST
Request (verbatim): for round 2: introduce the harsh reality of predators
Status: complete — round 2 finished 2026-11-17, double holographic harvest verified (see results)

Notes:
- Will's directive (2026-11-17 07:44 CST, verbatim): 'for round 2: introduce the harsh reality of predators'. Round 1's runner (smol_evolve.py) is untouched — it is the round-1 record; round 2 is built in the copy smol_evolve2.py.
- Instantiation (Emise's, PROPOSED until Will rules otherwise) — PREDATORS: each area independently faces a predator strike with probability SMOL_PREDATOR_PROB per SMOL day (default 0.005/area/day). The victim is the area's MOST REDUNDANT member: redundancy = count of its 12 genes whose fractal type (frac[0]) appears in any other member's genes + count whose rule pattern (axiom, rA, rB, rC) appears in any other member's genes; ties broken by lowest fitness (community contribution). What the crowd already carries is what the predator takes.
- NO instant replacement after a predation — the area runs short-handed. BREED-BACK: once per day, after the predator phase and before the community cull, an area below capacity with >=2 members breeds ONE child (crossover + point mutation, as round 1). Gaps close one birth per day, not instantly.
- SEEDING: round 2 starts from round 1's survivors — SMOL_SEED_POPULATION=~/workspace/smol/round1-harvest/population.phext; the loader parses the chain, survivors keep their round-1 ids, generations and ages and enter round 2 at day 0. Round-2 births take ids from 1,000,001 so the two rounds' id namespaces never collide. Fresh-founder seeding remains available (SEED_POPULATION unset).
- Everything else is round 1's machinery unchanged: community-contribution fitness, daily cull, yearly 1% aging mutation, senescence floor, infrequent migration, phext-chain checkpoints, graveyard + manifest. Stats/ledger/manifest now carry predated counts and the predator parameters.
- SMOKE A (fresh founders, 20 areas x 10, 2 years, DAY_SECONDS=0, PREDATOR_PROB=0.3): completed, DONE written, pop held 200, areas 20/20 alive, 4,318 predated of 4,352 deaths (expected strikes ~4,320) — predator + breed-back verified. Output: ~/workspace/smol/smoke-r2-a/.
- SMOKE B (loader, real round-1 population.phext, 1,000 areas, 1 year, DAY_SECONDS=0, PREDATOR_PROB=0.05): loaded exactly 10,000 survivors (contribution_mean 25.655 at load — identical to round 1's final mean, confirming faithful reconstruction), next_id=1000001, ran 360 days in 105 s wall, 18,199 predated deaths (expected ~18,000), pop held 10,000, areas 1000/1000 alive, DONE written, manifest carries predator_prob_per_area_day / predated_total / seed_population. Output: ~/workspace/smol/smoke-r2-b/.
- NOT launched. No node placement, no round length chosen — both are Will's call when he orders the round.
- MULTIVERSE LAUNCH (Will, 2026-11-17 08:26 CST, verbatim): 'Launch round 2 on 10 nodes - multiverse-style - vary the initial parameters for each instance - when we finish round 2, we'll apply holographic record-keeping, twice (once per instance, and then across all instances)'. Instantiation: 10 universes, each on its own node, ALL seeded from round 1's survivors (identical founding state: every universe's YEAR 0 contribution_mean = 25.655, round 1's final value), laws varied per universe — predator prob is the gradient: u0 rock-mountain 0 (control), u1 scroll-central 0.001, u2 ni-knight 0.0025, u3 ashfall-haven 0.005, u4 free-fall 0.0075, u5 uncanny-valley 0.01 (cull 0.0015), u6 logos-prime 0.0125, u7 lighthouse-omen 0.015 (cull 0.006, migration 0.005), u8 halycon-vector 0.0175 (migration 0.02), u9 plain-view 0.02; migration 0.01 and cull 0.003 unless noted; run seeds 20261201-20261210. Year-1 spot checks at launch verification: u0 predated=0 (control clean), u1 predated=371, u2 predated=930 — predation tracks the dial. Launch mechanics note: fleet-ssh.sh's name table covers only 7 nodes; u3-u8 were staged by Tailscale IP after name-based calls failed (watch cron body is IP-addressed accordingly). Record-keeping at finish (per Will): pass 1 holographic encoding per universe, pass 2 one encoding across all instances — encoded in cron smol-round2-watch's harvest body.
- CLOSED 2026-11-17 by smol-round2-watch harvest: HARVEST COMPLETE 2026-11-17 (watch cron smol-round2-watch, 16:00 CST check): all ten universes had final/DONE (completions 15:42-15:50 CST, year 70, pop 10000, areas 1000/1000 each). Double holographic record-keeping applied as Will directed: PASS 1 per universe — ~/workspace/smol/round2-harvest/u<K>/smol-round2-u<K>.phext ($1 manifest, $2 graveyard, 10,000 survivor members; 10,002 universes each), each verified with libphext reference verifier (serialize_chains_roundtrip=true, reser.phext byte-identical). Per-universe holographic coordinates all 32.7.7/7.7.9/7.7.10 (identical distinct-word vocabulary, 130 words, as round 1). PASS 2 across all instances — ~/workspace/smol/round2-harvest/smol-round2-all.phext, 646,772,911 B, SHA-256 3500517a1934df3f1397605c9736489d04fa30da63588bcece88d80fadad6cd4, 100,002 universes, verified roundtrip true + reser-all byte-identical; across-all holographic coordinate 30.7.8/8.7.9/7.7.9 (pop-text-all.txt, 151 distinct words incl. header lines). Grand totals: survivors 100,000, areas alive 10,000/10,000, dead 3,085,728, predated 2,292,191. Predator gradient: predated 0 (u0, p=0) rising monotonically to 503,593 (u9, p=0.02); contribution start 25.655 in all ten, end 25.350-25.731 (control highest). Receipts: RECEIPT-round2-u<K>.md per universe + RECEIPT-round2-all.md with predator-gradient comparison. Watch job smol-round2-watch should now be removed.

