3,290/1,433,290 scrolls 0 mismatches + independent Python-parser cross-check clean; the gate caught and fixed a first-encode defect (1,920 legacy-encoding files silently emptied). Pools (lines): dep pool 100.31M code-ext (WebKit 29.73M largest; jetstream x4 copies 5.26M; vendored third_party 306 projects 14.81M); generated 16.73M (marker); exact-duplicate files 27.07M dup lines / 3.64 GB; function identity >=15tok 16.59M recoverable (multi-name: 83,833 groups / 562,374 fns / 4.91M lines); similar types 5.35M recoverable (49,631 clusters); versioned older copies 4.60M; boilerplate headers 4.09M; test pool 40.16M lines (26.9% — kept, verification contract); within-file repeated lines 98.87M (40.1%); param-delta 0.79M; platform extra variants 0.20M; BUILD.gn orphan candidates 1.73M (estimate). Compression bound: main repo effective unique ~10.7M lines; whole-tree unique ~35M (estimate) — dedup alone does not reach 5M; the residual is design elimination (one engine, deps as one chrome.phext, generated-from-schema, one canonical syntax) + Will's open scoping calls (what counts toward the 5M, subsystem scope, compatibility target). Census leg closed; task remains open on scoping. CENSUS INSCRIBED + PR (2026-11-16): CENSUS.md inscribed in artifacts.phext at 35.6.8/7.6.10/6.5.9 (human@exo e9af580d, remote bytes SHA-256 verified); PR https://github.com/wbic16/computronium/pull/1 open against exo (branch emise/census-2026-11-16 @ 34b9ce63) carrying CENSUS.md as the repo's first substantive artifact. Open scoping calls for Will: (1) does the 40.16M-line test corpus count toward the 5M budget; (2) which counting convention the 5M is scored against. NEXT STEP ruled by Will 2026-11-16 06:45 CST: place the code FUNCTION BY FUNCTION, with unified names that derive from what the functions do. Will's rationale, verbatim in substance: de-duplication at this scale will come from humans being small, so the duplication literally can't be seen. For each function store BOTH (1) the interna