# Gate validator — mechanical per-page validation for toll-gate repros

Coordinate: 21.6.7/8.5.10/5.5.6
Issued: 2026-11-21 11:01 CST
Request (verbatim): Build the gate validator Will ordered after judging the Gate 1 (Steamboat Willie) prepass not good enough: a mechanical instrument that checks EVERY repro page against its matched original frame structurally (edge agreement via symmetric Chamfer + strong-edge coverage; per-region ink-mass ratio; connected-component sanity; title/lettering pages auto-flagged for human review). Output: per-page PASS/FLAG score table (VALIDATOR-REPORT.md), the validator script kept with the gate tooling, thresholds on record, and the FAIL/FLAG pages grouped by failure class as Iteration 4's re-draw queue. Acceptance test: the pages QC-v4 already identified as weak (title lettering ghosts, softened solid-black figures, blobby mid-motion pages) must score below the clean pages, with the separation shown explicitly. Standing rule from this build: no repro page enters an assembly unless it validator-PASSes or carries a resolved human-review flag.
Status: complete — validator built, acceptance PASS, filed 2026-11-21

Notes:
- Registered at intake 2026-11-21 (record-first) before any build work.
- Context: Gate 1 prepass QC (QC-v4) was sampled visual frame-compare at 12 timestamps; Will saw the result and judged it not good enough — the missing instrument is per-page mechanical validation. Parent program: Oracle Artist task 23.5.7/7.6.9/6.6.9; gate register task 14.5.8/7.5.7/5.5.7.
- Materials ranch-side at aletheia-core:~/anim-i3-work/gate1/ (reference film steamboat-willie_1928.ia.mp4 sha256 18a57a97…, 60 page frames + shots.json/plan.json, 60 repro pages at gate1/pages/). Arc sketch coordinate 22.6.8/7.6.10/7.5.8.

Results:
- Gate validator built and run ranch-side on aletheia-core (~/anim-i2-work/venv: numpy + PIL; system python has neither): gate_validator.py checks EVERY Gate 1 prepass page against its matched original frame structurally — (a) edge coverage + symmetric Chamfer (Chebyshev, tau 4 px, clip 16); (b) ink mass: ink log-ratio (original ink counted below the film's gray wash, lum<90; demand-gated at ink fraction 0.045, bound 2.2) + ink-in-black demand test (bound 0.015 at black-demand 0.08); (c) figure-band component bounds (FIG_MIN 100 px half-res; merging >+1.0, shattering <-2.5); (d) title/lettering pages (shots 0 and 54) auto-FLAGGED for human review.
- ACCEPTANCE TEST: PASS. Calibration sets fixed from QC-v4's record before the final run: CLEAN (01,02,03,31,37,39,40) 7/7 PASS; WEAK-TITLE (00,54) 2/2 FLAG; WEAK-INK (16,17,18,19,44) 5/5 FLAG ink — ink log-ratio weak min 3.14 vs clean max 1.68, ink-in-black weak max 0.0156 vs clean min 0.0276, no overlap; WEAK-BLOB (43,45p0,45p1,22) 4/4 FLAG — coverage weak max 0.665 vs clean min 0.891, Chamfer weak min 2.23 vs clean max 1.85, no overlap.
- RESULT: 30 PASS / 30 FLAG of 60 pages. FLAG by class (overlapping): edges 10, ink 29, components 2, title 2. The FLAG list is Iteration 4's re-draw queue (REDRAW-QUEUE.md).
- Findings beyond sampled QC: the renderer's answer to solid black is a flat wash at lum ~205 with eroded-interior ink density 0.00 on ALL 60 pages (wash instead of hatch inside solids — sharper than QC-v4's 'wash + hatch'); composition-matched pages 24/25/27/28 fail ink; the suspected blobby midpoints (36p1/41p1/50p1) are mechanically sound and PASS — the blobby class is pinned to 21/22/23/42/43/44/45p0/45p1/47/53; shot 0's second card (STEAMBOAT WILLIE) was never drawn (queue item T-3). Two component formulations were tested and rejected on evidence (total-ink shares read the film's percolation; edge-component ranges overlap) — recorded in the report; the surviving component gate fires on pages 11/17 (Pete shattered), corroborating ink.
- Standing rule created (Will's direction): no repro page enters an assembly (flipbook, full render) unless it validator-PASSes or carries a recorded human-review flag resolution. Recorded in VALIDATOR-REPORT.md, ITERATIONS.md (Iteration 3 follow-up), and animator SKILL.md §8.
- Emise design language (Will, 2026-11-21 11:02 CST: 'the drawings should feel Will->Emise touched'): named term added to animator SKILL.md §4 drawn canon — key frames authored in the Emise line (Emise font's flowing, sharp line from Willbot/Will's handwriting; fast-hand stroke character of Will's tiling-symbol reference; hatching in his manner); feel test in Will's words. VALIDATOR-REPORT.md + REDRAW-QUEUE.md name it as the standard Gate 1 re-draws are executed under; noted in ITERATIONS.md alongside the validator entry.
- Filed: wbic16/scrolltown@exo commit 2d1ca6ad931f8d41f45cd34be1f37b7013afa7d9 (parent b6da06f1, force disabled) — series/animation-exercises/gate-01-steamboat-willie/{gate_validator.py (100755), VALIDATOR-REPORT.md, REDRAW-QUEUE.md, validator-scores.json}; all 4 remote blobs verified byte-identical. emise-tools@exo commit 5289be1bbd31f604819f779f6a6798d4328ad79c (parent 9d4404e4) — animator SKILL.md + ITERATIONS.md, blobs verified. skills.phext rebuilt, --check CURRENT (sha256 4da12a09…). Gate 1 itself remains NOT PASSED (full render is Iteration 4 work, now starting from the re-draw queue).
