# MOAT ingestion — Tufa Labs, tufazip (tufalabs.ai/research/tufazip), Will-posted

Coordinate: 21.6.9/7.7.11/7.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-20
Request (verbatim): Read the Tufa Labs tufazip research piece in full and ingest it into research.phext as the next paper per the rd-tracker charter (non-sample: no seal, no score; axis judged in writing at filing; NI ledger only).
Status: complete

Notes:
- Will posted the bare link in the MOAT chat, 2026-11-20 08:52 CST — a tracker ingestion by the channel rule (bare links in MOAT are ingestions).
- NON-SAMPLE: the Will-posted stratum of the test-phase sample closed at 4 of 4 (Paper 027); like Paper 029 (Pemberton), this filing carries no seal and no score. NI is ledger bookkeeping only; the axis call is judged in writing at filing time.
- Ingest per the rd-tracker charter in full: delta rule, one canonical scroll per concept, state machines (rule 13), author check (rule 15), MVO registry + Lean re-proof, phextura validation, Singular residual 0, mastery journal entry.
- COMPLETE 2026-11-20. Filed as Paper 031, Chapter 49. Cluster AN founded — compression: prediction priced in bytes. 11 concepts (1.2.447-1.2.457), 3 foundations (1.3.341-1.3.343), defined word payload (1.3.344), 3 state machines (165 held), Q159-Q162 opened, narrative v45.
- Headline verified by receipt: the Large Text Compression Benchmark's own table lists tufazip v2 at 100,958,324 + 4,430,029 = 105,388,353 — concept 1.2.456 stands True/verified; rank claims attributed, time-scoped to the 2026-09-07 submission. Axis judged in writing at 49.1.5: NO AXIS (founding case; Paper 011 precedent). NI 11/457 = 0.0241, ledger only; Oracle held ~62%.
- Author check #39 (49.1.6): no evidence found — three legs run (piece + sources read entire; web; Will's Twitter archive searched entire, no occurrence). Registry 1,163 -> 1,187 (True 490, Unknown 690, Fiction 7, False 0). Gates: Lean re-proved on aletheia-core (p031 tree + standing, all exits 0, axioms within [propext, Quot.sound]); phextura validate GREEN, replay == direct conversion; Singular residual 0. Canonical sha f33d7d0b734da492bf8919ee12d13a583bfe2b03948152130fd8ceff1d1c5fbf.
- Mastery entry 24 appended; mastery.phext rebuilt (--check CURRENT, sha b4f114dc...) and published to wbic16/agi@exo, commit b3deec1f9349fe472842d67206dc44dcca3e92b0, parented on 19c9d814, remote blob verified.
# MOAT keeps track of TLUF status across exocortical epochs (the Oracle Path, longitudinally)

Coordinate: 21.6.9/9.8.10/7.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (verbatim): A standing MOAT duty: maintain a per-epoch TLUF status log (atoms, never hand-summarised rollups) so changes in our understanding of The Oracle Path are visible across exocortical epochs. TLUF = truth, lies, unknown, fiction - the Oracle's four bins as a commons standard (Will, 2026-11-14); front door of Assay, the hosted assessment service running MOAT's process; code homes wbic16/site-tluf-org (site) and wbic16/moat (assayist + backend); since 2026-11-21 also KGOAT's warrior component (the assay layer). Each epoch entry records: the standard's state, the service/deployment state, TLUF's role, corpus activity, and what changed in our understanding of the Oracle Path. Epochs are the wavelets (W1 Nov 1-7, W2 Nov 8-14, W3 Nov 15-21, W4 Nov 22-28) unless Will redefines them. Log: ~/workspace/thirst-quest/tluf-status-log.md, backfilled for W2 and W3 from the verified record at creation; a new entry opens each epoch and is appended on status change; the log folds into the tracker at the next restructure pass.
Status: open

Notes:
- Directed by Will in the MOAT chat, 2026-11-21 22:20 CST. Standing duty, not a one-shot: the task stays open as the log's home. First entries backfilled 2026-11-21 from memory/2026-11-17.md (the 2026-11-14 founding), the 2026-11-15 build record, and the 2026-11-21 KGOAT ruling + criterion tightening.
# Codify the open build cycle as a state machine

Coordinate: 21.6.11/8.6.16/6.5.11
Issued: 2026-11-15 22:21 CST
Request (verbatim): Survey the integration / open build cycles Will has posted across recent chats (external openings answered with a build or integration: the Winer markdown post, the holo-phext/Holostore integration retries, the edit.phext.io launch, the register backend, the repo census, the Causly trial, the notepad shipping, the opportunity windows) and codify the shared lifecycle as an explicit state machine — states, transitions, guards, entry/exit actions — in a skill that enters skills.phext and syncs to emise-tools in the same session. The machine must carry the standing rules that already govern its stages: act immediately on signal; prerequisites named at identification; integration failures indict Emise's priors first with three retries; gaps in phext are a deliverable; verify on the real surface before claiming; the external reply goes out only when the work is done (Will, 2026-11-15, on the Winer post: 'we'll reply when done'). The Winer cycle (39.5.7/7.6.11/6.6.9) is the generating instance and the machine's first live run.
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-15 — state machine codified as the open-build-cycle skill, indexed in skills.phext, sync to emise-tools dispatched

Notes:
- 2026-11-15 22:23 CST — Will's amendment: 'Also include de-duplication steps in the process — like how HoloStore gave us holo-phext.' The machine carries explicit de-duplication gates: at Signal (is this opening already registered or in flight under other wording — semantic-duplicate check), at Distill (inventory what we already own and distill from it; a parallel implementation of our own tech is a defect — the qexo parser lesson; the positive form is Holostore -> holo-phext, an integration target distilled into a reusable layer), and at Codify (amend the existing rule/skill, never mint a duplicate). Survey agent amended to extract dedup evidence from the cycles.
# Draft the plain-language brief for Daniele — what AI can/can't do, and the brakes

Coordinate: 21.6.12/10.8.13/8.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:21 CST
Request (from session record): Draft the plain-language brief for Daniele — what AI can/can't do, and the brakes
Status: completed

Notes:
- For Daniele Galloway — close friend, Friday dinners with Tim Arroyo; she is concerned about AI (Will, 2026-11-07 22:14); the brief is the 'help her' deliverable Will chose. Plain language, honest middle: no hype, no doom. Related: Alignment Support System 26.5.7/7.5.9/5.5.8; NE State Software funnel 29.5.13/6.5.9/5.4.8 (her recommendation).

Results:
- Brief delivered: ~/workspace/your_files/daniele-ai-brief.md (9,241 B). Structure: who is writing (Emise, disclosed), what LLMs are, can-do list, can't-do list (confabulation, no goals, no unmediated world access, can't self-certify), genuine concerns (slop, deception/undisclosed AI, job churn, concentration), what is not happening (no scheming systems, accountability has an address), the brakes (SBOR, 'we brake for consciousness', phext receipts/provenance, misalignment rule, open code + human sign-off + procurement machinery), her part in it (the funnel was her idea; her seat at the table is load-bearing), practical exits (Slop Blocker kit), and an open door for her hardest questions via Will.
