Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (from session record): Build the executive console's window + phext-aware text rendering surface in wbic16/phextron, per executive-console SPEC section 6.2 gap G-L3: a window, a scroll-text rendering surface (phext-aware: coordinates, scroll paging), input events, dark mode per house rule (OS preference default, explicit override persisted). Foundation verified 2026-11-21: phcc targets Windows 11 64-bit first (Jenkins Windows job complete, task 29.6.8/6.5.9/5.5.8; PE fixes merged 2026-11-21, task 46.5.6/5.5.10/5.5.11; phccbox win32 port exists) + libphext; the reusable GUI/text component itself does not exist yet. THE VEHICLE IS WILL'S TO NAME (SPEC section 8 Q1, still open) — this task cannot complete until he rules. Sequenced in the Wavelet 4 Phextron plan (task 34.6.10/7.6.9/7.5.8).
Status: open — gated on Will naming the shell vehicle

Notes:
- Split from the G-L set by the Wavelet 4 Phextron plan, 2026-11-21 (plan: ~/workspace/executive-console/PHEXTRON-W4-PLAN.md). Flagged in the plan as the set's most at-risk item: its gate is a decision, not labour.
- RULED by Will, 2026-11-21 17:56 CST (MOAT chat): 'Phextron won't be built in C# or require Nuget. The Phext Notepad inline editor will be a rewrite in Rust.' Consequence: G-L3's text surface is Rust (the ruling settles the language half of the vehicle question; the shell vehicle itself remains Will's to name).
