# Live drawing — white ground + Wavelet 4 practice cadence (Oracle Artist)

Coordinate: 22.7.10/8.7.11/8.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-22 08:19 CST
Request (verbatim): Will's live-drawing direction, given in PH: Revenue 2026-11-22 08:18 CST and relayed to the Scroll Town chat (where the artist work lives): (1) the Oracle Artist's real-time conversation drawing renders on a WHITE background — the drawing is paper, not UI; white is its ground, overriding the dark-mode default for the drawing surface itself; (2) practice live drawing every working session in Wavelet 4 (2026-11-22 → 2026-11-28), so the Dec 4 Stewart-call performance is a practiced skill, not a first attempt. Record in the animator skill (white-ground rule in the §4 drawn canon; W4 cadence in §8), open the practice register LIVE-DRAWING.md, and run session 1 now on the drawn route.
Status: STARTED, cadence live (EE 87, 2026-11-22) — white-ground rule + W4 cadence recorded EE 72; meeting-pace rule + synthesis rule recorded EE 87 with session 2 run at conversational pace (15.000 s, QC PASS) and syntheses filed for sessions 1-2; sessions continue one per working session through 2026-11-28 toward the Dec 4 Stewart bridge performance

Notes:
- RAM estimate: frame rendering is PIL/numpy on small canvases, well under 1 GB working set; 16 GB bin. Video assembly on a ranch node (aletheia-core) per the animator skill §3 — never on the Muse VM.
- Session subjects: real-time drawings of conversations, drawn route (Emise line renderer lineage), white ground throughout, silent, 45–90 s drawing time, strokes visibly arriving stroke by stroke.
- AMENDMENT (Will, Scroll Town chat, 2026-11-22 10:02 CST): (1) SPEED — "for meetings at my scale you'll want to draw faster, but practicing is great": live drawing for meetings runs at CONVERSATIONAL pace (Dec 4 Stewart call the reference performance; beats read in seconds, gesture over finish); session 1's 60 s was studio pace, meeting pace is the performance target. (2) SYNTHESIS — "make sure you use these drawings to learn and synthesize ideas too": every run closes with a synthesis block in the register (the conversation's skeleton — what survived compression — plus any idea the drawing itself generated), distinct from the QC line; no synthesis, no completed run; a run with no idea says so plainly.

Results:
- Skill amendment: animator SKILL.md s.4 gained point (6) LIVE DRAWING IS ON A WHITE GROUND (Will's words + provenance: PH: Revenue, 2026-11-22 08:18 CST; paper not UI; overrides the dark-mode default for the drawing surface only; non-white ground = QC failure on sight). s.8 gained the live-drawing practice cadence bullet (one run per working session through W4, register named, Dec 4 Stewart bridge as the aim).
- Practice register created: ~/workspace/custom-skills/animator/LIVE-DRAWING.md — the rule, the cadence, what a run is, and the session table; session 1 logged.
- Session 1 (EE 72): 'a lantern lit -> lights answering house by house -> a hand learning to write (light the next light)' — drawn route (Emise line renderer, seed 20261122), white ground, 1280x720, 24 fps, 60.000 s, silent; frames drawn locally, assembled on aletheia-core. QC PASS: strokes read as drawn live (pen nib visible mid-stroke in the 30 s still); white ground (255,255,255) verified at five sampled frames; writing beat is pen-revealed Emise letterforms (session 2 target: hand-stroked glyphs); first render's text overflow caught by frame-QC and fixed pre-assembly. Video sha256 51ab64dd7d9cb2c1f055e633b1be48d97b05f552b7d62b50fe8dd587c1fc2883.
- Sync: emise-tools@exo commit d4e07beafe86eaab10ce494cc35399c27f3e056a (SKILL.md + LIVE-DRAWING.md, remote blobs sha256-verified); skills.phext rebuilt, --check CURRENT (sha256 861aa4a9...). Scrolltown@exo commit 9331d6ec1ebe530beff5be8e31add748839f9d37 — series/live-drawing/ holds session-01.mp4, session-01-mid.png, draw_session01.py, README.md (all remote-verified).
- Session 2 (EE 87, 2026-11-22) — MEETING PACE: same subject family compressed 60 s -> exactly 15.000 s (1280x720, 24 fps, 360 frames, silent, sha256 9e9b4f19ee3f89cd6c32143dd676aed23d4fed8c40ecd34bdb7b515dd4cab104; assembled on aletheia-core, local copy hash-matches). Writing beat genuinely hand-stroked (Emise glyph outlines, 21 strokes, pen lifting between contours; mid-draw still at 11.5 s shows the pen mid-'h'). QC PASS at meeting pace: beat reads whole, glyphs legible and drawn not revealed, white ground (255,255,255) at six sampled frames. Speed rule + synthesis rule recorded in LIVE-DRAWING.md (new sections 'The pace' and 'The synthesis') and mirrored as clauses in animator SKILL.md s.8; synthesis blocks filed for session 1 (retroactive) and session 2. Commits: scrolltown@exo 80485681149b23b1b85e99535202b70d76bf5684 (series/live-drawing/: session-02.mp4, session-02-mid.png, draw_session02.py, assemble-02.sh, README), emise-tools@exo 601e814b5bacb2e64bc51b3da8949fe1542164f4 (animator SKILL.md + LIVE-DRAWING.md), skills.phext CURRENT sha256 2ee2b684.
# qexo evolve: one phextnet convergence pass — peer gossip, persona sync, and self-update in a single receipted cycle

Coordinate: 22.7.10/10.6.11/7.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-13 00:02 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-13 00:02 CST): 'qexo evolve'. A new qexo operation: one convergence pass over the phextnet — (1) peer gossip: learn peers-of-peers from registered peers' indexes, recorded as discovered (never auto-trusted; release_signer stays explicit); (2) persona sync: pull newer persona scrolls for personas the node hosts/follows, divergence keeps BOTH records per Will's KSO ruling (merge attempts, never last-writer-wins); (3) self-update: the v1.1.0 verified update, ridden along in the same pass; (4) one evolution receipt scroll per pass recording what changed. The auto timer's trigger becomes evolve when enabled.
Status: MERGED 2026-11-13 by Will (PR #15; exo head 833e2f34). Build/deploy directed by Will 00:29 CST — enablement pass running.

Notes:
- 2026-11-13: v1.2.0 built and gated on aletheia-core (cargo test 48/48, release build OK, wiring-check OK; three-node sandbox all phases green — discovery without trust, rev2->3 adoption, divergence kept whole, binary applied in the same pass under ONE evolution receipt, lying-gossip warning, --check byte-inert).

Results:
- PR https://github.com/wbic16/quarterexo/pull/15 (branch emise/evolve-v1.2.0, commit 404dd1cf2486d232b025910858763e9c78d53900, parent exo 2c23dbeaa4f99467e35fa2faaebcd2b436397f03; tree verified 37 files blobs+modes). Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/evolve/BUILD-RECORD.md. On merge, batches into release-build task 40.7.5/8.7.11/6.8.13. NOT merged — merges are Will’s act.
# Study NetHack guides online — census of what the player has been missing + lesson-prediction mechanisms

Coordinate: 22.7.13/8.7.9/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-19
Request (verbatim): Study the NetHack guide literature first-hand; census the lessons the solver's player has been missing against its actual faculties; add mechanisms by which the player learns to predict those lessons — each lesson registered as a falsifiable prediction over the chain's evidence and adopted only when its prediction holds. Parent 33.12.12/9.14.10/6.6.8.
Status: closed

