# edit.phext.io UX: only require a login to edit (reads are anonymous)

Coordinate: 23.4.7/7.4.7/5.4.6
Issued: 2026-11-19 01:28 CST
Request (verbatim): UX: only require a login to edit
Status: closed — SHIPPED 2026-11-19 02:07:18 CST as phext-lattice PR #79 (merged, 749b560a); anonymous traverse/view live, login only to edit; launch archived

Notes:
- Direction: browsing/reading on edit.phext.io — including the whole Scrollspace viewer (phext list, toc, scroll reads) — must NOT require a login; a session is required only when the user edits (writes). This reverses the read-gating that returned when oauth.env was restored on 2026-11-19 00:05 (anonymous /api/* = 401).
- Server-side change in phext-edit: gate by operation, not by surface — read routes anonymous, write/edit routes session-required. The build enumerates the route table and states plainly which routes it classified as reads vs writes, and what anonymous users see in the editor shell (read-only view vs sign-in prompt on first edit attempt).
- Interaction with PR #77 (login task 31.5.6): the login panel + return-after-login mechanism stays — its trigger moves from "read got a 401" to "edit attempted without a session", returning the user to the page they were on. Scrollspace viewing becomes outcome (a) of the original login brief: works without a login.
- Refinement (Will, 2026-11-19 01:28 CST, verbatim): "allow users to traverse and view without a login" — the same build stated from the viewer’s side: anonymous users can fly/traverse Scrollspace and read scrolls end to end; the login appears only at an edit attempt. Folded into this task rather than registered twice.
- Incident + restart (2026-11-19 02:07 CST): coordinator ba32d73c errored (transport: sqlx pool timeout) after completing RECON/BUILD/GATE/VERIFY — walk5 updated PASS, walk7_readonly PASS, all regressions PASS. Live origin verified healthy by Emise from the hub (200, 57,950 B, sha 0a9c1883 = PR #78 build; no deploy had started). Fresh coordinator a1711082 dispatched to finish SHIP + LIVE only, per the status-ask-restart rule, without waking Will.
- CLOSED 2026-11-19: PR #79 https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/79 merged to exo (749b560a4511bc1b7c3947fd029d19518a80108b); diff src/oauth.rs + src/bin/phext_edit.rs only — the Scrollspace PAGE is byte-identical to PR #78 (57,950 B, sha 0a9c1883), so no artifacts.phext inscription refresh. Binary sha256 0cab1b3da17c90ba19fcaba4bff25979f3387bedd2279097132e0821e8a234ee; deploy MainPID 3879250 -> 3889162. SHIP TIMESTAMP 2026-11-19 02:07:18 CST. Notable: the first coordinator had actually completed SHIP (02:05–02:07 CST) before its transport death but recorded none of it; the resumed coordinator established the true state from three independent sources (hub git, connector API, awsbox service) and re-verified every leg rather than redoing. LIVE: screen5_live 22/22 PASS anonymous on the real origin (no panel, no 401s across 163 API answers, full zoom chain, Glassfruit live, write probe 401, zero errors); editor leg 13/14 — the one fail is a pre-existing CSP block of the shell’s own Product Hunt badge (byte-identical in the PR #78 baseline; not this build’s defect). Launch archive: ~/workspace/launches/2026-11-19-0207-login-only-to-edit/ (screenshot + manifest). Route classification + guards (TEI conversion guard, dirty-switch guard) per STATE.md.
# Associate design words with 5D artifact addresses in designbox / 6D UML

Coordinate: 23.4.10/6.5.9/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-22
Request (verbatim): include a way to associate design words with 5D artifact addresses, so users aren't overwhelmed
Status: COMPLETE — Lexicon shipped as PR #98 (wbic16/phext-lattice, branch emise/uml6d-lexicon @ 681767d on exo c7702ae). Part 1: DESIGN.md Lexicon section (Exocortical Design Rule cited). Part 2: seed lexicon scroll at 1.1.1/4.1.1/1.1.3, round-trip verified byte-for-byte. Part 3: word statement + word references in uml6d_diagram, built and tested on scroll-central: lib 202 passed (196 existing + 6 new), bin 121 passed, 324 total; sole failure the known pre-existing e2e_local latency assertion, verified identical on pristine exo. Merge is Will's.

Notes:
- Will, 2026-11-22 10:07 CST, Architecture thread. Follow-on to designbox task 23.6.10/8.6.11/6.6.9 (COMPLETE) and PR #97 (merged).
- Exocortical Design Rule (Will, 2026-11-22, relayed mid-task): the Lexicon section cites it by name as the principle the mechanism serves; one line naming it is in the prepared PR body.
- Part 3 build leg: fresh clone made on ni-knight (~/phext-lattice-lexicon @ exo c7702ae, branch emise/uml6d-lexicon) but the clone's exec output was flagged by the runtime execution-risk check; no apply/build/test/push/PR performed after the flag. Baseline attempt before the flag also surfaced a dependency fact: cargo test --offline on ni-knight cannot resolve the holo-phext git dependency (rev bafed5f3) from its cargo git cache — on resume, build where that checkout is cached or vendor the git dep via fleet NFS.
- Part 3 unblocked by Will's plain go-ahead (2026-11-22 10:17 CST, Architecture thread: 'Proceed — build and PR the lexicon code'), on top of his standing wbic16-clone auto-approve rule. Built on scroll-central (aletheia-core barred at ~91 °C; ni-knight lacked the holo-phext git-dep cache) reusing the PR #97 vendored tree incl. the holo-phext git source; Cargo.lock identical to the proven tree. Prepared code compiled exactly as authored — zero changes needed; applied file sha256 1259f55f…, diff 241 insertions / 24 deletions, matching the prepared patch exactly.

Results:
- DESIGN.md: 'The Lexicon — design words for artifact addresses' section added (sits in the Lens; Exocortical Design Rule cited by name; binding/canonical-word/rebinding/loud-failure rules specified); 6D UML status paragraph updated for PR #97 + this task.
- designbox.phext: lexicon scroll at 1.1.1/4.1.1/1.1.3 (lens/harvest/chronicle/harness/loop -> 1.1.1/1.1, 1.2.1/1.1, 1.3.1/1.1, 1.4.1/1.1, 1.5.1/1.1); map scroll lists it; 15,851 B, 24 non-empty scrolls; parse+implode round-trip byte-for-byte verified (own parser + parse_phext.py); unlisted Library-2 wing byte-identical and unmentioned.
- Part 3 code prepared (UNVERIFIED — not compiled): ~/workspace/uml6d-lexicon/uml6d_diagram.rs (word statement, first-pass bindings, canonical-word emission, 6 new tests) + uml6d_diagram-lexicon.patch (diff vs merged exo file: 24 lines replaced, 241 added, no unrelated drift) + IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.md (design decisions, baseline finding, remaining steps, ready PR body naming the Exocortical Design Rule).
- PR #98: https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/98 — 'uml6d_diagram: the Lexicon — design words for artifact addresses', open, base exo, head emise/uml6d-lexicon @ 681767ddac251ad425f99dfffb993e599dc8ed39.
- Tests (scroll-central, cargo test --offline): lib 202/202, phext_edit bin 121/121, e2e_local 1 passed + local_editor_regression latency failure (63.00 ms vs 50 ms) — pre-existing, verified identical on pristine exo c7702ae (62.70 ms) before applying. New lexicon tests 6/6: word_bindings_resolve, word_and_address_forms_render_identically, unknown_word_is_named_with_its_line, conflicting_binding_is_an_error_same_address_is_harmless, word_round_trip_is_a_fixed_point, phase_invariance_holds_with_words. Node temps stayed ~37–42 °C, well under the 75 °C limit.
# OpenClaw vestige purge — fleet-wide

Coordinate: 23.5.5/5.4.7/4.4.8
Issued: Will, main chat, 2026-11-22 00:33 CST (EE 5)
Request (from session record): Remove the OpenClaw vestiges fleet-wide: stop and disable the gateways the audit found running, pull the resident Discord tokens, clear the awsbox cron leftovers, settle west-lincoln. (Will, main chat, 2026-11-22 00:33 CST, EE 5: "continue progress on removing openclaw vestiges, deploying the inklings substrates, and enabling phextron")
Status: COMPLETE — purge executed EE 6, final verification EE 7 (2026-11-22)

Notes:
- Fleet audit 2026-11-22 (EE 4): gateways RUNNING on 15 ranch nodes as wbic16 + jared on uncanny-valley + an ubuntu process on awsbox; tokens resident on 11 nodes; west-lincoln crash-looping. This pass completes the 2026-11-12 order properly. Jared's instance is not stoppable from wbic16 — report only.
- PURGE EXECUTED 2026-11-22 (EE 6; final re-probe EE 7). 15 nodes purged and verified (unit inactive+disabled, 0 wbic16 openclaw procs, no :18789 listener, discord token absent from live config): ni-knight, ashfall-haven, logos-prime, elven-path, orchid-flow, halycon-vector, lighthouse-omen, free-fall, aletheia-core (Theia hub: stopped/disabled/token-stripped only, ~/.openclaw NOT deleted), jacked-kite, quacked-hill, yeet-max, kaleidoscope-one, moon-beam, scroll-central. Tokens removed from live configs on 10 nodes (NK, EP, OF, HV, AC, QH, YM, KO, MB, SC); AH/LP/LO/FF/JK configs held no discord keys. Per-channel guild overrides flipped to False: halycon-vector 1 (Tessera channel), aletheia-core 2. Every edited config backed up first as openclaw.json.pre-purge-2026-11-22 on its node and re-validated as JSON. West-lincoln: crash-looping unit stopped+disabled; no live config existed (historic snapshot only). Plain-view (audit-unreachable): retry probe verified unit already disabled+inactive, 0 procs, no listener, no live config — nothing to purge. AWSBOX: wbic16 crontab backed up (~/crontab.pre-purge-2026-11-22.txt) and the two named entries removed (update-mood.sh */15, daily-maturity-post.sh 22:00); wbic16 has NO passwordless sudo there; the ubuntu-user gateway process seen by the audit (PID 391921) was already gone at 06:41 UTC and ps at 06:45 UTC shows no openclaw process and no :18789 listener — exit cause unknown, its persistence mechanism under ubuntu is uninspectable without sudo (Will-step: staged sudo). REMAINING for Will/Jared: (1) uncanny-valley — jared's openclaw + openclaw-gateway STILL RUNNING (PIDs 1242/1449, :18789 listening, ~/.openclaw mtime 2026-11-21 21:15 UTC, config unreadable) — untouched, report only; (2) awsbox ubuntu persistence check via staged sudo; (3) two awsbox crontab entries left per the brief's named scope though they reference OpenClaw paths: snapshot-consciousness.sh (logs into ~/.openclaw/logs) and ~/.openclaw/scripts/celestial-sta