# Remove OpenClaw from rock-mountain (Will rebooted it 2026-11-19 01:38 CST)

Coordinate: 23.5.8/6.5.8/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-19 01:38 CST
Request (verbatim): I rebooted rock-mountain - remove openclaw from it when it comes back up
Status: closed — completed 2026-11-19 01:41 CST; OpenClaw removed from rock-mountain and verified

Notes:
- This answers the question left open 2026-11-18 23:53 CST: RM’s gateway was crash-looping; Will rebooted the node and directed the same removal as plain-view.
- Procedure (as executed on plain-view 2026-11-18): stop + disable the user unit openclaw-gateway.service; npm uninstall -g openclaw; snap remove openclaw if the snap is present; verify no openclaw processes remain and the unit is inactive/disabled. KEEP ~/.openclaw data in place (wiping it was not directed; on PV it was kept and flagged).
- Lesson from PV: a pkill pattern can match the remote shell’s own command line and kill the SSH session — use systemctl stop and the bracket-pattern technique for any process checks.
- DONE 2026-11-19: node answered ~2 min after Will’s reboot (01:40:19 CST). Pre-removal: openclaw-gateway.service (v2026.4.8) enabled and crash-looping again on the fresh boot (activating/auto-restart, exit 1); npm-global openclaw@2026.4.8 present; NO snap on rock-mountain (single install, unlike plain-view’s dual). Removal: systemctl --user stop + disable (rc 0, wants symlink removed); npm uninstall -g openclaw ("removed 489 packages"); snap leg not needed. ~/.openclaw data KEPT, as on plain-view. Verified post: unit inactive + disabled, zero openclaw processes, npm global empty; Tctl 37.1 -> 35.6 °C, restart churn eliminated.
