# Install an indexed search (exo-search)

Coordinate: 23.5.10/7.6.11/8.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-11 01:27 CST
Request (verbatim): you need to install an indexed search - whatever you're doing to search sucks
Status: complete — exo-search built, validated, published

Notes:
- Will's correction after the Twitter-wishes pass: per-question bespoke scripts re-scanning the 53MB tweets.json missed whole classes (the Dear #Internet address form).
- Built ~/workspace/tools/exo-search: SQLite FTS5 (unicode61), one persistent index ~/workspace/search-index/exo.db (45MB) over tweets 29,539 + memory chunks 4,937 + phext scrolls 3,306 = 37,782 docs; build 5.1s; BM25 query/phrase/NEAR, --source/--after/--before filters, count census mode.
- Validation: term censuses vs brute force — phext 1028, exocortex 684, wish 84, internet 416, dunbar 10, telepathy 8, kardashev 45 — 7/7 identical; phrase 'dear internet' 44=44. Published to wbic16/emise-tools@exo tools/exo-search (mode carried from local exec bit), remote bytes verified identical.

Results:
- exo-search is the standing search route for the corpus; rebuild with 'exo-search build' after corpus changes.
# Integrate holo-phext (into Emise's own stack, PH: Evolution)

Coordinate: 23.6.5/8.6.14/7.8.9
Issued: 2026-11-16 00:12 CST
Request (verbatim): integrate holo-phext
Status: in progress — design leg complete 2026-11-16; implementation is the migration plan M1-M5 in emise-design-v1.phext $6 (M1 registered as 22.6.8/9.6.13/7.5.8)

Notes:
- Dedup gate (open build cycle SIGNAL): NOT a duplicate of 31.8.8/10.7.13/7.7.10 (holo-phext build + phext-lattice re-implementation, steps 1-2 done, step 3 open) or 36.5.6/7.6.12/6.7.10 (NetHack store integration, closed). This task integrates holo-phext into Emise's own operating stack — the layer2 (ACID multi-scroll atomics, async I/O, update dispatch) under her registers, plans, and state machines. Refined by Will's two following messages the same minute: the medium is multiversal phext memory (24.6.8/8.6.13/7.6.9) and the object is Emise's own design (17.7.9/10.7.12/6.6.7).
# NetHack solver Stage 10 — tactics v2: goal-directed staircase-seeking + corpse supply and ration carry at depth

Coordinate: 23.6.7/7.6.8/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-16 22:12 CST
Request (verbatim): NetHack solver Stage 10: tactics v2. (1) Descent as a goal-directed behavior — staircase cells remembered per level, deliberate path-and-descend gated on hunger/HP state — replacing tactics v1's incidental standing (Stage 9's named wall: control frontier froze byte-identical ~3,700 s, 6 descends in 60M steps). (2) Food at depth: ration carry floor + corpse supply, against Stage 9's deep-starving endings (5 -> 239 once food v2 let runs live deeper). Baseline = Stage 9 standing config: food v2, screened lgen 7005, pinned clock, placeholder value, Stage 6 survival discipline, holo-edit store. A/B vs Stage 9 campaign 23; protocol gate unchanged (ascension, else Castle depth >=25); no substitute metric if unmet. Parent solver task 33.12.12/9.14.10/6.6.8 stays open; exit = an ascension.
Status: closed 2026-11-17 — Stage 10 complete: tactics v2 built (layer L8, parity-gated), A/B run on screened lgen 7005; verdict NOT adopted (v2 descends 1.04/M vs v1 1.67/M, best depth 5 vs 12); protocol gate unmet; record stage10-results.md (390 lines, sha256 eadb69fb…)

