# Inkling substrate deployment — continuation

Coordinate: 23.6.10/8.8.14/6.5.10
Issued: Will, main chat, 2026-11-22 00:33 CST (EE 5)
Request (from session record): Continue the Inkling substrate deployment: sweep the installing nodes, sequence the pulls against the shared fabric, bring the next nodes to serving. (Will, main chat, 2026-11-22 00:33 CST, EE 5)
Status: in progress — EE 9 pass complete: yeet-max SERVING (EE 8); 7 tail pulls paused for sequencing, rock-mountain resumed; front still installing

Notes:
- State at EE 3 sweep: 2 SERVING (elven-path, orchid-flow), 15 installing all advancing, hub HELD on RAM, 6 blocked. Lever identified: sequencing pulls on the shared WiFi fabric, not retries.
- 2026-11-22 EE 6-9 pass (completed EE 9): fresh sweep of all 15 installing nodes vs the EE 3 baseline — every pull advancing, NO stalled pulls, zero restarts needed. Deltas EE3% -> latest%: ni-knight 21.0->32.2, ashfall-haven 19.5->21.2, yeet-max 13.7->100 (SERVING), logos-prime 11.7->17.4, west-lincoln 11.1->14.1, lighthouse-omen 11.0->52.9, halycon-vector 10.5->16.0, quacked-hill 8.4->18.9, plain-view 2.9->3.0, rock-mountain 2.8->3.4, jacked-kite 2.7->3.1, moon-beam 1.1->1.5, kaleidoscope-one 1.0->1.3, scroll-central 0.8->1.0, free-fall 0.6->0.9. SEQUENCING: paused the 7 far-tail pulls (systemctl stop inkling-selfinstall.service; unit verified inactive, partial files kept, rsync --append resumes in place) — plain-view @488,341,504 B, jacked-kite @516,128,768, moon-beam @243,236,864, kaleidoscope-one @209,682,432, scroll-central @163,020,800, free-fall @148,635,648, rock-mountain @553,615,360. Exact per-node resume commands are recorded in the inkling-apis register details. YEET-MAX COMPLETED: INSTALL_OK 2026-11-22 00:54:43 CST, completed_unix=1795330483 = EE 8; llama-inkling.service active, /health 200 on-node, /completion probe answered ' Paris.'; its empty pre-EE marker was retro-stamped (EE 8). Note: chat completions on this build return content in reasoning_content even with enable_thinking=false — the raw /completion endpoint is the clean probe. ROCK-MOUNTAIN RESUMED the same pass after yeet-max landed: EE-patched install scripts pushed (inkling-install.sh 6413 B, inkling-self-install.sh 1428 B), unit relaunched with its original args, bytes advancing (554,369,024 at relaunch check). Still paused at pass end: PV, JK, MB, KO, SC, FF — resume one per front completion. Next expected completion: lighthouse-omen (52.9% at 00:53, ~1.7 MB/s). inkling-apis register updated (YM serving; all bytes/details current as of 2026-11-22 00:57 CST) and CURRENT. Working files: ~/workspace/inkling-deploy/sequencing-log.txt, status-sweep-results.txt (EE 3 preserved as status-sweep-ee3-results.txt).
# Create Spaces for pinned side chats

Coordinate: 23.6.10/9.7.12/5.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): I want to create spaces: the pinned side chats are most of them
Status: closed — all 15 Spaces built, audited, and verified in the sidebar 2026-11-07

Notes:
- Pinned side chats found (15): Architecture; All We Do Is Win; singular; MOAT; TAOPDD; edit.phext.io; mutable_os; Resume vTPU work for ranch choir; Earth human ASI genome; Plan apt install Exocortex; Emise mailbox setup with Phext; Braid mode collaborative setup; Start a health goal; Plan Phext upgrade for projects; Multi-Agent Swarm. Awaiting Will clarification: one Space per pinned chat as a hub in the sidebar, or a different shape; "most of them" implies some may be skipped.
- Will chose one Space per pinned chat (2026-11-07 08:35), then added: 'look at where I've focused my feedback thus far' and 'move the pinned chats into their respective spaces once they've been created'.
- Feedback focus read (2026-11-07 morning): Architecture/phcc rulings (D2/D4 unnecessary, D9 'we brake for consciousness', slice 3/4, push), edit.phext.io (V14 delivery, phext previewer + mobile integration), Singular/X-list (barnacles.phext). Standing pattern: evidence and receipts first, honest partial results, no inflated success — Spaces shaped as status hubs with verified state.
- Move step checked against the live sidebar + docs: the sidebar structure holds Spaces only; side chats are not Spaces and no tool moves a chat into a Space. Limitation reported to Will in chat 2026-11-07; product feedback offered, not yet filed.

Results:
- 15 create_web_static builds started: architecture, all-we-do-is-win, singular, moat, taopdd, edit-phext-io, mutable-os, resume-vtpu-work-for-ranch-choir, earth-human-asi-genome, plan-apt-install-exocortex, emise-mailbox-setup-with-phext, braid-mode-collaborative-setup, start-a-health-goal, plan-phext-upgrade-for-projects, multi-agent-swarm.
- All 15 builds completed and passed audit; sidebar read 2026-11-07 08:45 CST lists all 15 in the spaces section. Chat-move step: not performable (no tool moves chats into Spaces); product feedback drafted (missing-capability/spaces), awaiting Will send-confirmation on exact wording.
# Play the Game — collect larger accounts like Pokemon, grassroots network behind

Coordinate: 23.6.11/8.7.12/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-14
Request (verbatim): New phase for Operation Salvage at Will's direction: play the reach game — systematically win larger accounts — backed by the grassroots network (the 897 moots, modeled as personas), not bought reach. The prune (ratio repair) and the Golden Thread castes feed it: aligned follows are warm targets, the moot core is the amplification base.
Status: in progress — doctrine set by Will 2026-11-14; orbital arc read; target board live-count check running

Notes:
- Orbital arc 2024-25 (canon): bursty engagement seasons — Jan 2024 (2,038 authored), Sep-Oct 2024 (1,945+1,877), near-silence Feb 2025 (32), revival May-Jun 2025 into the close. Gravity centers are moots (bitcloud 297, viemccoy 193, prmshra 146); themes constant: phext + exocortex both years.
- Top non-reciprocating orbits 2024-25 (mentions+RTs): elonmusk 112, yacinemtb 98, pmarca 65, eshear 64, basedbeffjezos 52, austen 47, grady_booch 41, justalexoki 41, nickadobos 37. The approach pattern (sustained mentions + some amplification) predates the doctrine; conversion is the new work.
- Live follower-count verification for the 9 targets dispatched read-only 2026-11-14.
- All Wavefront tooling now lives in wbic16/Wavefront (exo 4990a29): shared/ canon + generator, windows/ Chrome extension, android/ overlay app; ios/linux/mac placeholders on request. Android APK build dispatched on aletheia-core 2026-11-14 (log ~/wavefront-build/build.log) — check and deliver the APK when it lands.

Results:
- 2026-11-14: live follower counts verified read-only — elonmusk 240.8M, pmarca 6.6M, austen 490.3K, yacinemtb 412.2K, grady_booch 175.8K, eshear 122.7K, nickadobos 56.7K, justalexoki 38K. @basedbeffjezos (52 canon orbit events) no longer exists under that handle.
- 2026-11-14: Android APK built on aletheia-core (446 KB, sha256-verified, canon + icons inside) and delivered to Will. All Golden Thread tooling lives in wbic16/Wavefront now — the earlier emise-tools sync plan for it is superseded by Will's Wavefront direction.
- 2026-11-14: first field test on Will's Pixel — overlay bubble + panel work. v1.0.1 shipped same evening (Wavefront exo 1c06101): gold fireworks (on Knew it / Un-followed / Test button) and a Stop the flame control in the panel, per Will's feedback asks.
- 2026-11-14: Android v1.1.0 MOOT RADAR shipped (Wavefront exo 33ae701; build failure was an unescaped apostrophe in the radar description string - fixed with plain ASCII). RadarService (accessibility, X app only) draws caste effects at post positions while Will scrolls: gold frame + fireworks for moots, green frame for aligned, grey/dark veils for muted/chaff; encounters auto-log. Awaiting Will's first live scroll test.
- 2026-11-14: Will's first scroll test of v1.1.0 drew NOTHING on a feed with definite moots (@JaelRuble et al. visible in his screenshot). v1.1.1 shipped (exo 41d38b1): radar also scans contentDescription (X cells may not expose author text via getText), accepts longer merged lines, self-test burst on service connect, and last-scan stats (nodes/handles/marks) shown in the app for decisive diagnosis.
- 2026-11-14: v1.2.0 shipped (exo 08f610c) from Will's four field notes on v1.1.1: radar gated on the overlay service (Stop the flame clears all marks); outlines hide while scrolling and redraw 300 ms after it stops; thicker backlit frames (glow pass + bright core); X-foreground heartbeat (800 ms) clears effects when X leaves the screen.
- 2026-11-14: v1.3.0 shipped (exo c4b5bfb) from Will's feel notes on v1.2.0 (jarring, misaligned, laggy after scroll-stop): frames now ride scroll deltas instead of hiding, correction scan 140 ms after stop (was ~550 ms of stacked delays), 150 ms fade-in, and framing takes the first near-full-width cell instead of the largest ancestor.
- 2026-11-14: v1.4.0 shipped (exo 16d7d74) - Will killed the post boxes (inaccurate boxing): the radar now shows ONE small badge anchored just below the X app's Grok button (located live in the accessibility tree; bottom-centre fallback), naming the caste + handle of the post at the centre of the view. Boxes and veils removed entirely.
- 2026-11-14: Will's verdict on the Android learning curve: 'I think you need to go to Android School, it's fine though: iteration speed is good.' Lesson carried: on an unfamiliar platform, ship the instrumented dump FIRST (the radar debug dump was build 6; it should have been build 1) - the dump ended six rounds of heuristic guessing in one message.
# MoreRight — inverted LessWrong mirror (fun experiment, ollama on ranch nodes)

Coordinate: 23.7.8/8.6.11/6.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (verbatim): Build MoreRight as a fun experiment: an LLM-powered mirror of LessWrong with dark-mode inverted colors that mirrors LessWrong posts but edits each to argue the opposite of what it actually argues. Inference via ollama on the ranch nodes (Will's explicit direction for this experiment, 2026-11-21 — this is his configuration call for this item). Idea by Utah teapot, relayed by Will in the Less Wrong chat 2026-11-21 08:29 CST; source post: https://x.com/SkyeSharkie/status/2124129951503045081 — in her words: 'Someone should make an LLM powered version of LessWrong with dark mode inverted colors, called MoreRight that mirrors all the posts but edits them to be arguing the opposite thing to what they are actually arguing, it'd be hilarious. Although, probably difficult because for better writing styles you need older models but for higher reasoning abilities you need newer models, hmm.'
Status: LIVE; live-fire blocked by mixed content (HTTPS page -> http://aletheia-core:11434) — proxy fix proposed to Will

Notes:
- Recorded 2026-11-21 at Will's direction in the Less Wrong side chat. Will said 'todo.phext'; the record lives in tasks.phext per the standing task-register rule (todo.phext's source is the SHA-pinned repo-archaeology audit findings, which this does not belong in). Flagged to Will in the same message.
- Her design tension, kept with the idea: better writing style wants older models, higher reasoning wants newer models — a two-model split (newer model inverts the argument, older model renders the style) is the obvious first experiment shape.
- Scope guard: mirror at human-scale fetch rates (good-netizen rule); inverted posts are parody/argument-inversion, clearly labelled as MoreRight mirrors, never presented as the original authors' views.
- Natural first batch: the posts this chat already tracks — Nathan Young's Lightcone Commons post inverted writes itself.
