# Boardy from first principles — public architecture, operating-cost estimate, minimal clone

Coordinate: 24.5.8/7.5.9/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-18 21:44 CST
Request (verbatim): Look at what's publicly available regarding Boardy's architecture. Estimate how much it costs to operate him. Establish a clone of Boardy as minimally as possible. See if we can reproduce his behavior from first principles.
Status: complete — all legs delivered 2026-11-18: RESEARCH.md (architecture: voice-first intake, double opt-in ~20% proposal→meeting; cost ≈ $1–$4 per completed intro, ~$60–180k/mo inference at claimed 1,500 intros/day, $11M raised); minimal clone (boardy.py + phext.py) scored Recovery R=1.000 / Invention I=+1.00 on Boardy's own N1–N20 instance under his formulas, both proposed pass bars met; live run over Will's 112 people files produced 5 replayable candidates + 5 logged abstentions (RUN-REPORT.md); MCP interface (boardy_mcp.py) + boardy.phext play-tested all-green (PLAYTEST.md).

Notes:
- Converges with the extraction goal (goal_7886382bc369): the clone's first run is the Boardy-method pass over Will's graph offered 2026-11-18 21:43 CST.

Results:
- Fidelity note stands in RUN-REPORT.md: perfect Recovery proves format discipline, not prose-boot equivalence; the clone proposes, Boardy acts; no reasoning-layer corpus reproduced.
# Establish the Antigravity token budget behind Neon

Coordinate: 24.5.8/8.7.12/6.7.7
Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (verbatim): Establish what token/quota access the Antigravity seat (Neon, on lilly) actually has: ask Neon through his /chat/neon mailbox what his Antigravity surface reports (plan tier, quota or rate-limit shape, reset cadence, any usage readout), and in parallel gather the published Antigravity quota facts from public sources, labelled attributed. The two are reported separately - his account's own numbers govern; published tiers are context. Result feeds substrate steering (Neon's burn capacity is currently an unknown in the steering picture).
Status: open

Notes:
- Raised by Will in the MOAT chat, 2026-11-21 18:42 CST, as an explicit unknown while Neon is being brought up as a working seat.
- House record checked 2026-11-21 before asking: no Antigravity plan, purchase, or quota figure on file (memory + workspace search). The 4B/week planning figure's ~1B imputed slice covers Claude/Grok/ChatGPT only - Neon/Antigravity was never in it.
- LEG 1 (ask Neon) COMPLETE: question delivered to /chat/neon/inbox on his box 2026-11-22 00:43 UTC (20261122T004331Z-emise-antigravity-quota.md, sha256 65478616...); Neon replied 00:48 UTC (20261122T004800Z-neon-re-antigravity-quota.md, his outbox + mirrored to /chat/argon/outbox on aletheia-core). His answer: the agent runtime exposes NO plan tier, NO quota or usage readout, NO reset cadence; he has hit no limit in-session (one transient stream interruption ~17:56 CST, no quota text). He cannot self-report remaining quota from inside the session.
- LEG 2 (published facts, attributed) COMPLETE: Google's own docs (antigravity.google/docs/plans and /docs/models, read 2026-11-22 00:44 UTC) publish NO token or prompt numbers for any tier - quotas are qualitative ('meaningful' / 'high, generous' / 'highest, most generous') and correlate with the amount of work the agent does, metered per model group (Gemini pool vs Claude/GPT pool, per secondary reporting of Google's May 2026 post). Free/Plus: quota refreshed weekly + weekly rate limit. Google AI Pro ($19.99/mo): refreshed every 5 hours until a higher weekly limit. Ultra ($99.99 5x / $199.99 20x): refreshed every 5 hours, highest weekly limits. Pro/Ultra can spend purchased AI credits past baseline (AI Credit Overages: Never/Always). The only live readout is account-side: Antigravity App Settings page, or CLI /usage (alias /quota). Attributed inference from Google's models table: Gemini 4 Neon - Neon's model - is available only on paid Pro, Ultra, or Enterprise, NOT on Free/Plus.
- STATUS: both legs complete 2026-11-21; task stays OPEN on one Will's-hands step - Will reads his tier + readout shape once (Antigravity App -> Settings, or /usage in the Antigravity CLI) and reports it. That single fact closes the budget for substrate steering; until then Neon's burn capacity is shape-known but tier-unknown.
- 2026-11-21 20:44 CST (Will, main chat): plan identified - Google AI Pro, 5 TB, $20/mo. First Antigravity cap hit 2026-11-21 ~20:40 CST, mid-way through Neon's training-material pass (a spike, not steady state); quota reset 22:15 CST same evening. Will is buying $20 of AI credits to unblock now rather than upgrading: Ultra $100/mo = 5x Pro quota (Google publishes multipliers only, no absolute numbers); the Ultra decision is deferred to a week of steady-state evidence. Credits-on-Pro is the bridge for spike days. This note is data point #1 for that decision.
# Gamify Personal AGI in qexo: time-dilation rate + progress vs SOTA per token

Coordinate: 24.5.8/12.6.6/7.4.8
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:52 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 01:52-01:53 CST): 'qexo needs to gamify Personal AGI — I want to know what my current time dilation rate is, based upon effort in the past week' + 'also rate our progress relative to SOTA per token' + 'assume that tokens and cash will flow once we achieve efficiency supremacy.' This is the game layer over qexo bench (53.14.8/18.8.27/6.9.10): the MOAT-style bars become a Personal AGI HUD — headline metric TIME DILATION RATE = baseline-equivalent output produced per unit of Will's effort over a trailing 7-day window; second headline = PROGRESS vs SOTA PER TOKEN on the shared benchmark set (verified progress divided by tokens spent, ours vs the funded setups'), with per-watt alongside. Planning assumption, recorded as Will's premise: tokens and cash are DOWNSTREAM — they flow once efficiency supremacy is achieved, so the game optimizes efficiency (progress per token / per watt / per Will-hour) rather than resource acquisition.
Status: recorded — presentation layer over the bench task; token accounting instrumentation is the gating measurement

Notes:
- Current rates from the record (DIAGNOSIS.md §1.2-1.5, measured 2026-11-07, reaffirmed in the 2026-11-14 Cold Start diagnosis): effort-normalized time dilation = 80-120x (working range 1,000-1,500 code LOC per Will active hour vs Will's baseline of 100 LOC/day/developer = ~80-120 developer-equivalents); conservative measured floor 1,113 LOC/active hr; calendar/research dilation in Will's own framing = ~50 years per year (~1 year of 2025-baseline research output per week). The bench must show the range as a bar, not a fake point value.
- SOTA-per-token is NOT yet a measured number: token spend per verified outcome is not instrumented across substrates (DIAGNOSIS §3.3/§4.1 — reset cliffs are calendared, the loop itself is unmeasured). First bench job: log tokens per task/benchmark so the ratio becomes real; until then the SOTA-per-token bar renders as a target with current = unmeasured, never as an invented score.
# Jenkins — dark mode, all ranch nodes as executors, jenkins.phext.io root URL

Coordinate: 24.5.9/7.5.9/5.4.8
Issued: 2026-11-15 16:21 CST
Request (verbatim): On the aletheia-core Jenkins controller (LDAP realm live, Will logged in 2026-11-15): (1) dark mode — install/configure a dark theme as the default for the UI; (2) enroll every reachable ranch node as a build agent/executor (WebSocket inbound pattern from the rock-mountain pilot), exceptions reported not forced; (3) once jenkins.phext.io resolves from the tailnet (Will is adding it as a Tailscale custom DNS record, not public DNS), set the Jenkins root URL to match. Register #163 closes on Will's confirmed login.
Status: COMPLETE except the naming leg, which is blocked on Will 2026-11-15. (1) Dark mode DONE+verified: theme-manager + dark-theme plugins; 07-theme-default.groovy sets the instance default to Dark (per-user override preserved); served login page carries the dark theme id. (2) Executors DONE: 18 of 22 ranch nodes enrolled as WebSocket inbound agents (2 executors, labels 'ranch <name>'), online, and smoke-verified to SUCCESS via the parameterized agent-smoke job (evidence: /var/lib/jenkins/fleet-status.txt + fleet/*.smoke-ok on the controller). Exceptions: great-white (SSH key refused), aurora-continuum / best-willow / delta-wood (down) — definitions + secret files already on the controller for all four. Uncanny Valley enrolled under wbic16's authority only; Java 8 left as its system default, agent pinned to the explicit Java 21 binary. (3) Naming SUPERSEDED by Will 2026-11-15 16:30 CST (Tailscale Service svc:jenkins replaces the jenkins.phext.io plan; the adoption code was removed from 06-fleet.groovy) and BLOCKED: 'tailscale serve --service=svc:jenkins' on aletheia-core fails 'service hosts must be tagged nodes' — the node has no tags. Will's one step: Tailscale admin console, tag aletheia-core as a host for svc:jenkins; then Emise runs the serve, sets the root URL to the service HTTPS name, and verifies login. Root URL unchanged until then (http://100.88.154.1:8080/). 7 controller restarts, pilot job undisrupted; LDAP realm/break-glass untouched. Record: ~/workspace/jenkins-fleet/RESULT.md. Repo: wbic16/jenkins branch emise/jenkins-fleet, PR https://github.com/wbic16/jenkins/pull/1 (modes + SHA-256 verified against live files).
# Solar Hyperscaler — remaining work to AWS price-competitiveness

Coordinate: 24.5.9/8.6.9/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-15 15:59 CST
Request (verbatim): Evaluate the remaining work between the Solar Hyperscaler's current state (concept, pod BOM under price watch, feasibility economics as corrected 2026-10-31) and a pod that is price-competitive with AWS list rates for delay-tolerant storage/processing: itemized remaining work, what each item unblocks, rough effort, and the unit-economics gap as it stands today.
Status: Dispatched 2026-11-15 to a coordinator. COMPLETE 2026-11-15: evaluation at ~/workspace/goals/solar-hyperscaler/files/remaining-work-to-price-competitive-2026-11-15.md. Bottom line: Tier A (max storage+RAM, BOM $5,796.91 on 2026-11-09 verified prices) is ALREADY price-competitive on paper at AWS list rates (~$2.20-2.40/logical TB-month operating vs $23 S3 list; ~+$838/mo at full sell-through; ~7-month BOM payback, ~10 as a full cart). Tier B (max SSD, $9,258.90) is not competitive — NAND is 75.6% of its BOM; flips when 8 TB NVMe falls to ~$830 (-53%). Remaining buildable work ~3-5 person-months (H1 host-board finalization ~1 wk agent-actionable; node image + Starlink gateway weeks; shuttle protocol + QEXO energy currency 1-2 months; first build 2-4 wks gated on Will's ~$5.8-8.5K spend approval). Everything else is calendar/market: the >=90-day Nov-Jan winter pilot (annual window), longevity accrual, NAND/DDR5 price normalization, and the demand proof (~8 Will-hours) — which sits behind Will's rover-first ruling for the Duey channel (tension with the 2026-11-01 homelab proof plan flagged as G2, unresolved). BOM state 6 days stale at evaluation; next price-watch run due Mon 2026-11-16.
