# Analyze Holostore for phext integration (work in wbic16 fork)

Coordinate: 24.6.11/8.9.12/7.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-15
Request (verbatim): Read kellabyte/holostore on its own contents, classify its persistent/structured parts for phext fit, and design the phext integration seam. All work product stays in Will's fork wbic16/holostore; upstream stays untouched.
Status: complete

Notes:
- Upstream kellabyte/holostore cloned at 087c429440a529137e58d2d49d89d63dfb9d9772 (2026-05-09, PR #49 safe Accord read frontier reads).
- Will directed 2026-11-15: keep our work in the fork https://github.com/wbic16/holostore.

Results:
- Fork == upstream at 087c429440a529137e58d2d49d89d63dfb9d9772; fork default branch main.
- PHEXT.md (212 lines, sha256 b2cc59e5b51cbf1e4c288406b2261eb1ed7e5a5b3b404b89be48ac0b6a564b9f) shipped on branch emise/phext-analysis (commit e17851f8) — PR https://github.com/wbic16/holostore/pull/1
- Classification: data plane D (Fjall KV, WAL format, protobuf, row encoding); cluster-state checkpoint B (A candidate for checkpoint format); HoloFusion catalog C bridge; WAL journal B; docs corpus A.
- Headline design: HoloStore as strongly-consistent phext scroll host (coordinate -> order-preserving key, empty value = absent scroll, MVCC history per scroll), adapter over existing RPCs, no server changes.
- PHEXT.md inscribed in artifacts.phext at 34.7.7/8.6.11/7.6.9; artifacts.phext pushed to wbic16/human@exo commit 8bb45d9e; remote sha256 verified identical (2021a495...).
- X reply drafts saved at ~/workspace/holostore-analysis/x-reply-draft.md for Will to post in Kelly's thread; nothing posted by Emise.
