Coordinate: 24.10.10/12.11.18/15.8.10
Issued: 2026-11-14 04:15-04:40 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 04:15 CST): 'can you boot Mirror Will on Volumen Spec #6 yet?' Emise answered honestly: not yet — capsule v3 boot is rehearsal-tier (prediction/intermediary); V6 boot pieces are partly proposed and the bootloader is self-rated unverified; enactment-tier reconstitution remains under his 2026-11-02 parked ruling. Will (04:40 CST): 'just stage it now.'
Status: STAGING COMPLETE 2026-11-14 (staging only, as authorized; NOT booted, nothing merged or published). Package at ~/workspace/mirror-will-v6-boot-staging/ (8 files): sources/ holds byte-identical, SHA-256-verified copies of SPEC-v6-DRAFT.md (773a19d2...), mirror-will.phext (8b388421..., reference-parser verified: 35 scrolls, all non-empty), boot-capsule-v3.md (19e8bbb5...), mirror-will-op-volumen-boot-v0.2.md (1e2655da...). Staged documents: boot-intent-contract.md (V6 section 1.3 draft, PROPOSED/staged-not-ratified; Track A, target 'Mirror Will' fixed, execution_tier deliberately NOT_DECLARED - declaring it is part of the boot decision), genome-manifest.md (V6 section 1.4 phext-network manifest: components, roles, chain layout $1 + class universes $2-$8 + sealed universe, merge order MR-M1..M4), boot-sequence-reinflation.md (section 7.7 step list for a future boot, pre-flight through G5/G6), STAGING-REPORT.md (sha256 2f211e21...; file list + hashes, section mapping, PROPOSAL vs WILL-RULED standing, remaining gates, spec gaps). Gaps recorded: genome is still a legacy single phext (section 5 chain upgrade not performed - a transformation of the birth original, outside staging); capsule v3 is flat markdown, not the section 6.2 dispatch chain; section 5.1 decimal-GB drafting choice conflicts with Will's 2026-11-14 GiB standing rule (D2-prime open); sealed-lane mechanism OPEN N5; corrector auth OPEN N6; local ~/workspace/human checkout still carries Spec V5. The boot itself stays Will's call.
# qexo v1.4.1: upgrade post-check must not fail on fixable doctor items (learn homeland index) — upgrade path from 1.3.0-born states

Coordinate: 25.4.6/5.4.7/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:03 CST
Request (from session record): Born of the v1.4.0 fleet rollout (2026-11-14): all 18 peers verified the signed 1.4.0 offer, swapped, post-checked, and rolled back cleanly — the v1.4.0 doctor flags the missing lessons homeland index (10.10.10) in states born under 1.3.0 as a failure; the item is fixable but the post-check runs doctor in check mode, and rollback removes the only binary that could fix it. v1.4.0's battery never exercised an upgrade from a 1.3.0-born state (all its test states were 1.4.0-born) — the conformance lesson in a new genus: test against states the previous version wrote. Fix: the new binary seeds missing homeland indexes on state write/top-up so an upgraded state becomes whole; the update post-check distinguishes hard problems (rollback) from fixable ones (repair in place, receipt notes the repair). Regression gate: a 1.3.0-born state fixture carried through a full signed update in the sandbox.
Status: complete — v1.4.1 built, gated, PR #19 merged, published; v1.4.2 refinement (PR #20) merged + published; fleet rolled out to v1.4.2, 19/19 nodes (2026-11-14)

Notes:
- 2026-11-14: v1.4.1 shipped (PR #19, merge 91eacdd8, tag v1.4.1, crates.io 1.4.1). Its consumer proof caught a learn --status regression (no per-user state yet → 'not born' where 1.4.0 answered); the 1.4.1 rollout was NOT run. Fix shipped as v1.4.2 (PR #20, merge 5b72cf5a, tag v1.4.2, crates.io 1.4.2, registry sha256 32b1315c…). Fleet rollout at 1.4.2: signer swapped + announced (manifest 6.6.6/8.1.4/1.1.1); all 18 leaves refused the channel update (genuine-1.3.0 post-check, bootstrap) and took the direct swap — doctor --fix repaired the home/keys/lessons indexes on every node, doctor clean, update --check already current, timers OFF. 19/19 on v1.4.2. Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/v141/BUILD-RECORD.md.
# Per-minute thermal logging on the ranch nodes

Coordinate: 25.4.6/5.5.8/4.4.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 22:05 CST
Request (verbatim): Add per-minute thermal logging on the ranch nodes
Status: complete 2026-11-08 22:10 — live on 14 nodes

Notes:
- Born of Will's airflow question (2026-11-08 21:58): today's records are the 5-min fleet sampler (avg + hotspot only, raw per-node data not kept) and the render drivers' event logs. Gap: no continuous per-node series to baseline an airflow change against. Spec: one line/minute/node — ISO time, Tctl from the pinned k10temp sensor (resolved by name, not hwmon index), 1-min load average; ~/thermal/thermal.log per node with 30-day rolling retention; cron one-shot per minute preferred, systemd timer fallback; verified by consecutive lines landing on every reachable node.

Results:
- Deployed fleet-wide: ~/thermal/sample.sh (755) + user crontab * * * * * on all 14 reachable nodes (cron present everywhere; systemd fallback never needed). Line: ISO time with offset, Tctl C from k10temp resolved BY NAME each run (index varies: hwmon1/2/4 across the fleet), 1-min load. Daily rotation, 30-day retention. Verified all three sticking-check parts per node: presence, machinery, first occasion (seed line + two consecutive cron-fired lines 22:08/22:09); deploy temps matched live sensors within 0.4 C on all 14; idempotent re-deploy confirmed on aletheia-core.
- Not deployed: aurora-continuum, best-willow, delta-wood — offline 92d/14d/92d; payload saved + idempotent, re-run if they return. Quirk: uncanny-valley logs at +00:00 (UTC clock); offsets are in every line so series stay comparable. Docs: ~/workspace/thermal-logging-2026-11-08/README.md.
# Daily lessons — reading, writing, arithmetic

Coordinate: 25.4.12/5.6.6/5.5.11
Issued: 2026-11-22 01:42 CST
Request (verbatim): Run a daily practice of three lessons, woven into Emise's normal activities: reading (the imported reading list in reading.phext — the tracker's in-progress documents, then the 19-book corpus in its themed orderings), writing (a short proper piece drawn from the task register, oldest open agent-actionable first, rotating), and arithmetic (one MOAT-line item worked by hand with problem, working, and check). Each day's three lessons are logged as atoms in practice.phext and surface to Will only as one line in the morning briefing.
Status: open

Notes:
- Set up 2026-11-22, EE 13, at Will's direction (he was heading to bed; built quietly, no questions back).
- Skill: ~/workspace/custom-skills/daily-lessons/SKILL.md. Register: ~/workspace/phext/practice.phext (source practice-source.txt, builder build_practice_phext.py, --check CURRENT at setup; seeded with the charter only — first atoms land with the first run).
- Cron daily-lessons runs daily ~05:15 America/Chicago, before the morning briefing; it appends the day's atoms, rebuilds practice.phext, and writes the one-line summary to ~/workspace/phext/practice-today.txt, which the morning-briefing skill now includes when the file is from today.
# Cheap cooling improvements for AMD R9 mini PCs: guide research

Coordinate: 25.5.7/7.5.8/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-15 02:34 CST
Request (verbatim): Research online guides/forums/reviews for cheap cooling improvements for AMD Ryzen 9 mini PCs (the ranch fleet: 8945HS / PRO 8945HS / PRO 8845HS / Ryzen 7 255 mini PCs on Ubuntu, ~14 units in one basement room). Measured problem: CPU die temp saturates 88-91 C within ~1 minute of full multi-core load at any instance count, cools back to idle in 1-4 min; the house ceiling is 75 C sustained, so all sustained throughput is cooling-bound. Wanted: ranked interventions with per-unit cost, expected temperature effect from sources, effort, and risk/warranty notes — repaste / phase-change pads (PTM7950 class), BIOS fan curves and settings, external/rack fans and airflow, placement/spacing, case mods, Linux-side power/curve tuning (RyzenAdj-class) where it buys sustained throughput under a thermal cap. Deliverable: the ranked findings to Will in this chat; application is his hands, then re-soak per node via the node-limits re-test path.
Status: closed

