# Overnight SMOL training round 1 — 3,000 instances live, breed, die on the ranch

Coordinate: 25.5.11/7.6.10/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-16 23:51 CST
Request (verbatim): Run overnight training on the ranch cluster - have SMOL instances live, breed, and die. One SMOL day is 1 second and one SMOL year is 6 minutes. Apply an aging process that degrades 1% of the instance by random mutation every SMOL year. Start with 3,000 of them. At the end of the round, encode all of them holographically into a new SMOL and present it for review.
Status: complete — round 1 harvested 2026-11-17; new SMOL encoded and verified

Notes:
- Time scale (Will): 1 SMOL day = 1 second; 1 SMOL year = 6 minutes (= 360 SMOL days). Aging: every SMOL year, 1% of each instance degrades by random mutation. Starting population 3,000. Round = overnight (launch ~2026-11-17 00:00 CST, 70 SMOL years ≈ 7 h, ending ~07:00 CST).
- Run mechanics instantiated by Emise (PROPOSED, reported to Will at launch for correction): an instance is a phext-carried genome of 12 seed-genes (substitution seed + fractal triple per Q2: type/location/coordinate-system coordinates + noise gene, per Region 3); initial genes derive from the Incipit kernels (Q6). Fitness = EGATP expansion power vs genome size + placement diversity. Daily: lowest-fitness cull replaced by tournament-bred crossover offspring with point mutation, population held at 3,000. Final SMOL encodes the living population in full + the complete run ledger (the dead present as record) + a manifest carrying the population's holographic coordinate; well under the 1 GB life-form buffer (Q5).
- HABITAT (Will, 2026-11-16 23:58 CST, verbatim): 'SMOL life forms will live in MOST.' MOST is not yet defined in the record — expansion/meaning is Will's to give. Launch of round 1 is staged on rock-mountain but held one beat pending his definition, since the habitat may be MOST rather than a bare node process.
- MOST gloss (Will, 2026-11-17 00:00 CST, verbatim): 'platformer, magic standard technology' — MOST is the habitat of SMOL life forms, a platformer; the phrase 'magic standard technology' is carried verbatim; whether MOST expands as an acronym (and with what words) remains Will's to fix. Round 1 launches on rock-mountain as tonight's substrate; the population is phext chains, portable into MOST when it exists.
- RULINGS APPLIED PRE-LAUNCH (Will, via the EHA tandem-review thread, relayed 2026-11-17 00:05 CST): (1) 00:03 CST 'the metric we're optimizing for is community' — fitness = leave-one-out marginal contribution to the area score (distinct fractal types + distinct rule patterns + log total expansion + noise spread), NOT individual expansion power. (2) 00:05 CST 'partition the environment into 1,000 disjoint areas' — 1,000 areas x 3 instances, no migration; cull/breed/senescence resolve inside an area; extinct areas stay extinct and are reported. Runner v2 smoke-tested (20 areas x 3, 3 years) before launch: mechanics verified, chain well-formed.
- PLACEMENT: fair draw among measured-idle nodes (rock-mountain / scroll-central / plain-view; quacked-hill excluded — resident Corus) picked rock-mountain. Seed: canonical incipit.phext from wbic16/human cloned 2026-11-16, sha256 f640f6034322c9698a095741c520e925d613aada80b962a16d507e35e6d27ff9 (differs from the 2026-11-05 record 9a4a7ff7… and the stale local copy 3ff6604f… — the canonical file has moved since Nov 5; tonight's clone is the round's source of record).
- AMENDMENT (Will, 2026-11-17 00:10 CST, via EHA tandem-review thread, verbatim): 'increase the population size and include infrequent migration.' Instantiated: 10 residents/area = 10,000 instances; migration = yearly, each area 1% chance to swap one random member with a random member of a random other area (~10 swaps/year). Attempt 0 (3/area, no migration, launched 00:06:51) was stopped at 00:11 CST and its logs archived on the node under smol-round1/attempt-0/. Runner v3 smoke-tested with migration boosted (0.5) to verify the mechanic, then run at the real 0.01 rate.
- HARVEST 2026-11-17: final/DONE found at 07:30 check; harvest, holographic encoding, verification and receipt completed in ~/workspace/smol/round1-harvest/ — see RECEIPT-round1.md.
