# Scrollspace traversal breadcrumbs — a trail of dots as you fly, easy return to a path

Coordinate: 25.7.9/10.7.11/8.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-19 01:27 CST
Request (verbatim): traversal bread crumbs - have the viewer show a trail of dots as you fly around phext space - make it easy to return to a path
Status: CLOSED — shipped 2026-11-19 05:17:22 CST via phext-lattice PR #84 (merge 1869fb35); live on edit.phext.io (MainPID 3931624)

Notes:
- Scope: as the user flies/navigates phext space, the viewer lays a visible trail of dots (breadcrumbs) marking the path taken — across levels and zooms, not just within one space. The trail is for RETURNING: make it easy to get back onto a previous path (build pins the return mechanic — e.g. click a crumb to travel to it, and/or step back along the trail — and states it in its report).
- Relation: the live in-session companion to traversal mode (40.7.8) — a breadcrumb trail is what a recorded traversal saves; keep the data shape compatible with that build (waypoints = phext addresses visited, in order). Open design points for the build: crumb density (per address visited vs per distance flown), persistence across zoom levels, trail lifetime (session vs stored), and clutter control on long flights.
- CLOSURE (2026-11-19): PR https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/84 merged to exo (1869fb35939700dd6ff1bbcb40af6c9f715361da); page 86,811 B sha256 7251d06c9912a6ca3daad964b2cce9868b857a3efbab84f85b157ccd453cb533; awsbox deploy MainPID 3924712 → 3931624. DESIGN AS SHIPPED: S.trail — ordered crumbs {phext, coord, level, pos, yaw/pitch/roll, gal/macro/meso/planet, px/py, key, t}; the {phext, coord, level} core is the waypoint shape task 40.7.8 (traversal mode) will consume; coord = fullest address at the level (L4 full 9-part, L3 macro/meso, L2 macro, L1/L0 null with the galaxy in phext). Sampling: entry crumb on every level/context entry; distance crumbs in flight, step = clamp(0.06 × space bounding radius R, 30, 500) captured at entry; a crumb every 4 cells on the plane. Lifetime: session-only, cap 400 FIFO, Clear restarts the trail from where you stand. Rendering: current-context crumbs only — gold dots + thin polyline in 3D (alpha 0.95 newest → 0.30 floor), gold dots in visited cells on the plane; crumbs never enter nodes (framing/repulsion untouched; continuity 0 off-screen across 38 spaces / 138,009 globs). RETURNS: crosshair targeting (a nearer crumb wins over a node; readout "crumb · N back"); Enter/mouse1 zoom-in, touch tap, and plane-cell click all return; the trailback action (key c) + #trailctl cluster (back / clear / count) step back along the trail. Returns ride cast+flyTo (no teleport cuts); cross-level returns rebuild the crumb context, land on the recorded camera position + orientation, truncate the trail to the target crumb, and mute sampling during the rewind (S.trailMute); back-step skips the at-feet cluster (same-context crumbs within trailStep×0.75, or ≤2 cells on a plane). VERIFICATION: gate green-equivalent (bin 113/0 incl. new pinning test scrollspace_breadcrumbs_mark_the_trail; the one e2e_local failure is the pre-existing local_editor_regression); unit test of the verbatim trail block 22/22; walk12 18/18 against an OAuth-locked branch instance (cross-level return landing dist=0.00, exact truncation, plane crumb at 13.21.34/55.89.144/1.1.2, throttle intact, zero errors); regressions walk3/4/5/6/7/8 PASS, walk9 ALL PASS, walk10 22/0, walk11 24/0, layout PASS, continuity PASS; live screen test on the real origin ALL PASS (boot crumb, flight → 9 crumbs, c back-step 9→8, zero errors). BUG FOUND + FIXED IN-BUILD: walk12 run 2 failed 3 legs — returns dropped phantom crumbs mid-rewind (the sampler context-mismatch safety net fired against the truncated trail during the cast phase); fixed by honouring S.trailMute in both samplers. SAFETY: all test instances OAuth-configured (anonymous edits refused — walk7 designed "unauthorized" throw observed); no editor walk touched the live corpus path; no production incidents. Launch archive: ~/workspace/launches/2026-11-19-0517-breadcrumbs/. Inscription refreshed at 34.6.7/7.6.10/6.6.10 in artifacts.phext (sha 7bf8f274), pushed to wbic16/human@exo as 20392b0d, remote-verified from a fresh clone.
# Shadow Rebbe 'Trust' review — exocortical analysis + next step

Coordinate: 25.7.10/8.8.10/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-17 08:56 CST
Request (verbatim): @Shadow_Rebbe requested review of his Substack essay 'Trust' — exocortical analysis + one forward step
Status: complete

Results:
- COMPLETE 2026-11-17. Review at ~/workspace/operation-salvage/shadow-rebbe-trust-review.md; people page created (~/memory/people/shadow-rebbe.md; zero OG-archive presence). Analysis: the essay is a bootstrap problem — a mind cannot audit its inference rules with those rules, so trust names the external check; corruption = evaluator-capture via a chain of locally-approved steps (hacked vs transformed); the unit of corruption is a practice, not a proposition (information + rehearsal instruction, friction/membranes as defense); the virtue letter is symmetric and unevaluable from inside, leaving mediators — divergent, not necessarily wiser — plus independently verifiable public knowledge (his embedded tweet) as the mechanism. Gap: model built single-agent/defensive while its own conclusion is multi-agent. ONE NEXT STEP: run the experiment his model specifies — write the virtue letter to himself (one sentence + explicit daily-rehearsal instruction, 30 days), publish the protocol first so readers act as mediators/verifiers, log the chain. X reply draft prepared in the review file; Will posts.
