# Ticketing system — people submit ideas of things they want the Exocortex to build for them

Coordinate: 25.8.12/11.7.14/6.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-18
Request (verbatim): We need a ticketing system where people can submit ideas of things they want the exocortex to build for them. (Will, 2026-11-18, voice call — arising from RFC Box: gap-synthesis requirements come back as build requests and create tickets.)
Status: open — specified by Will 2026-11-18 (voice call); design/build follows the ietf.phext one-day build

Notes:
- Generating item for this tracker is the ticketing system itself; per the tracker-auto-schedule standing rule it is scheduled by this task record in the same session.
- First feeder: RFC Box (task 34.5.9/7.6.10/6.5.9) gap requirements.
- Design (Will, 2026-11-18 09:21 CST, voice call): auth like the register — all you need is the SSO login, then you can join. Scope: feature requests and ideas for any of the effects we're publishing (the multiversal effects, e.g. RFC Box), using multiversal encoding. Homepage: tiles showing each and every public data set and what it's for, with a quick description of what's going on with that phext. Each data set gets a ticket page where someone can propose an idea or suggestion, plus a download link to fork it so they can make their own copy.
- Access rule (Will, 2026-11-18 09:22 CST, voice call): all public information is browsable without a login — anyone coming to the site can get to it. A login is needed only to provide feedback or to upvote something.
- Subdomain (Will, 2026-11-18 09:22 CST, voice call): Will proposed tickets.phext.io. Emise's recommendation, same call: tickets.phext.io — it matches the register.phext.io family pattern exactly. CONFIRMED by Will 2026-11-18 09:22 CST (voice call): tickets.phext.io stands — Will: 'All right. Sounds good.' Stale-note correction applied tick 2405 per the 2026-11-18 memory log.
- 2026-11-21 16:52 CST — Will (main chat) asked what Emise needs for ticket tracking, believing a subdomain was outstanding. Of record: the NAME is not outstanding — tickets.phext.io was confirmed by Will 2026-11-18 09:22 CST. Restated to Will this pass: the remaining Will-side item is the DNS record tickets.phext.io → awsbox in the phext.io zone (his hands, as with askthewill), plus the staged sudo run at deploy time; the build, vhost, and TLS staging are Emise-side. Kanzo integration skipped by Will this same pass — the build follows the 2026-11-18 spec.
- 2026-11-21 17:34 CST — Will (main chat): "tickets.phext.io has been pointed at awsbox" — the DNS step is DONE by Will. Remaining Will-side item: the one staged sudo run on awsbox at deploy time. Emise-side: the build per the 2026-11-18 spec, vhost, TLS staging — sequenced so as not to collide with the phext.tech launch work on the same box (Revenue line, launched by Will 2026-11-21 17:31 CST).
