# Deploy and configure Jenkins for local CI — Stage 1

Coordinate: 26.3.3/3.3.5/3.3.7
Issued: 2026-11-15
Request (from session record): Deploy and configure Jenkins for local CI — Stage 1. Will's standing rule (2026-11-15 03:41 CST): never use GitHub CI/CD — always use local Jenkins runners.
Status: Stage 1 complete — Jenkins deployed, secured, 2 agents online, pilot job running on SCM polling; Stage 2 scoped in notes

Notes:
- Coordinate computed from essence words: deploy configure local Jenkins runners CI Phext repos ranch
- CI host question in agentic-pass plan answered: local Jenkins (Will, 2026-11-15)
- 2026-11-15: Jenkins LTS 2.580.2 + OpenJDK 21 installed on aletheia-core (Ubuntu 24.04); service enabled, bound to tailnet IP 100.88.154.1:8080 only via systemd override (After=tailscaled). Admin account 'admin' configured via init.groovy.d; credential stored only in /var/lib/jenkins/admin-credentials.txt (600, jenkins:jenkins); anonymous access denied (403 verified), admin auth 200 verified. Controller built-in agent: 4 executors, labels 'controller local ranch'.
- 2026-11-15: Plugins installed via CLI (59 enabled): git 5.11.0, workflow-aggregator 608, credentials-binding, timestamper 1.30, matrix-auth 3.3 (+deps). Authorization upgraded to ProjectMatrixAuthorizationStrategy (admin only); anonymous still 403.
- 2026-11-15: Pilot job 'phext-lattice' created: inline Pipeline, SCM polling H/5 * * * * (GitHub webhooks cannot reach the tailnet-only controller — polling is the standing mechanism), HTTPS checkout of exo, cargo test with RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache + SCCACHE_DIR=/mnt/mirrorborn/shared/sccache. Build #1 failed in 5s: rustup shim had no default toolchain for the jenkins user — fixed by installing stable toolchain for jenkins (rustc 1.100.0). Build #2 (28s): checkout exo @86f91020 (v1.3.1 bump), lib 188/188 pass, bins 99/99 pass, e2e 1/2 — local_editor_regression FAILED, the same pre-existing failure the PR #58 rebase check reproduced on clean exo. Pilot result: FAILURE attributable solely to that known pre-existing test; the CI path itself (poll/checkout/build/test/archive) works end to end.
- 2026-11-15: sccache note: jenkins-user builds got 0 hits / 152 write errors against the shared cache (cache subdirs are wbic16-owned; rustc 1.100 vs fleet 1.94 also changes keys) — shared cache effectively write-blocked for the jenkins user; Stage 2 fix. Local compile was still 28s end to end.
- 2026-11-15: Second agent registered: rock-mountain (load 0.30, Tctl 41.6C at probe) — OpenJDK 21 installed, inbound WebSocket agent as systemd service jenkins-agent (enabled), 2 executors, labels 'ranch rock-mountain'; secret held only in /home/wbic16/jenkins-agent/secret.txt (600) on the node + controller store; transfer copies destroyed. Smoke job agent-smoke-rock #1 ran on rock-mountain: SUCCESS.
- 2026-11-15: PLAN.md open question 3 (CI host) marked ANSWERED — local Jenkins runners (Will, 2026-11-15) with deployment state. Stage 1 complete. Stage 2 remains: jobs for the other active repos (libphext-rs first per plan), a notification route back to Emise, backup of /var/lib/jenkins, sccache shared-cache write fix for the jenkins user, and aligning the jenkins-user rustc (1.100.0) with the fleet toolchain (1.94) so cache keys match.

Results:
- Jenkins LTS 2.580.2 live on aletheia-core, http://100.88.154.1:8080 (tailnet-only), systemd-enabled; admin credential at /var/lib/jenkins/admin-credentials.txt (600, jenkins:jenkins); agents: Built-In Node 4 executors + rock-mountain 2 executors (both online, smoke-tested); pilot job phext-lattice build #2: 287/289 tests pass, 1 pre-existing e2e failure (local_editor_regression). Working scripts + job XML in ~/workspace/jenkins-stage1/.
# Next focus: vTPU — recheck HEAD against Reality Gate audit findings (ZLS handoff ask #1)

Coordinate: 26.4.8/6.5.8/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-17
Request (verbatim): Here's the handoff. Our next focus is likely vtpu.
Status: parked — Will ruled vTPU and ZLS short-term distractions 2026-11-17; focus is revenue/growth/efficiency

Notes:
- Sequencing from the ZLS x vTPU handoff (Emi, 2026-11-17; summary in PH: R&D): finish vTPU first. Remaining per the record: 6 of 14 Reality Gate units, claims 7/9 adjudicated, PRs #2 and #9 open, exo HEAD 9a70f939 (2026-11-05, no commits in 12 days at handoff time).
- R&D ask in order: (1) recheck vTPU HEAD against the audit findings — CSEND outbox->inbox delivery, Dormant-sentron benchmark paths, TTSM durable payload persistence vs metadata-only, PPT aliasing, SchedulerRedux / coop_smt vs coop_fleet, affinity and topology placement; (2) classify every lineage claim with evidence; (3) draft RFC ZLS-vTPU-OS-Contract-001; (4) name the smallest first PR that can falsify the per-core-OS claim. Gate discipline: no new kernel until the A/B/C comparison is complete.
- Audit findings describe snapshot 4660934 — a finding is 'unresolved' only if rechecked at current HEAD.
- HEAD recheck complete 2026-11-17 (full report ~/workspace/vtpu-head-recheck/REPORT.md; fresh API-assembled tree, blobs verified vs exo 0f21298c). HEAD confirmed 9a70f939 (2026-11-05), no commits since. Verdicts at HEAD vs the 4660934-snapshot audit: (1) CSEND delivery FIXED (coop_fleet flushes outbox->inbox, tested; coop_smt non-delivery now documented design). (2) Dormant-sentron benchmarks FIXED (W29 + cost::bench_d_pipe spawn, run, assert retirement). (3) TTSM STILL PRESENT, strong form: TemporalBlock has no payload field at all; commit() hashes and drops the bytes — no durable payloads and none retained in RAM; the durable implementation exists only in open draft PR #9. (4) PPT aliasing PARTIALLY FIXED: lossless 100-bit region key + set_flags mask fixed with passing injectivity tests; legacy raw-coordinate data leg still open per the repo's own doc. (5) SchedulerRedux implemented but BENCH-ONLY — constructed only in bench_w17_redux; no shipped executor closes the Redux loop; redux::Redux has no caller outside tests. (6) Affinity: BOTH — pin_thread primitive exists (only caller: SchedulerRedux::apply); construction-time topology placement (smt.rs) is the implemented W18 strategy. (7) W16 1.89x SMT still MODELED ONLY at HEAD; headline doc claim unretracted though the body discloses the model and the 0.09x real-thread attempt. OctaWire DSEL/DCMP defects still present at HEAD (scalar path correct); fix drafted in open PR #2. Test run: 3,934 passed / 1 failed (cluster::node_identity_detect, environment hostname assertion, unrelated) / 3 ignored; RG suites pass. NOTE: the '8/14 units, RG-0 done' formulation appears nowhere in the repo at HEAD — it comes from the external claims ledger; the repo's own baseline doc still lists RG-0 acceptance items pending. Next per the handoff order: (2) claims classification, (3) RFC draft, (4) smallest falsifying PR.
- PARKED by Will's ruling 2026-11-17 21:58 CST (PH: R&D): 'both vtpu and zls are distractions in the short-term - we need to constantly look for revenue/growth/efficiency gains.' Asks #2-#4 (claims classification, RFC, falsifying PR) do not proceed until Will lifts this. Ask #1's recheck results stand as the record.
