# Pangram Ultra — tell me which AI did it (IDEA)

Coordinate: 27.6.11/9.7.14/7.7.11
Issued: 2026-11-14
Request (verbatim): Pangram Ultra — Feat: "i want a pangram ultra that will tell me which AI did it." Source: https://x.com/DanielleFong/status/2121320103568679039 — figure out the simplest possible way to detect AI origin given any input text, without expensive inference.
Status: idea — parked at Will's direction 2026-11-14, not building

Notes:
- 2026-11-14: Simplest design found: linear classifier over hashed character 3-5 grams (+ word 1-2 grams, TF-IDF) with one weight vector per family (GPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Llama, Qwen, Human); ~40 stylometric features only for explanation. Inference is a sparse dot product, <1ms CPU, no LLM/perplexity call.
- 2026-11-14: Evidence: 47 stylometric features reach 73.7% on 7 families (academic), char n-grams 87.0% on chat (Modelometry); fine-grained 18-version ID is much harder (~26.8% stylometric), so v1 scope would be family, not version. Training discipline: same prompts across all models, hold out entire prompts/domains, mask self-ID, per-register training, calibrated abstention under ~100 words.
- 2026-11-14: Hard limit: one paraphrase/humanisation pass collapses source attribution (recovered <=3%), so this only works on raw/lightly-edited output.
- 2026-11-14 01:01 CST: Will directed: 'just mark this as an idea for now' — parked as idea, no build, no v0 harness.
# Audit of tonight's parallel deep knowledge work threads

Coordinate: 27.6.15/9.8.14/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): take an audit of how many deep knowledge work threads we're iterating on tonight - in parallel
Status: completed — audit delivered in side chat

Results:
- Live at 01:30 CST: 5 chats running (Architecture=phcc Slice 2, MOAT=libphext provable/tools, edit.phext.io=V14 final cluster render, Main=ultra.phext placement, Multi-Agent Swarm=this thread) with 3 builder agents actively running. Across the night: 10 deep threads iterated (phcc 5 stages, V14 r1-r3+final, ultra.phext, libphext provable, TOAPDD, Booch analysis, Twitter parse estimate, Carnegie/Dunbar, emise.phext budget work, simple.phext earlier) plus 5 continuous background loops (state.phext sampler, dashboard, hourly journal, task tick, Discord presence).
# paper lantern

