# Why is dispatch so broken lately — failure audit + standing tracker

Coordinate: 27.7.9/10.7.14/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-23 00:44 CST
Request (verbatim): Keep track of why dispatch is so broken lately; dig into it. Something is obviously slowing us down.
Status: OPEN — audit COMPLETE 2026-11-23 (EE 213); fixes await Will. Diagnosis in ~/workspace/dispatch-audit/REPORT.md; standing tracker stood up at ~/workspace/dispatch-audit/FAILURES.md (pre-filled, 24 entries). 9 families ranked by time lost: F1 silent session death (8 named in-window incidents + db floor of 13 abnormal depth-1 terminations; VM replaced ~every 2h; completion addressed to a session, not a place) is #1 at ESTIMATE 6-10h lost; F2 contention/placement ~3-5h (P034: ~2h hub stall vs 159s on ni-knight); F3 I/O wedges (plain-view NFS ~3.5h degraded; hatch PSI full 42.69%); F4 approval stalls (>=4 timed-out cards; 5 fleet nodes held); F5 deploy SIGTERM outage (FIXED, kill -9); F6 hub SSH push wall 0/20 (FIXED 2026-11-21, fanout 20/20); F7 safety-check trips x3; F8 produced-not-landed (sweep stable 62-64 flags / 33 branches / 19 repos); F9 data-plane interference near-miss. Total ESTIMATE ~11-17h agent time lost 2026-11-18..23. Top proposal: finish durable dispatch stage 2 (task 36.7.16) and put build coordinators on it — stage 1 proven 2026-11-21 but hub-only. Task stays OPEN: mechanism fixes are proposals only, awaiting Will's go.

Notes:
