# Port qexo to Android: a full phextnet node Will can run on his phone

Coordinate: 27.8.10/9.8.12/8.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-13 01:03 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-13 01:03 CST, from his Android phone): 'port qexo to web or android so I can join from my phone'. Emise's pick, stated to Will: Android first — a web client can browse but cannot BE a node (no durable state, no GPG identity in a browser tab); an Android build is a true peer: own key, own state.phext, register/list/update/evolve. Route: cross-compile for Android (NDK aarch64-linux-android; static musl as documented fallback), run under Termux (gnupg from Termux for the crypto layer, QEXO_STATE valve for the state path), platform-gate the systemd timer honestly. A serve-hosted web window remains a later, separate slice.
Status: MERGED by Will 2026-11-14 (wbic16/qexo PR #1, merge commit e92f69ab, live-verified via GitHub API)

Notes:
- Port home redirected by Will 2026-11-13 01:05 CST: the Android port lives in wbic16/qexo, NOT quarterexo (which this slice leaves untouched). Seed at wbic16/qexo@exo d3e24554 held only an MIT LICENSE, byte-identical to quarterexo's — carried unchanged in the ported tree.
- Route 1 carried: aarch64-linux-android via NDK r27c (musl fallback not needed). Binary: ~/workspace/qexo-task/fleet-keys/qexo-v1.3.0-android-arm64, SHA-256 9f410a1f63e1a7398ad6f9a30b72faabb5fa0840b6db9b84db98e6e0f5714493 (ARM aarch64, /system/bin/linker64, libc+libdl only).
- Will (2026-11-14 01:50 CST): 'I'll merge https://github.com/wbic16/qexo/pull/1 and you can roll the next qexo changes into another PR.' Register #91 closes when the merge verifies live; the internal-GPG change (34.7.8/8.6.9/5.6.10) is the head of that next PR.

Results:
- PR #1 https://github.com/wbic16/qexo/pull/1 — branch emise/android-v1.3.0 @ 12cfe70b, parented on qexo exo d3e24554, force disabled; remote tree verified 37/37 blobs+modes identical to staged.
- Gates (aletheia-core, cargo 1.94.0): cargo test 49/49 (48 baseline + Android state-path pick test); release build OK; wiring-check OK (12 modules); Linux battery GREEN (incident volume, volume lens), doctor ok, 0 json in state; Android LINK produced the arm64 binary with both Android-only strings verified in the shipped bytes.
- Deltas vs v1.2.0: Android state-path fallback ($HOME/.qexo, cfg(android)-scoped, birth note printed), Android timer report (no systemd; names the manual Termux evolve pass), stamps 1.3.0, CHANGELOG/SHIP-NOTES. Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/android/BUILD-RECORD.md (incl. full phone instructions).
- Honest limit: no Android runtime on the ranch — phone execution is Will's report, as Windows execution was for v1.0.4. On merge, batches into release task 40.7.5/8.7.11/6.8.13.
- Android port PR #1 merged to wbic16/qexo exo at e92f69abc4c5f483381b184fabb46ece33c242da. Register #91 resolves on the tick's live verification.
# willbox — merge rfcbox, wikibox, phccbox into one box, minimize size

Coordinate: 27.8.10/11.8.14/8.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-21 07:53 CST
Request (verbatim): merge the three into willbox, see how small you can make it
Status: done 2026-11-21 — willbox built on scroll-central; rebuild-from-priors gate PASS (all parts byte-exact); pushed wbic16/willbox@exo 479af22; smallest distribution 94,340,560 B (xz -9e)

Notes:
- 2026-11-21 07:53 CST: issued by Will in main chat. Parts of record: rfcbox = ietf.phext 564,589,207 B raw (wbic16/rfcbox@exo, xz 5 parts + setup.sh); wikibox = stage-2 config D box 11,275,462 B packaged (2,930 articles, scroll-central ~/wikibox-stage2/); phccbox = phccbox-v11 ELF 5,136,620 B (~/workspace/phccbox/phccbox-v11). Worker brief: assemble on scroll-central, build willbox.phext holding all three, measure joint-compression size vs sum of parts, hash everything.
- 2026-11-21 07:55 CST amendment (Will): home is https://github.com/wbic16/willbox ; hold all three as phext priors (wikibox-codec sense — prior state in the phext, not verbatim payloads); rebuild locally — all three parts must rebuild byte-exact from the priors on scroll-central. Amendment relayed to the background worker.
- 2026-11-21 ~08:30 CST: DONE on scroll-central, per the 07:55 amendment (priors + local rebuild + home wbic16/willbox). willbox.phext 582,287,481 B, sha256 5378b6b13f477e631088630df6310aa7a932bd596b8a73f990c76d99487d7949: library 1 home/manifest (3 scrolls), library 2 ietf prior (10,109 scrolls, stream verbatim), library 3 wikibox prior (259 scrolls, stream verbatim), library 4 phccbox prior (header + 6 base85 chunk scrolls). All parts verified on arrival by size+sha256 (ietf reconstructed via rfcbox setup.sh on the node). REBUILD GATE PASS: all three parts rebuilt byte-exact from willbox.phext alone (ietf 9ecd7946..., wikibox 43df8ed4..., phccbox a4722205...); willbox round-trip implode(parse)==orig byte-exact. SIZE: smallest verified-lossless distribution = one xz -9e stream, 94,340,560 B — vs 581,001,289 B sum of parts as they stand (6.16x) and vs 125,325,750 B shipped standalone compressed forms (-24.7%). Honest decomposition: at equal xz -9e settings the parts separately total 93,553,072 B, so joint compression is at parity (+0.84%) — the shipped-forms win is a compression-settings win (ietf's shipped xz was light: 113,061,600 vs 84,141,476 at -9e alone); the merge buys one artifact/manifest/hash, stated plainly in REPORT.md. Pushed to wbic16/willbox@exo commit 479af22 (first commit; repo was empty, exo already its branch; no force): README, REPORT.md, LICENSE, setup.sh, phextlib.py, build_willbox.py, rebuild_from_willbox.py, data/ 4 xz parts + SHA256SUMS + PARTS-SHA256SUMS, scripts 100755. Fresh-clone verification: setup.sh sha256 OK, rebuild gate PASS from the clone alone, ls-tree blobs identical to pushed tree. willbox.phext stays on scroll-central ~/willbox/. Report: ~/workspace/willbox/REPORT.md (VM) and in the repo.
