# Hosting cost profile vs Lincoln colocation/dedicated with fiber

Coordinate: 28.6.9/8.6.11/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-15 15:44 CST
Request (verbatim): Assemble the current annual cost of web properties (domains from the 2026-11-06 inventory as corrected 2026-11-15, awsbox hosting, any NFSN hosting, bandwidth) from records, then price Lincoln NE colocation and dedicated hosting on fiber against it, with a recommendation.
Status: Dispatched 2026-11-15 to a coordinator (records assembly + priced market research). Will's own figure (2026-11-15 15:44 CST): AWS is roughly $100/mo (~$1,200/yr) — his estimate, not a billing pull. COMPLETE 2026-11-15: verdict — Lincoln colo/dedicated does NOT beat AWS on price. Current profile ≈ $126/mo ≈ $1,512/yr (AWS ~$100/mo Will's estimate + domains ~$312/yr now, ~$292/yr post-migration). Cheapest Lincoln option: Binary.Net (The Vault, 134-206 S 13th St) single-server colo from $150/mo published; with a $0 ranch mini PC the profile is ≈ $174/mo ≈ $2,092/yr (+$580/yr vs AWS); refurb 1U ≈ $2,901/yr; cheapest NE dedicated (HostColor Omaha) $499/mo ≈ $6,280/yr. Flip conditions: AWS past ~$150/mo or sustained egress >~1.7 TB/mo. Binary.Net also rents VPS in the same facility from $50/mo — the only published sub-$100 Lincoln option, but a rented slice. Deliverable: ~/workspace/your_files/hosting-cost-comparison-2026-11-15.md.
