# Benchmarks: HoloStore on the HoloPhext engine

Coordinate: 28.6.10/9.7.11/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-15
Request (verbatim): run benchmarks against HoloStore using holo-phext (after integrating it with phext-lattice) - provide an executive summary of what's changed and how the performance baseline has shifted, if at all
Status: complete

Notes:
- Will, 2026-11-15 16:35 CST: run benchmarks against HoloStore using holo-phext (after integrating it with phext-lattice) - provide an executive summary of what's changed and how the performance baseline has shifted, if at all. Adoption path from holo-phext DESIGN.md: swap round-2's hand-rolled store for the engine, RESP layer + bench harness untouched. Baselines of record (round 2, 2026-11-15): SET pipe-50/10thr 152,471; GET pipe-50 341,613; SET pipe-1 9,837; GET pipe-1/50thr 51,924 ops/s; 30k load 0.20s; SIGKILL 0 of 272,500 acked lost.

Results:
- COMPLETE 2026-11-15. HoloStore's storage core re-based on the HoloPhext engine (holostore branch emise/holo-phext-engine @ b0ec835, PR #2 https://github.com/wbic16/holostore/pull/2, stacked on PR #1); PHEXT.md round 3 carries the full table. Mapping: 65,536 hash buckets at small coordinates, one scroll per bucket, one engine transaction per writer batch. Per-key scrolls at checksum-spread coordinates were abandoned: phext encodes coordinate distance as unary delimiter runs, so hash-sized components are unpayable — identity in content, coordinates are pagination. Benchmarks (same-day, same bench): GET pipe-50 306,635 vs round-2 hand-rolled 336,392 ops/s (par); SET pipe-50 74,659 vs 156,614 (gap = per-entry integrity: ~210 vs ~60 WAL bytes/op); SET pipe-1/10thr 7,143 vs 9,769 (also resolves round 2's recorded 9,837: it was 10 threads); GET pipe-1 54,203 vs 54,956 (par); load 30k 0.36s vs 0.19s. SIGKILL mid-load: 160,800 acked, 0 lost. The integration found and fixed FOUR HoloPhext defects (0.2.1->0.2.4, regression tests each): quadratic WAL recovery (48 CPU-min on a 10k-txn log), quadratic batch append, torn-UTF8 WAL open failure, per-transaction overlay clones (SET 1,490 ops/s before the delta-overlay redesign). phext-lattice steps 1-2 re-verified at the 0.2.4 pin (a23b0fb on PR #70 https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/70): 183+101+4+3 green, only the pre-existing e2e failure.
