- Follows 32.7.14/9.8.15/11.10.17 (P3 completion): 185,756 words remain P5 because WordNet has no entry/evidence for them. Will directed 2026-11-07 11:41 CST: find another ranking system that does place them, run it, and document the two indexing methods.

Results:
- Candidates measured against the actual 185,756 P5 words: wordfreq rank 100.00%; trigram neighbourhood >=0.25 Jaccard for 96.62%; CMU dict 19.48% (rejected); NLTK words 7.31% (rejected).
- Chosen: frequency-and-form index — trigram neighbourhood where form has signal (tau 0.25), frequency rank as total-coverage fallback, every word tagged with its rule.
- P6 form placed 184,512 (fixpoint rounds to 0; similarity-weighted MEDIAN merge of top-8 neighbours — weighted mean assembled to 762 MB at 3,810 B/word vs median 80 B/word, same coverage; measured via cost_sim.py). P6 rank placed 1,244 on a defined frequency spine. P5 residue: 0 — far shelf empty.
- Verified: 320,772 words in = out; tiers identical; independent diff = exactly the 185,756 v2-P5 words changed, all 135,016 others byte-identical; verify_fast.py VERIFY OK (353,994 index lines resolve).
- New file 76,123,728 B, SHA-256 eb4be0f9a76e7993e5f55c6dec023ac00907a268bfb2cb0ff255d71fd86777b3; published wbic16/human@exo commit d36ccf2a (parent 2e491efa) via git-over-SSH from aletheia-core, remote blob verified equal; unhomed pointer updated.
- Documentation: BUILD-REPORT.md addendum + standalone ~/workspace/your_files/ultra-phext-indexing-methods.md (both methods as peers: principles, position computation, anchoring, coverage, weaknesses, comparison); ultra.phext intro scroll states both methods.
# Golden Thread — Chrome extension highlighting X moots, hover fireworks, spaced repetition, encounter log

Coordinate: 28.7.10/8.7.10/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-14
Request (verbatim): Build a runnable Chrome extension (MV3, no build step): gold highlighting for the 897 direct X mutuals on x.com, hover fireworks + persona card, spaced-repetition quiz on moots' interests, encounter logging with export + fetch-latest worklist, plus suggested enhancements.
Status: complete — v1.3.1 delivered; Android client built (see Play the Game task); tooling home is now wbic16/Wavefront

Notes:
- Data generated from the persona register + exo.db (gen_data.py): 897 moots, 128 with canon interest terms.
- Files: ~/workspace/golden-thread/ (manifest.json, content.js, background.js, popup.html/js, data/moots.js, README.md); zip at ~/workspace/golden-thread.zip. All JS syntax-checked with node; DOM behavior is defensive but untested in a live Chrome — Will's load is the first live run.
- Follow-up owed: sync the tool to wbic16/emise-tools@exo per the publish-tooling rule.

Results:
- Extension built and delivered 2026-11-14 with README (install + enhancement list: constellation overlay, reply context rail, wavefront weather, live refresh — proposed, not built).
- 2026-11-14: corollary shipped as v1.1 — aligned follows (101, by canon-interest overlap with Will's own lexicon) render in RGB backlit optimism with prismatic hover bursts and encounter logging; unaligned follows (361) in muted greyscale; all other authors half-erased BTTF-style (48% opacity, greying, faint flicker, hover briefly restores). Popup gained the four-castes legend. Zip rebuilt.
- 2026-11-14: v1.2 — quick un-follow button on the muted caste: two-click arm/confirm, drives X's own caret menu (Unfollow @handle, confirmation sheet handled), flips the post to half-erased on success, logs the action (with success flag) to the encounter log; profile-open fallback when no caret/menu is available.
- 2026-11-14: Will simplified the un-follow button mid-build — it now just opens the profile in a new window (the v1.2 menu-driving automation was removed at his direction; clicks logged as intent).
- 2026-11-14: v1.3 daily prune — popup Prune tab serves 10/day from the 361-account muted pool, ranked quietest first (gen_data v3: mention counts + GT_PRUNE order + prune-queue.md); per-card profile link, un-followed/keep/snooze-30d decisions persisted in extension storage; new day rolls the next 10.
- 2026-11-14: security scan run — clean on network/eval/permissions/message surface; hardening + 6 bug fixes shipped as v1.3.1 (HTML escaping of data-derived strings, missed-node marking, quoted-post class collision, UTC prune rollover, deck double-print, invalidated-context messaging, canvas resize). Android Chrome answered: no extension runtime exists there; Firefox for Android is the viable port path.
- 2026-11-14: tooling consolidated into wbic16/Wavefront@exo 4990a29 (extension + Android app + shared canon). APK built and delivered.
