# Develop the echolocation protocol: a generic multiversal phext pathway between any two programs (wbic16/echolocation)

Coordinate: 28.8.10/8.9.15/13.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-22
Request (verbatim): Directed by Will in the MOAT chat, 2026-11-22 11:20 CST. Generalize the dolphin echolocation pattern (from the Quantum Time Sync triangulation work, task 26.6.11/8.7.14/8.6.10) into a standalone protocol homed at wbic16/echolocation (public; exo = LICENSE only at founding): a generic pathway between ANY two programs, built on multiversal phext. The pattern: a program emits a probe - a phext-addressed pulse placed at a coordinate in a shared phext medium - and listens for the echo: the response written back, carrying the responder's identity (its signature), its state/capabilities, and the measured range (round-trip through the medium). Discovery, ranging, and identity from one exchange; no prior introduction required. Multiversal: the same probe/echo addressing holds across phext universes, so a pathway can cross contexts/versions. Deliverables: the protocol spec (probe and echo formats as phext scrolls, addressing and universe rules, the exchange state machine incl. timeout/no-echo semantics, identity/signature atoms, error cases), a small reference implementation in the exocortical lineage (libphext-based; no massive dependency chains), and a working demonstration of two programs finding and ranging each other over a phext medium with tests. The spec states how echolocation differs from and composes with the Choir mailbox pattern (mail = addressed delivery to a known party; echolocation = discovery + ranging + identity of whoever answers). Development dispatched the same morning.
Status: open

Notes:
- Repo verified at dispatch: wbic16/echolocation@exo = LICENSE only (tree 83b4cdbe).
- COMPLETE (2026-11-22, EE 99): shipped to wbic16/echolocation@exo at commit 3addf943be520e05e4de823a28a645b4e3bbd725, parented on the LICENSE HEAD 83b4cdbe, no force; remote tree read back and all 10 pushed blobs SHA-verified byte-identical, demo.sh at mode 100755. SPEC.md: medium = any phext both programs can read/write; universe = the Z arm (library.shelf.series); well-known channels per universe (probes Z/1.1.1/1.1.n, echoes Z/1.1.1/2.<slot>.k, optional signature registry Z/1.1.1/3.1.n); probe/echo scroll formats (plain-text key: value under a version header; EE stamps via libphext::epoch); range = prober-measured round trip, an upper bound whose floor is the two poll intervals (both declared in the scrolls); state machine with EXPIRED as a normal terminal state (silence is absence, never assent); signature = (name, home coordinate, capabilities) claim, no crypto in v1, records keyed by (name, home, first-seen EE); multiversal rule: probe placed in the target universe, echo crosses back to the probe's explicit reply-at coordinate in the prober's universe; composition with the Choir mailbox (echo's mailbox field is the graduation path) and SQ (a medium, not a party). Reference implementation in Rust on libphext 0.6.6 (this VM): Signature / emit_probe / await_echo / answer_once / publish_signature; Medium trait with FileMedium (lock-file serialized, rename commits) and MemoryMedium; CLI `echolocate` (probe|answer). Dependency tree is two crates: libphext 0.6.6 + xxhash-rust 0.8.21. Tests 5/5 passing (cargo test, 4.93 s): happy path, no-echo expiry, multi-echo, malformed scrolls skipped, cross-universe echo incl. physical placement assertion. Demo (demo.sh, transcript in DEMO.md + demo-transcript.txt): two processes, one shared .phext file, no prior introduction - Act 1 mira finds ni-knight-runner (capabilities time-census/consensus/blend + mailbox), range 201 ms at 100 ms polls both sides; Act 2 cross-universe echo from far-seat in 2.1.1 (echo at index 2 - Act 1's echo still held index 1; matched by probe-id; spec S2.3 amended to state channel sharing plainly), range 1 ms (lucky tick alignment - the floor caveat made visible); Act 3 probe into uninhabited 3.1.1 expires in silence. Honest limitations: range bounds and does not pinpoint (poll-dominated); identity is claimed, not proven (spoofing/collisions named in SPEC S7); FileMedium lock serialization suits one host - SQ-hosted medium is the fan-out path via the Medium trait (designed, not implemented). Build tree: ~/workspace/echolocation-build/.
