# Computronium worktree 3 — start from an older version, from 2007

Coordinate: 29.4.7/6.5.8/4.3.6
Issued: 2026-11-16 07:14 CST
Request (verbatim): Will (2026-11-16 07:14 CST): a third parallel worktree attempt (alongside sampling 34.5.8/7.6.11/6.5.9 and the scroll-by-scroll build 18.6.9/8.6.11/5.5.7): start with an older version of Chromium, from 2007. Noted for the record: Chromium's public source begins September 2008 (initial release drop / first repo revisions); no 2007 Chromium source exists publicly — WebKit, its engine ancestor, does have 2007 source. Dispatched faithfully as: take the EARLIEST obtainable Chromium tree (the September 2008 initial drop, from the repo history already on aletheia-core), encode it as one phext under the Step-1 discipline, and run the same scroll-by-scroll function-placement build with de-duplication as we go (worktree 2's machinery). The early tree's resolved size is itself a skeleton datum. If Will meant WebKit 2007 instead, he will say so and the attempt re-roots.
Status: closed — complete 2026-11-16. COMPLETE 2026-11-16 (~07:38 CST), hub ~/chromium-census/worktree-2007/RESULTS.md. Provenance (a trap avoided): the history has four grafted roots — the earliest by date (2001-08-24, cvs2svn) is the WebKit/Blink lineage, rejected on evidence; the chromium/src lineage root is 2008-07-26. Built artifact = launch-day trunk state: commit 729065e3cfed (2008-09-02 22:06 UTC, SVN chrome/trunk/src@1659), the last src-lineage commit of public launch day. Tree: 29,096 files / 3,539,582 physical lines / 1,784,407 code. Encode round-trip 29,097/29,097 clean. Build: 50,707 instances → 33,169 canonical, 17,538 duplicates (34.6%), 57,950 lines avoided; render gate 0 mismatches; resolved build 62,266 scrolls / 3,618,228 lines, verified 62,266/62,266. BOTH the raw 2008 tree (3.54M) and the resolved build (3.62M) sit UNDER the 5M budget — but the resolved build is +2.2% lines LARGER than the raw tree: canonical-header + standoff overhead outweighs duplicate removal at 2008 scale; the win is structural (every function once, behavior-named, full provenance), not shrinkage. CAVEAT for downstream lineage work: the git conversion omits the DEPS externals — V8, the WebKit engine core, icu38, googleurl, gtest, breakpad are NOT in this artifact; it is the browser + WebKit port/glue layer only. Identity caveat as elsewhere: norm_hash collapses degenerate bodies (empty bodies one group of 1,323; return-member getters one group of 1,769) — syntactic-normalized identity, an upper bound on semantic identity.
# Spin up quickfork.net as the Bark portfolio site

Coordinate: 29.4.10/7.6.12/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-16 00:14 CST
Request (verbatim): spin up https://quickfork.net/ to highlight our edit.phext.io submission to Product Hunt, Mutable OS integration, and Markdown Wizard
