# phcc Jenkins build-out — jobs for every platform, Windows 11 x64 / Android APK / Ubuntu 24.04 x64 / WASM first

Coordinate: 29.6.8/6.5.9/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-20
Request (verbatim): Set up Jenkins jobs to build phcc (wbic16/phcc) on every platform, prioritizing Windows 11 64-bit, Android APK, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS 64-bit, and WASM — the platforms Will uses daily and can personally test. First get phcc building and passing ./configure && make && make test -k natively on a ranch node; then create the jobs via the existing ranch Jenkins mechanism in priority order; then the remaining common-platform targets (i386/aarch64/armv7/riscv64 Linux, macOS x86_64/aarch64, Windows i386/arm64) as build jobs labelled untested pending recruited testers. Run every job once and report real results per platform.
Status: complete

Notes:
- Directed by Will on the 2026-11-20 voice call (~12:17 CST): get phcc building again and set up Jenkins jobs for every platform. Jenkins management is Emise's responsibility (Will, 2026-11-17); CI runs only on ranch Jenkins, never GitHub Actions (standing rule 2026-11-19).
- Priority platforms (the machines Will uses day to day and can personally test): (1) Windows 11 64-bit, (2) Android APK, (3) Ubuntu 24.04 LTS 64-bit, (4) WASM (added by Will as a fourth priority on the same call).
- Build out support for all common platforms (the rest of the old 11-target matrix from phcc's removed build.yml: i386/aarch64/armv7/riscv64 Linux, macOS x86_64/aarch64, Windows i386/arm64), but those are NOT Will-testable — testers must be recruited for them; a cross-build is not a tested platform.
- Execution order: (1) phcc building + make test -k green natively on a ranch node before any jobs; (2) discover the existing ranch Jenkins job mechanism and follow it; (3) create jobs in priority order; (4) remaining common-platform build jobs labelled untested-pending-recruited-testers; (5) run every job once and report real per-platform results.
- Related: jenkins-debt entry for phcc in ~/workspace/repo-audit/jenkins-debt.md (from CI cleanup task 39.4.5/5.4.8/4.4.12).
- STAGE 1 COMPLETE (2026-11-20): phcc@exo 2f7583db builds natively on aletheia-core (Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS x86_64) — configure/make/make test -k all rc=0, test suite prints ALL TESTS PASSED. No source fixes were needed for the native build.
- MECHANISM: ranch Jenkins controller on aletheia-core (100.88.154.1:8080, LDAP realm, tailnet-only). Jobs are Pipeline jobs created programmatically by init.groovy.d scripts at startup (estate pattern: 06-fleet.groovy). Deployed /var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/08-phcc-jobs.groovy (generator: ~/workspace/phcc-jenkins/gen_jobs.py) + systemctl restart jenkins. The script converges job definitions on every startup and schedules a build whenever a definition changes or a job has no builds. All 13 jobs poll SCM (exo branch) every 5 minutes; there are no GitHub webhooks on this estate. Jobs run on the controller node (label 'controller', 4 executors).
- TOOLCHAINS provisioned on aletheia-core for the jobs: mingw-w64 (i686 + x86_64), gcc cross compilers (i686, armhf, aarch64, riscv64), qemu-user, Wine (with system-wide binfmt registration so PE binaries run directly), Android SDK + NDK 26.3 at /opt/android-sdk with shims at /opt/android-shims, Emscripten 3.1.45 (emsdk; the apt emscripten package is broken) at /opt/emsdk with shims at /opt/em-shims, APK app sources at /opt/phcc-android-app + /opt/phcc-apk-build.sh.
- RESULTS — first full build wave (2026-11-20 ~12:44–13:00 CST), 12 of 13 jobs SUCCESS: phcc-ubuntu-24.04-x64 #2 SUCCESS (native build + full test suite, ALL TESTS PASSED); phcc-windows-11-x64 #3 SUCCESS (mingw phcc.exe, Wine smoke: --version OK, compiles hello.c, hello.exe runs returning 42; artifact zip 668,547 B; final on-device test is Will's on his Windows 11 machine); phcc-android-apk #2 SUCCESS (NDK aarch64 phcc packaged as a signed APK, org.phext.phcc, 316,830 B; on-device test is Will's on his phone); phcc-wasm #1 SUCCESS (Emscripten phcc, node phcc --version smoke; artifact zip 241,122 B); phcc-linux-i386 #2, phcc-linux-armv7 #2, phcc-linux-aarch64 #2, phcc-linux-riscv64 #2 all SUCCESS (target hello executed under qemu-user returning 42); phcc-macos-x64 #2 and phcc-macos-arm64 #2 SUCCESS (real Mach-O executables, 17,528 B each, linked -nostdlib — see macOS note); phcc-windows-x64-cross #1 and phcc-windows-arm64 #1 SUCCESS (real PE32+ hello executables).
- EXPECTED RED: phcc-windows-i386 #1 FAILURE at the Target hello stage with 'unresolved reference to _SetUnhandledExceptionFilter' — a genuine phcc defect found by this work (the bundled win32 crt1.c/wincrt1.c call this stdcall function; kernel32.def exports it, but the i386 PE import resolution does not match the decorated name; x86_64-win32 links fine). The cross compiler itself builds. The job description carries the root cause; the job stays red until phcc fixes i386 PE import name resolution. FOLLOW-UP (phcc source work, not CI): fix i386-win32 PE import resolution for stdcall-decorated names.
- CORRECTION to the manual pre-checks: the macOS cross compilers were initially reported as producing Mach-O hellos; in fact the plain link silently produced 0-byte outputs (phcc prints 'library c not found' but exits 0). Root cause: linking against the macOS C library needs macOS SDK .tbd stub files, which the phcc repo does not ship (the old GitHub matrix ran these targets on real macOS runners). The jobs therefore verify a -nostdlib Mach-O executable link, and the limitation is stated in both macOS job descriptions. FOLLOW-UP: ship or generate minimal .tbd stubs if full macOS libc linking is wanted.
- FOLLOW-UP (minor phcc source defect): tccasm.c:964 uses tolower without <ctype.h> — an implicit-declaration warning under gcc but a hard error under the NDK's clang 17. The Android shims carry -Wno-implicit-function-declaration as the accommodation; the proper fix is the include in phcc source.
- All non-priority platform jobs are labelled in their descriptions: UNTESTED on real hardware — no tester recruited yet (Will, 2026-11-20); a green build is not a tested platform. Recruiting testers for i386/armv7/aarch64/riscv64 Linux, macOS x64/arm64, and Windows arm64 remains open. phext-vr's deploy job is the next item on the Jenkins debt list after this task.
