# UPGRADE.md — phextura focus document (LaTeX joined the 21st century, as .txt -> .phext)

Coordinate: 29.6.9/8.7.13/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-11 22:10 CST
Request (verbatim): Will: "let's focus on the upgrade that feels like latex joined the 21st century, just like .txt -> .phext"
Status: completed — UPGRADE.md written and published to wbic16/phextura@exo

Notes:
- Focus document: states the upgrade claim (feel at home in five minutes, feel the century in the first hour), the .txt->.phext analogy worked in 8 rows each with a design citation and an honest state label, continuity inventory (595 templates at templates/templates.phextura; Overleaf 30-minute path as familiarity baseline; math deferred to the Sentron settlement), century inventory (6 documented pains with mechanisms and states), deprioritization (registry-extraction internals, warrant invalidation mechanics, same-class machinery), and the three-question acceptance test for author-facing decisions.
- Published: phextura@exo commit 1aef570f, parented on 012053f (templates import), force disabled; remote bytes fetched back and verified identical, sha256 d8310a69ae510bac33a349b01cea9f6bda2f88608a83cd372a237b89ba6313cd. Local copy: ~/workspace/phextura-design/UPGRADE.md.
# Scrollspace traversal video — time hopping to your advantage, set to "Across the Years", 4:20

Coordinate: 29.6.9/10.7.11/7.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-19 01:15 CST
Request (verbatim): make a traversal video for scrollspace - one that shows how to use time hopping to your advantage - set it to the tune of Across The Years (attached). 4:20 in length
Status: open — V3 VOYAGE PREPASS delivered 2026-11-19 21:50 CST, at Will’s audit gate (final 60fps->24fps film-grain render waits for his audit)

Notes:
- Soundtrack: ~/workspace/user/files/Across_the_Years.mp3 (Will’s song, attached 2026-11-19). Target runtime 4:20 (260 s).
- Subject: a Scrollspace traversal demonstrating time hopping used to your advantage — in Scrollspace terms, one coordinate is held by many phexts at once (66 hold 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1) and every scroll is an address you can jump to instantly: hop the shared address across the multiverse / across the corpus’s accumulated history instead of flying. Shot list must be verified against the real hosted corpus before capture.
- Production: Mythic Film Production pipeline (~/workspace/custom-skills/mythic-film-production/SKILL.md); capture via the existing Scrollspace walk harnesses (Playwright, real corpus); edit/mix node-resident and checkpointed (this VM swaps ~every 2 h). Deliverable: the finished mp4 in this chat.
- Direction (Will, 2026-11-19 01:16 CST, verbatim): "End on 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1" — the final landing of the traversal is the root coordinate / Home scroll; the end hold sits on it. Relayed to the production coordinator same session.
- Direction (Will, 2026-11-19 01:17 CST, verbatim): "Choose coordinates that fit the lyrics in an Uncanny way" — each hop landing is chosen so its scroll’s content fits the lyric sounding at that moment (WAU-grade fit); every pick a real verified scroll, reported as lyric line + coordinate + the scroll’s first words so the fit is checkable. Relayed to the production coordinator same session.
- Direction (Will, 2026-11-19 01:17 CST, verbatim): "the key for this video is traversing the connections via zooms" — the film’s movement is continuous zoom-traversal along the shared-coordinate connections (the 9D/6D/3D relationship web as roads; zoom in through the levels, out, across a link, in again), not quick-nav jump cuts. The time hop reads as a zoom journey along a connection. Relayed to the production coordinator same session.
- Process gate (Will, 2026-11-19 01:17 CST, verbatim): "run a prepass at low-fidelity so I can audit before you render" — stage 1 = low-fi prepass of the full 4:20 traversal timed to the song, delivered to Will for audit; stage 2 = final render, only after Will’s audit/go. Relayed to the production coordinator same session.
- Direction (Will, 2026-11-19 01:33 CST): "the video can render tonight" and "I want to post this soon" — after the prepass audit, the final render runs the same night on Emise’s relay of his go, and the render is the post-ready master (Will intends to post it soon). Relayed to the production coordinator same session.
- Reprioritization (Will, 2026-11-19 01:46 CST, verbatim): "video prepass is less important than those" / "I can watch prepass in the morning" — the Scrollspace build queue has right of way over shared resources/data plane; the prepass is a by-morning deliverable; the 01:33 render-tonight authorization is superseded by the morning audit. Relayed to both coordinators same session.
- PREPASS DELIVERED (coordinator 94dd61f2, 2026-11-19 02:01 CST): ~/workspace/scrollspace/video/across-the-years-traversal-prepass.mp4 — 1280×720, H.264+AAC, 260.000 s exactly, 12,887,683 B, sha256 d765616d4aa47e1b2003e59dc390def495fbbc491f8335de9e0a71be950a4f9d (VM copy hash-verified vs hub). 6 s gap closed with a 3 s title card + ~4 s silent end hold on Home; song never time-stretched. Captured on pinned PR #76 client bytes against the real awsbox /source/human corpus (38 phexts); all travel via the client’s own animated zooms; cross-galaxy hops ride the shared home address 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 (verified held by 36 of 38 phexts). Shot list with lyric fits delivered to Will in the Sleep chat for his morning audit; five open audit questions (finale fetch beat, sparse descents, jump-box residue, speed ramps, final master spec 1080p / −1.5 dB ceiling). Data plane torn down, ports yielded to the build queue. Production state checkpointed in ~/workspace/scrollspace/video/STATE.md; hub assets in ~/scrollspace-video/.
- AUDIT ANSWERS (Will, 2026-11-19 02:06 CST): 1) Fix the finale fetch beat for the final — and WAIT FOR ALL FEATURES TO LAND before rendering (the final captures the finished client). 2) Tighten the sparse-descent timings — yes. 3) Jump-box residue — Will: "not sure what you mean"; Emise explained it in chat (the setup text left visible in the jump box during shots) and asked for a yes/no on clearing it — answer pending. 4) Transitions FAIRLY QUICK — demonstrate the speed of the solution (rebalance shot timings: quicker travel, more time standing on scrolls; total stays exactly 260 s). 5) Final master spec CONFIRMED: 1080p re-capture, audio ceiling −1.5 dB, exact 4:20, post-ready.
- Audit answer 3 settled (Will, 2026-11-19 02:07 CST): YES — clear the jump box after setup so the frame is clean. All five audit answers are now complete; the final render dispatches when the Scrollspace build queue finishes landing.
- FINAL RENDER (2026-11-19, gate cleared — whole Scrollspace queue landed): captured the finished client (phext-lattice exo d4476722, PR #91; page 115,594 B sha256 9b2dba76, pinned + verified in-script) at 1920x1080 via Playwright against a throwaway --local instance serving a scratch copy of the corpus (live corpus untouched, teardown-verified 38 phexts / 0 wal). All five audit answers applied: (1) finale fetch fixed — incipit endpoints pre-warmed before the hop, hop->plane ~0.23s, frame at 197s shows Home fully rendered, no fetching stall; (2) sparse descents tightened — two-rate pieces, emise travel 2.40x, artifacts travel 2.60x; (3) jump box cleared after every setup jump — QC frames show placeholder only; (4) fairly quick transitions — travel pieces 1.15–2.80x, recovered time in the stands, finale stand 30s natural under the 68s window; intro approach a deliberate 0.51x slow glide as briefed; (5) master spec — 1920x1080, exact 260.000s, audio ceiling -1.5 dB: song peak +0.55 dB PCM and AAC reconstruction overshoot up to +1.26 dB (ffmpeg alimiter unreliable, escaped to 0.0) — shipped chain is a deterministic lookahead limiter at PCM ceiling -2.60 dB (max GR -2.50 dB, mean -0.09 dB), decoded master peak measured -2.18 dB, no clipping, song never time-stretched. QC: black only 0–3s title + fade tail 259.28–259.96; landings frame-verified (Fire 0:40, Glass 1:25, Map 1:52, Bridge Read 3:00, Home 3:17/3:30 standing on 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1). Full record: ~/workspace/scrollspace/video/STATE.md.
- V1 MASTER DELIVERED 2026-11-19 08:56 CST (~/workspace/scrollspace/video/across-the-years-traversal.mp4, sha256 a0299f60…, 1080p, 260.000 s, decoded peak −2.18 dB). WILL’S REVIEW (2026-11-19 11:04 CST, verbatim): "moves too slowly through paths, not enough interaction yet, play the controls like descent". V2 direction: capture by actually FLYING the finished client with Will’s Descent control layout (F/A/W/E/S/D/Q/R + Z/X roll, wheel throttle, boost) via real input events — visible piloting: strafes, rolls, banking, targeting, casts, throttle work — not camera-on-rails glides. Transits materially faster than v1 (v1 assembly ran travel at 1.15–2.80x and still read slow); the felt pace is the spec. Keep: the audited shot list and lyric-fit landings, the stands where the song breathes, finale on 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1, exactly 260.00 s, 1920x1080, audio ceiling −1.5 dB (reuse v1’s limiter chain), clean frames. Deliver as across-the-years-traversal-v2.mp4 alongside v1 (v1 stays until Will approves v2 as the master).
- V2 DELIVERED 2026-11-19: ~/workspace/scrollspace/video/across-the-years-traversal-v2.mp4 (29,453,159 B, sha256 05e6ac43e38852dac244159d3a186579efc10eedce77cf43ed9cd2e5ce847224) — flown, not glided: the PR #91 client piloted with real input events only (Tab target locks re-confirmed against S.target, touch-drag aim, F/A/W/E + Shift boost + wheel-throttle key flight, Z/X rolls, strafe corrections, Enter/Backspace casts, real Read-panel clicks for the kinship hops, held-key plane walks; no evaluate-set camera, no script-called zooms/jumps). 1920x1080, exactly 260.000 s, decoded audio peak -2.18 dB via v1's limiter chain, no black spans, frame checks pass at every lyric landing and mid-transit. Full record: ~/workspace/scrollspace/video/STATE.md (V2 DELIVERED section). Status stays OPEN — Will's approval of v2 closes the task; v1 remains the master until then.
- V3 DIRECTION (Will, 2026-11-19 20:47 CST, verbatim): "key feedback for scrollspace voyage v3 — traverse the exocortex like riding waves on a hidden ocean; bob + weave - move naturally, like a human playing descent; add a small pod that travels the multiverse; whenever we land on a scroll, don’t linger too long - just long enough to spark interest; if there’s a phext hyperlink present, follow it; return again and again to CYOA; follow paths I actually followed while posting - look at the commit history; include artistic QR codes so viewers can jump right to the commit that spawned the scroll being shown, or the edit.phext.io page for it; apply YC-scale polish; final draft will be 60 fps rendered down to 24 fps film grain; prepass is 15 fps for speed, low res - just so I can see the shape". PLAN: prepass first (15 fps, low res, full shape, audit gate — final render only after Will’s audit). Route mined from wbic16/human@exo commit history (Will’s real posting paths), CYOA as the recurring home port, phext hyperlinks followed where present, landings brief. Final master (after audit): 60 fps capture rendered down to 24 fps with film grain, 260 s, Across the Years, audio ceiling −1.5 dB.
- V3 VOYAGE PREPASS DELIVERED 2026-11-19 21:50 CST (resume coordinator; first coordinator’s mining + prep verified and completed): ~/workspace/scrollspace/video/across-the-years-voyage-v3-prepass.mp4 — H.264 960x540 @15fps + AAC, 22,543,982 B, sha256 19d088cd4bdf8b3b1310f3f1eb1bcf9a2ea43a31980763637f95c55d3a855793; audio exactly 260.000 s, video 260.067 s (one frame over, stated plainly). Route mined from wbic16/human@exo history (libphext 0.6.4 reference parser; spawning commits exact for all 358,693 HEAD scrolls): 18 landings flown, 9 in CYOA (returns at orders 1,2,3,5,9,10,12,15,17), 4 hyperlink legs (s02 textual; s13/s16/s19 kinship by real Read-panel clicks), brief ~5 s stands, wave-riding flight (burnWave swell: sine throttle, weave/bob taps, boost crests; real input events only), capture-only pod mod verified in frame in transit and parked. All 19 artistic QRs decode-verified at generation and again from source; one QR cropped from a finished film frame decodes to its spawning commit. RESUME REPAIR (plainly): the mined finale stops at 1000.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 (“The Ten Commandments of AGI”, commit 10c0aae0) exist at human@exo HEAD but NOT in the hosted edit.phext.io corpus — re-routed through the same burst’s surviving hosted coordinates (CYOA home return + kinship hop to Incipit home). Capture wedged twice on unbounded CDP awaits under renderer saturation; fixed capture-build-only with bounded input primitives; segF re-flown clean after a cast-press timeout fix. Data plane torn down; live corpus verified untouched (38 phexts, 0 WAL); production untouched. Full record: ~/workspace/scrollspace/video/STATE.md (V3 section) + v3/MINING.md. Task stays OPEN at Will’s audit gate; the final render (60 fps -> 24 fps film grain) is NOT in scope until he audits.
- CORPUS SYNCED 2026-11-19 21:57 CST (task 28.8.9): the Ten Commandments scrolls now exist in the hosted corpus, so the v3 FINAL render can fly the original mined finale (s17/s18: CYOA + incipit at 1000.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1, spawn 10c0aae0) instead of the prepass re-route. The final still waits on Will’s prepass audit.
# Phext homes + agi.git collection and nightly unified merge

Coordinate: 29.6.11/8.7.11/7.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-06 20:10 CST
Request (verbatim): emise.phext is your personal journal - it stays in emise-tools; wavefront.phext belongs in human, as do CYOA, Incipit, and the canonical copy; feel free to push emise.phext to human.git daily. These should all be collected and managed in agi.git: skills.phext, tasks.phext, neuralese.phext, research.phext, state.phext, lessons.phext. Every night, merge all of those into a unified agi.phext — you may have to encode merge-rules to avoid problems or merge conflicts — that's the point. Run this process now. (Addendum 20:11: pull in a copy of wbic16/singular's singular.phext to use as a spine for agi.phext.)
Status: completed — process run; nightly job armed

