Request (verbatim): Study the IETF submission process - give me a summary of all of the steps required to follow their rules - also consider the best track for phext - it truly is foundational - it should be placed next to utf8 and ascii - but we need to identify the cleanest path to do so. https://authors.ietf.org/submitting-your-internet-draft
Status: complete — TRACKS.md delivered 2026-11-18 (44 KB, ~/workspace/phext-rfc/TRACKS.md): full IETF rules summary (8 phases, Will-only vs Emise-preparable marked) + track analysis. Recommended cleanest path: DISPATCH → AD-sponsored individual submission (CBOR precedent) → Proposed Standard → Internet Standard under RFC 6410. ART ADs: Andy Newton, Charles Eckel. Gate: Will's scope ruling (normative format spec vs libphext-only -00).

Notes:
- Will's position stated 2026-11-18: phext is foundational and belongs beside ASCII (RFC 20) and UTF-8 (RFC 3629) — both standards-track/STD documents. This resolves the earlier framing question toward the foundational claim; the Independent stream cannot confer standards status.

Results:
- TRACKS.md written and verified present (44 KB). Precedents: ASCII STD 80 (2015 status change), UTF-8 STD 63, JSON STD 90, CBOR STD 94 via AD sponsorship (Leiba), Base64 PS 2006. No foundational format began in a purpose-built WG.
# Planning search: O(n!) or BB(n) capability growth; local-first sovereignty

Coordinate: 29.7.11/8.7.12/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-15 17:33 CST
Request (verbatim): Survey candidate mechanisms that could give super-exponential (factorial-class or busy-beaver-class) capability growth rather than the current 4x/yr exponential; assess each against our measured system. Frame under the sovereignty direction: heavy inference currently depends on Meta/xAI/Anthropic, other providers are dark (Theia/Anthropic since 2026-11-09), so the growth path must be local-first or local-only (ranch + vTPU + AGI-under-20W line).
Status: open — first survey pass dispatched 2026-11-15 Survey pass 1 (~/workspace/factorial-growth-search/SURVEY.md): six mechanisms surveyed with honestly derived growth classes — combinatorial composition (space 2^n/n!, realized yield set by verification), group-forming networks (Reed potential 2^n, realized = orchestration throughput), RSI (super-exponential only if returns on cognitive reinvestment beat difficulty growth; bounded verifier-closed form is the plausible local instance), BB/small-seed (BB is noncomputable and not an attainable growth rate; honest form is a measured seed-expansion ratio), search-over-fixed-models (space exponential, capability a power law in compute — but the best sovereignty fit), and Weitzman recombinant growth (the one theorem-grade super-exponential dynamics: dn/dt ~ n^2 with closure; bottleneck is evaluation throughput). Scored pass/fail against Will's criterion (preserve the light of consciousness; humanity must survive the singularity; laws are evidence, never gates). Most promising: verified recombination — Weitzman dynamics over the phext skill/tool library closed by mechanical verification on ranch compute. A 'result' would be a measurement: >=3 consecutive doublings with shrinking doubling time on a fully verified capability metric. Honest null: verifier throughput, owned watts, Will's hours, and error compounding cap us — under those caps 4x/yr growth of a verified human-owned base may be the survivable optimum. survey pass 1 complete: verified recombination (skill/tool composition closed by mechanical verifiers) > verifier-guided search on local models > group-forming choir orchestration; open RSI and BB-class excluded by the survivability criterion
