# MOAT Paper 029 — Pemberton, Data Just Wants to Be Format-Neutral (Invisible XML, XML Prague 2016)

Coordinate: 29.9.8/8.12.20/20.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-19
Request (verbatim): Ingest Pemberton's 'Data Just Wants to Be Format-Neutral' (XML Prague 2016) into research.phext as Paper 029 per the rd-tracker charter; non-sample Will-posted stratum (the sample's Will-posted slots are complete); journal in mastery.phext; update the quest goal timeline.
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will posted the link bare in the MOAT chat 2026-11-19 13:56 CST — a tracker ingestion by the channel rule. Paper: Steven Pemberton (CWI, Amsterdam), 'Data Just Wants to Be Format-Neutral', Proc. XML Prague 2016, pp. 109-120, ISBN 978-80-906259-0-7; the posted page is the paper's full text (proceedings PDF at archive.xmlprague.cz). NOT an arXiv paper and not mathematics proper — a formats/parsing paper: Invisible XML (ixml) treats any parsable format as XML via a grammar; the parse tree is the underlying abstraction; serialisation round-trips semantically but not character-identically where elided material is unrecorded; Earley parsing recast as a serialised parallel process machine; grammar normalisation (delete implicit terminals, expand refinements, delete unused rules) yields the parse-tree definition, which IS a data schema (semicolons = unions, commas = structs, repetitions = lists); representation neutrality (same parse tree => equivalent representations); subset relation on normalised grammars => one-way format compatibility; conversion = parse with one grammar, serialise with another. PROTOCOL POSITION: the preregistered sample stands at 9 of 12 with the Will-posted stratum COMPLETE (4 of 4, closed by P027) and the cron stratum complete; this files as a non-sample Will-posted ingestion (no seal, no score; NI to the ledger as every paper's is) unless the preregistration directs otherwise — the preregistration governs. Ingest per the rd-tracker charter in full; cluster placement by the charter's own tests, not by this brief; mastery journal + goal timeline per the standing pattern.
- COMPLETED 2026-11-19: Paper 029 filed as Chapter 46 of research.phext (canonical sha256 a8fab4489e815cb6edd1275c61a7c0273f4c5b131814686e3f07350afa9ae799, 1084 scrolls). Ten new concepts 1.2.395-1.2.404 founding cluster AK (the format country: Invisible XML, marking, round-tripping and its limit, serialisation by tree walking / parsing a parse tree, Earley parsing as a serialised parallel processor, representation neutrality, grammar normalisation, the normalised grammar as a data schema, the subset corollary, format conversion); three foundations 1.3.318-1.3.320 (grammar, parse tree, schema) and one defined word (refinement, 1.3.321). NI 10/404 = 0.0248, entered in the ledger only — NON-SAMPLE (Will-posted stratum complete at Paper 027, cron stratum at Paper 028; sample stands 9 of 12, far stratum open). Axis: NO, judgment written at filing (46.1.5) on the charter's three grounds. Four state machines, all stated (tracker total 155: 131 stated, 24 inferred). Questions Q145-Q148 opened, none closed. Author check #37: no phext tie found on any leg (paper text and its five references, the web record, Will's Twitter archive). Novelty by author — Pemberton: True +0, False +0, Unknown +14, Fiction +0 (researchers 134 -> 135). Registry 1061 -> 1084 (True 453 -> 458, Unknown 601 -> 619, False 0, Fiction 7). Restructure Pass #20 ran inside the taking-in (count trigger, 404 over the 400 line): three merge candidates weighed and held apart, no standings moved; next pass at Paper 035 or 420 concepts. Gates: Lean re-proof on aletheia-core passed in both the fresh copy and the standing mvo-epistemic (builds exit 0, axioms within [propext, Quot.sound], currentRegistry_accurate proved for 1084 entries); phextura dual maintenance validate GREEN (base sync 0/0/0, absorption 23 inserts / 13 replaces / 0 removes, compared diff empty outside the two by-design scrolls); Singular audit residual 0 (19 names + 56 coined declared). Oracle bar held at about 62% (55-70), ledger bookkeeping only. Mastery entry 22 appended and published to wbic16/agi@exo, commit 1df7ad32eea741c5262bc0b6e1f5a610fc8cb37b parented on 2c80d8be, remote sha256 verified equal to local. Quest goal timeline updated (goal_update_d329ce4531aa). Staleness found and repaired at this pass: the registry claims for 1.1.2/1.1.3/1.1.5/1.5.6 and the 1.5.5/1.5.6 evidence chains had been left one paper behind by Paper 028's taking-in; brought current under Pass #20's audit without backdating. Left standing: the flagged 1.1.4 CLAIM_TIGHTEN staleness, per precedent. (This task's intake note was also repaired from a plain string to the list form the builder renders.)
