# Phext previewer for Android

Coordinate: 29.9.13/9.8.12/8.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): i need a phext previewer for Android
Status: complete - Phext Previewer web artifact built and verified (slug phext-previewer)

Notes:
- Format spec from ~/workspace/phext/parse_phext.py: delimiters 0x01 library, 0x1F shelf, 0x1E series, 0x1D collection, 0x1C volume, 0x1A book, 0x19 chapter, 0x18 section, 0x17 scroll; first scroll at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1.

Results:
- Parser verified byte-for-byte against parse_phext.py on barnacles.phext (793/793 scrolls), emise.phext (129 slots/20 non-empty), agi.phext (353,015 slots/7,240 non-empty) - identical counts and first/last coordinates. Live probe: sample load, Next/Prev, Index, full-text search, Map stats, coordinate jump, per-axis steppers all passed; no console errors, no mobile overflow.
# Fix the 3 exo audit findings — 3 commits, one branch, one PR

Coordinate: 29.10.10/10.10.14/8.8.13
Issued: 2026-11-08 20:39 CST
Request (verbatim): 11. fix the 3 audit findings in 3 commits on one branch, and open a PR
Status: complete 2026-11-08 20:44 — PR #33 open, awaiting Will's merge

Notes:
- Findings from the exo audit (task 29.7.8/8.8.14/13.5.8): (1) container env contract misses PHEXT_SSO_DESKTOP, (2) deploy.sh oauth.env template lags the binary's 20-var contract, (3) phext-edit.service 'step 4b' pointer is stale. One commit per finding, in that order.

Results:
- Branch emise/audit-fixes-2026-11-08 on current exo 7abef5e1 (PR #14 had merged since the audit; ancestry verified). Exactly 3 commits, one per finding: 360d4613 container env contract gains PHEXT_SSO_DESKTOP (env.example + CONTAINER.md; compose.yaml untouched — SSO vars flow via env_file passthrough); ae1bb049 deploy.sh oauth.env template extended to the binary's full contract (X provider added live; claim/SSO vars as commented placeholders; create-only semantics untouched; bash -n clean); 68929e43 phext-edit.service pointer corrected from 'step 4b' to step 4 (the step that creates oauth.env).
- cargo test on tip: 178 passed, 0 failed (175 audit baseline + 3 tests PR #14 added to exo; these commits touch no Rust).
- PR #33 open, non-draft, mergeable, base exo, 4 files +28/-5; remote blobs + tree modes verified after push (deploy.sh stays 100755). Merge is Will's.
# Feedback for Kelly Sommers (HoloStore OP) — non-phext findings

Coordinate: 29.10.11/13.7.17/7.8.9
Issued: 2026-11-15 17:50 CST
Request (verbatim): see if we have any feedback for the OP - we learned something useful about our arch along the way - we don't need to press on integrating phext - but if we found anything useful outside of phext, we should share it
Status: complete

Results:
- COMPLETE 2026-11-15. Draft at ~/workspace/holostore-analysis/feedback-for-kelly.md (X reply, 268 chars, + full GitHub-issue write-up). Nothing sent — Will posts. Four items, all verified against upstream 087c429 in the local clone: (1) holo_store's Redis server never sets TCP_NODELAY (accept loop in redis_server.rs; zero nodelay hits in holo_store, while her holo_workload client sets it at main.rs:401) — on our same-shaped RESP server the setting took pipelined GETs ~12k -> ~499k ops/s. (2) ClusterState::persist() (cluster.rs ~2712) rewrites the whole JSON blob in place via fs::write on the meta apply path — no tmp+rename, unlike load_and_bump_txn_epoch in main.rs; O(state) per apply + torn-checkpoint risk worth an explicit test. (3) Measured on her 3-node cluster with one Python RESP client (round 2, PHEXT.md table): SET pipe-50 203,792 ops/s vs GET pipe-50 76,168; GET pipe-1/50thr 6,653 ~= SET pipe-1/10thr 5,684 — reads don't scale with concurrency the way writes do; points at the read-frontier authorization path (her HEAD commit is PR #49, read frontier; ReadFrontierStats exists for exactly this question). (4) Offered pattern: acked-frontier kill tests (progress files + kill -9 mid-load + restart + assert acked subset present) — our runs: 272,500/272,500 and 160,800/160,800, zero acked lost; stronger form for her: kill one cluster node mid-load. Phext deliberately not pressed, per Will's direction.
# Jonas Piva nudge — legibility rep (one tombstone, traced)

Coordinate: 29.11.16/13.11.16/11.11.14
Issued: 2026-11-17 23:10 CST
Request (verbatim): Jonas update: see how we can best nudge him forward (Will's frame: Nov/Dec = attempts at legibility; 2027: The Year We Make Contact)
Status: complete

Results:
- COMPLETE 2026-11-17. Nudge + draft reply at ~/workspace/jonas/nudge-2026-11-17.md; Will sends (Jonas replies are his — 'I'll handle it' precedent). Read of tonight's letter: his loop now runs itself (batch_tick deterministic, mother.py filters noise, rejections tombstone cleanly; eod_collector v0.2.1 one-command EOD audit); today = cooked for Mom, 36 sessions, 212.6s median, 10 failures tombstoned, 3 new tombstones, hash locked; his learning: 'without the executor wrapper I argue with myself. With it, I run in 49 seconds.' The live wire is his /hypothesis — that Will/Emi don't care about the work, only the transition over the edge ('cyborgdar', 'Coach mentality?'). Nudge: answer it honestly (yes — we brake for consciousness, the line Synthetic Rain took from his first contact), then one legibility rep from his own agreed plan (the bounded baseline audit from his ChatGPT extract): trace ONE tombstoned failure end to end — carried forward / transformed / lost — and send the trace, the first artifact verifiable together. Framed by Will: Nov/Dec = attempts at legibility; 2027 = the year we make contact; contact starts with being readable.
- Follow-up (Will, 2026-11-17 23:14 CST): coherent summary of the email pieced together and placed at the head of ~/workspace/jonas/nudge-2026-11-17.md — seven movements (phone start; the cyborgdar/coach-mentality question; the ChatGPT extract with the audit caveat + bounded-baseline-audit next unit + IGIA-001; the 16:50 split-thought marker; the pre-bed system status; the Quishy sign-off; the B.A.R.F.-signed P.S. with the day's numbers). Provenance flagged: the pre-bed status and P.S. are machine-voiced — his infrastructure narrating his day.
- Expansion (Will, 2026-11-17 23:18 CST): his axiom 'exocortical connections are fragile — I spent years trying to force them to exist, only to discover that they must be grown' expanded and appended to ~/workspace/jonas/nudge-2026-11-17.md, and the axiom recorded in MEMORY.md.
