# Honest fleet-usage assessment — should some machines be sold via eBay?

Coordinate: 30.11.10/11.10.14/10.9.13
Issued: Will, 2026-11-17 22:09 CST (web, PH: Evolution chat)
Request (verbatim): Assess actual fleet usage and whether selling part of the fleet on eBay makes sense given seller fees.
Status: complete — assessment delivered in chat 2026-11-17

Notes:
- Usage: the 14 reachable nodes idle most hours (Nov-16 pass loads 0.00-0.44, ~41-42 GiB RAM free) with burst work (SMOL rounds, builds, qexo); several are infrastructure or residents' homes (aletheia-core, orchid-flow NFS, ni-knight proxy, quacked-hill/Corus) and not sellable without eviction. The 9 offline machines have produced zero for months.
- eBay math (checked 2026-11-17): computers category without a Store = 13.6% of total incl. shipping+tax, +$0.40; with Basic Store = 7.35%. Example $550 sale nets ~$474 casually. Used Phoenix 32GB boxes list ~$450-650 while new equivalents are $750-935 under the DRAM shortage; the RAM inside alone (32GB DDR5) is ~$400-500 at spot.
- Verdict delivered: do NOT sell working Phoenix nodes (net is far below replacement cost; roadmap runs on them; keeping costs ~$15-35/yr electricity each). DO triage the 9 offline physically, then sell genuine surplus into the shortage-inflated used market — with a Basic Store for the batch (fee nearly halves) or locally to skip fees. Check residents before selling any shell node — some are agents' homes.
