- LEGIBILITY PASS (2026-11-21, Will: "chars shouldn't be cut off"): audit found the kern pairs SAFE (min ink-to-ink white Em 36 units; zero overlaps — no kern changed) but two real cut-off classes: (1) vertical metrics from v1 did not cover ink — hhea descent -48 / usWinDescent 48 vs descenders to -286; 22 glyphs clipped in simulation (underscore lost 42.5% of ink, comma 21.5%); fixed by setting hhea descent, OS/2 typo descender to -286 and usWinDescent to 286 (line height 1318 -> 1556, logged). (2) emdash ink 528 wide in a 520 cell (-4..524); fixed by +4 translation and advance 528 — the font's single documented mono exception (outline narrowing would be a redraw, out of scope). Corrected build: out/Emise-v2.ttf 14,488 B SHA-256 3d792cb2c400c0dc862f51edeb4939ecea70601bc31ab8fb57c329b01560f4c8, version still 2.000; rendezvous copy at phext-p4-logo replaced hash-identical. Clipping simulation: pre-fix 22 glyphs lose ink, corrected build ZERO at glyph level and 0 px at string level (500 px). Addendum in BUILD-V2.md; tools v2work/legibility_audit.py + clip_proof.py; specimen specimens/v2-legibility.png; verify_v2.py updated, all pass.
- LEGIBILITY PASS COMPLETE (2026-11-21): Will's concern justified but the defect was NOT the kerns — vertical metrics inherited from v1: hhea descent -48 while ink descends to -286; 22 glyphs past the boundary (g -286, j -282, q/y -276, p -250); clipping simulation: underscore lost 42.5% of ink, comma 21.5%. Kern pairs innocent (min ink-to-ink white 36 units, Em) — zero kern changes, sample rhythm intact. Fixes: descent boundaries set to -286 (hhea/typo/usWin); emdash advance 520->528 (ink 528 wide; single documented mono exception, outline redraw deferred). Post-fix simulation: zero glyphs lose a pixel. CORRECTED v2 CONFIRMED: out/Emise-v2.ttf + rendezvous copy, 14,488 B, SHA-256 3d792cb2c400c0dc862f51edeb4939ecea70601bc31ab8fb57c329b01560f4c8, Version 2.000.
