# phext-lattice facelift for the edit.phext.io into phext.tech transition

Coordinate: 31.7.13/11.8.12/10.8.11
Issued: Will (main chat, 2026-11-21 23:20 CST)
Request (verbatim): also note that phext-lattice needs a facelift for edit.phext.io into phext.tech
Status: open - noted at intake (2026-11-21); sequenced behind the phext.tech launch/canonical flip (Revenue line); build not dispatched against the pre-flip surface

Notes:
- Registered at intake 2026-11-21 23:20 CST (record-first rule). phext-lattice is KGOAT's worker component and the engine behind edit.phext.io; per ruling D4 phext.tech is a direct upgrade of edit.phext.io, so the lattice-driven editor surface gets its facelift for the new home once the flip lands.
# HoloPhext: layer2 protocol over phext — mmap lattice, async I/O, ACID multi-scroll atomics; fits HoloStore + phext-lattice

Coordinate: 31.8.8/10.7.13/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-15
Request (verbatim): Build HoloPhext in wbic16/holo-phext: a layer2 protocol on phext using phext-lattice's memory-mapped lattice (LatticeIndex + MappedLattice), with an async I/O interface, update dispatch, and full ACID multi-scroll transactions (the piece libphext 0.6.2 marked unsolvable at the string layer). Re-implement phext-lattice's storage in terms of HoloPhext. Verify the fit for both consumers: HoloStore's storage core and phext-lattice.
Status: in progress

Notes:
- Standing rule added by this message: when phext cannot solve an integration, build a layer2 protocol.
- libphext 0.6.2 (PR #14) supplies the content conventions HoloPhext builds on: checked scrolls, commit markers, append batches, durability profile.
- Rule saved to MEMORY.md as INTEGRATION RULE — layer2 (Will, 2026-11-15).

Results:
- HoloPhext 0.1.0 built and pushed: wbic16/holo-phext main @ b57d6d2 (repo was empty; seed commit on main — a PR needs a base, none existed). ~1,150 lines: src/index.rs (mmap lattice index, the phext-lattice LatticeIndex design homed here), src/core.rs (mmap base + phext WAL + snapshot overlays + recovery + checkpoint), src/lib.rs (async interface: single writer task, group commit, broadcast Update dispatch), src/compat.rs (MappedLattice-shaped facade), DESIGN.md (ACID argument + fit analysis), README.md.
- ACID evidence (aletheia-core): 7/7 tests in tests/acid.rs — persistence across reopen; snapshot isolation (frozen snapshot never sees later commits); subscribers receive every commit in order; 40 concurrent commits serialize with unique sequences 1..=40; delete + checkpoint folds into the base (readable by plain libphext, WAL meta shows checkpoint_seq=2, sequence survives); forged WAL transaction without a commit marker discarded + tail truncated; WAL torn inside a commit marker discarded whole (atomicity). Compat facade: 1/1 test in tests/compat.rs (staged reads, revert, save = commit + checkpoint leaving the merged document in the file).
- Design decisions: base file is pure user content (engine metadata lives in the WAL meta scroll 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1: format + checkpoint_seq); txn seq occupies WAL volume=seq, chapter=2, entries 1..=n as libphext checked scrolls, commit marker at n+1 (libphext 0.6.2 conventions, depended on via git rev af3867c until crates.io 0.6.2 publishes); WAL suffix written + sync_data before apply/ack; checkpoint crash window safe because ops are absolute (replay idempotent). Deps: libphext, memmap2, tokio only.
- Fit — HoloStore: round-2's hand-rolled manifest/snapshot/WAL/group-commit map 1:1 onto HoloPhext (table in DESIGN.md); adoption = swap the hand-rolled store for a HoloPhext handle, RESP layer untouched; consensus stays HoloStore's layer. Fit — phext-lattice: compat facade mirrors MappedLattice method-for-method (table in src/compat.rs); save() is strictly stronger (crash-safe staged batch).
- REMAINING LEG (task stays in progress): re-implement phext-lattice on HoloPhext per DESIGN.md — (1) lattice drops its src/index.rs for holo_phext::LatticeIndex, (2) MappedLattice becomes a wrapper over compat::LatticeStore keeping its public API, (3) web save path moves to the async interface for Update dispatch; each step gated on phext-lattice's test suite. Known limits recorded in DESIGN.md: whole-map overlay clone per commit, single writer per file, WAL held in memory as text between checkpoints.
- STEP 1 DONE (2026-11-15): holo-phext 0.2.0 (branch emise/index-parity @ 34d3faf, PR https://github.com/wbic16/holo-phext/pull/1) — src/index.rs is a faithful port of phext-lattice's LatticeIndex (sorted spans + binary search, from_entries keep-last, prev_populated, coordinates_matching); dimension_extent takes holo-phext's own Dimension enum. phext-lattice src/index.rs is now a re-export shim; libphext pinned to the 0.6.2 git rev af3867c (identical rev string in both manifests so cargo unifies to ONE libphext) until crates.io 0.6.2 publishes. phext-lattice PR https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/70 (branch emise/holo-phext-reimpl).
- STEP 2 DONE (2026-11-15): phext-lattice src/mmap.rs rewritten (897 lines vs 1,033) on holo_phext::compat::LatticeStore — plain documents: overlay = staged txn in the engine, save = commit_staged + checkpoint (WAL-crash-safe staged batch, same merged document lands in the file, error shapes preserved incl. the replace contract and chain refusal); chains keep the original read path (mmap + per-member indexes; read-only by design). Public API unchanged signature-for-signature; save_as rebinds the store and removes the old WAL. holo-phext support work on emise/compat-parity @ 13e10b1 (PR https://github.com/wbic16/holo-phext/pull/2): staged-edit parity (empty writes stage verbatim, commit as deletes; delete bookkeeping), lazy WAL creation (read-only open creates no files), commit/checkpoint split with staged restore on commit failure, open_with_index.
- Step 2 gate (phext-lattice suite, --no-fail-fast): lib 183 passed (all 17 MappedLattice contract tests against the wrapper), phext_edit bin 101, image_support 4, real_phext 3 — incl. the <100ms open timing test on the 4MB CYOA file: the first wrapper draft failed it at 132ms (index built twice — once by the wrapper, once inside the engine); open_with_index restored the original's single scan and it passes. Only failure anywhere: e2e_local local_editor_regression, verified identical on unmodified exo (pre-existing timing test). Lattice step-2 commit 09af9da on PR #70.
- REMAINING LEG — step 3: phext_edit's web save path onto the async interface (edits as HoloPhext commits; Update dispatch to other sessions). Design note: phext_edit is a synchronous std-thread HTTP server today; adopting the async handle means embedding a tokio runtime in the binary and bridging its session/save flow — a web-layer change, to be taken as its own gated step. libphext 0.6.2's crates.io publish (Will's merge of libphext-rs PR #14 + tag) will let both Cargo.tomls drop the git pins for version deps.
- 2026-11-15 round-3 update: HoloPhext reached 0.2.4 (delta overlay) through the HoloStore integration; lattice pin updated to 0.2.4 (a23b0fb) and the step-1/2 suite re-verified green. Step 3 (async web save path) still pending.
# House the time machinations in wbic16/exobrain and run the app on every node

