Status: complete 2026-11-08 22:24 — all six PRs merged; final exo tip a02e0e1b; one follow-up (demo copy wording) dispatched separately

Notes:
- Verified live before dispatch: exo tip 9149600b = merge of #12, on top of #34 (d8e0e6e) and #33 merges; #12's tab-title + picker-link tweaks are in the log. Remaining unmerged: #4, #6, #7 (SKIP - ad funnel, leave open), #8, #9 (HOLD - integration branch containing #7's stack), #13, #31, #32. Merge order per Grok (minus #12, done by Will): #8, #6, #4, #31, #13, #32. Constraints: target exo only, never main; no new PRs; no direct pushes to exo/main; branch updates via --force-with-lease with backup branches; rebase the rest after each merge. Grok's handoff text is in Will's 2026-11-08 21:47 message in this chat.

Results:
- ALL SIX MERGED into exo, chain: 9149600 start -> #6 9e8897b -> #4 a4e1cb0 -> #8 b5d0588 -> #31 b20878e -> #13 6f4ec77 -> #32 a02e0e1 (final tip). Full suite at tip: 235 passed, 0 failed (independently re-verified by Emise: tip + merge chain read from the remote). Baseline correction: the real pre-program baseline was 211, not the 178 in Emise's brief; floor rose per merge to 235.
- Step 0 (#12 re-check): no defects — tab title and picker/search link styling match spec and sit clean with #34. Per-PR: backup branches pushed at every original head; conflicts resolved under Grok's guidance (#34's five fixes, #12 anchors, mmap/save invariants all preserved; #31 deploy files resolved as unions of #33 + sponsor bits; deploy.sh has zero --token; no new crates). #8's paintProviders preserve-and-prove satisfied: static anchors + session-driven hiding + ?next= winner logic intact, hrefs absolutized.
- #7 and #9 NOT touched — verified at the end via API: both open, heads byte-identical to start (a90c4048, c6a9a322). No direct pushes to exo/main (repo has no main); no new PRs opened by the program. Full record: ~/workspace/merge-wrapup-2026-11-08/REPORT.md. Coordinator disclosed two process incidents (a discarded pre-push rebase fumble in #8's cycle; a stale-build race in #4) — neither reached the remote.
- CASUALTY: #8 merged ~22:15 with the copy fix worded 'Signing in with Google, GitHub, or X opens the real editor'; Will's superseding wording ('Signing in enables the editor') arrived 22:16, after the merge. Follow-up one-line PR dispatched 22:2x (emise/demo-copy-signing-in).
- COPY FOLLOW-UP MERGED BY WILL (2026-11-08 22:38): PR #35 (branch emise/demo-copy-signing-in, one commit c093fc7, one line: 'Signing in enables the editor: ...') merged — exo tip now 3f88c5d. Open PRs remaining: #7 and #9 only, both parked under Will's earlier skip/hold rulings; their disposition is the last open question of the launch program.
