# Console Stage 1 — shell, edit.phext.io SSO, capability registry, first live panels

Coordinate: 33.5.5/5.4.7/5.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (verbatim): Stage 1 of the executive console (program task 43.2.3/2.2.8/2.3.5): (1) establish phext-lattice's real auth surface from the fresh exo tree (the local lattice checkout is stale) and design the desktop SSO flow against what exists — authorization code + PKCE with a loopback redirect, token stored in the OS credential store; any gap in lattice's OAuth for desktop clients is reported as a finding, never hacked around with password capture; (2) Tauri 2 shell scaffold with the SSO sign-in working end-to-end against the real edit.phext.io; (3) the phext capability registry (format + seed from skills.phext and the live services) rendered in the shell; (4) first live panels reading real data — tasks register, Waiting-on-Will, fleet status — each from its best live source, the source named on the panel; (5) establish the Windows 11 build path (where the .msi/.exe gets built) and report its state honestly.
Status: open

Notes:
- Directed by Will in the MOAT chat, 2026-11-21 09:47 CST. Stage order is the house rule: one stage at a time, in order.
- Dark mode per standing rule (OS preference default, explicit override persisted).
- STRUCK by Will's 2026-11-21 09:52 CST redirect: the 'best live source, labelled' panel plan — specifically panels reading the rendered waiting-on-will.md, the perpetual dashboard's data path, or raw register files. Those are human slop as data sources. Stage 1's primary deliverable is now the lattice-as-driver SPEC: what phext-lattice must expose for the console (auth/SSO, registry hosting, register data services, dispatch bridge, status feed, view/act token scopes), each struck slop surface mapped to its lattice replacement. Shell work re-scopes to the spec: SSO + registry served via lattice; panels only against specced lattice endpoints.
- Tauri scaffolding STOPPED per Will's veto (2026-11-21 09:55 CST). Stage 1 continues on the SPEC as its deliverable; the shell leg is held until Will names the stack.
- DEFINED by Will, 2026-11-21 09:56 CST: 'human slop meaning anything with a massive dependency chain — everything we build has to be rooted in the exocortical lineage that is phext-aware.' The console (shell included) must be buildable from the exocortical lineage — phext, libphext, phcc, SQ, phext-lattice, house tooling — with dependency chains we own and can enumerate. The SPEC gains a dependency-lineage section: every proposed component carries its enumerated chain; anything dragging a massive foreign chain is struck. The shell stack is not chosen from foreign frameworks; the spec states what a lineage-rooted shell requires and the vehicle remains Will's to name.
- Stage 1 executed 2026-11-21 under three Will rulings mid-flight: the lattice-as-driver redirect (09:52), the Tauri veto (09:55), and the human-slop definition (09:56). Deliverable is the SPEC: ~/workspace/executive-console/SPEC.md (ARCHITECTURE.md points at it). Tauri scaffold and the reqwest/keyring spike core were removed to recoverable trash; no Tauri artifacts are part of the deliverable.
- Auth verdict: lattice already implements the desktop SSO audience in code (wbic16/phext-lattice@exo 2ba5710f, src/oauth.rs; 54 oauth tests passed on aletheia-core incl. desktop exchange). Flow: system browser -> GET /api/auth/sso/desktop (loopback literal + state nonce) -> sealed single-use assertion -> POST /api/auth/desktop/exchange -> {session, csrf} sealed 14-day session for the OS credential store. No client registration, no refresh token, editor-list gate. LIVE GAP: the deployed edit.phext.io returns 404 for the desktop audience — PHEXT_SSO_DESKTOP is not set in deployment (SPEC R-A1, operations, no code). Web SSO audiences live-verified 302 the same pass; /api/session live-verified.
- Registry: format + seed built as the spec's fixture (~/workspace/executive-console/registry/capabilities.phext, 21 scrolls = Home + 20 capabilities, builder --check CURRENT); inscription-appears demonstrated against the fixture (20 -> 21). Lattice serving it is SPEC R-R1; until then any shell consumes the fixture, marked as such.
- Shell HELD pending Will's stack ruling (veto + lineage rule). SPEC §6 lineage audit: lattice's own chain verified clean (libphext 0.6.4 + holo-phext + ~13 small leaves, std TcpListener server, no framework). Console-side gaps: G-L1 lineage HTTP/TLS client, G-L2 thin Credential Manager binding, G-L3 window/text surface (vehicle Will's to name).
- Stage stays OPEN: shell held, R-A1 is an operator step, and the SPEC's lattice stages L1-L5 are follow-on work (candidates named on program task 43.2.3/2.2.8/2.3.5).
- Homes ruled by Will 2026-11-21: working set (SPEC, registry fixture, architecture) publishes to wbic16/gaia; tooling builds (the G-L gaps) go to wbic16/phextron. Auth ruling: desktop SSO for humans, MCP Auth for agents — no convergence work.
