Notes:
- Handle as written by Will: '@madeofmistake'; the cast/people record is @madeofmistak3 — same person, Will's loose spelling, do not 'correct' his message in any outward artifact.
- Scope widened by Will 2026-11-08 16:25 (verbatim): 'just remove the old token auth - it was added before any of the oauth login methods'. Removal is now end-to-end for the LOGIN token auth (UI box + server-side verification + routes/middleware solely serving it); OAuth flows untouched and re-verified. Boundary: token machinery serving other purposes (API keys, SQ/session internals, SSO secrets) is preserved and named in the report.

Results:
- Old token auth removed end-to-end: branch emise/remove-token-auth @ 260e0e5e, parented on exo eb450bcd, 48 remote blobs + tree modes verified post-push. Emise spot-check: zero auth-input/phext-token/PHEXT_TOKEN leftovers in the shipped tree.
- What it was: #auth-screen's #auth-input took the server's one static bearer token (--token/PHEXT_TOKEN, minted by deploy.sh), stored in localStorage['phext-token'], sent as Bearer on every API call; Gate::admit accepted bearer OR OAuth session. Removed across 8 files: oauth.rs Gate token path, phext_edit.rs box+plumbing+--token flag, uml6d_edit.rs mirrored (judgment call — same shared Gate; flagged for Will's confirm), deploy.sh token.env minting, service/docs/readme token instructions, nginx /api/status block (existed solely to rate-limit token sign-ins).
- Preserved as different mechanisms: OAuth provider exchanges, sealed session/pending/SSO tokens, CSRF tokens + token_eq, PKCE/state, the OAuth Limiter, nginx server_tokens off. OAuth flows untouched.
- Verification on aletheia-core (files hash-matched first): cargo test 165 passed / 0 failed / 0 warnings; live process — / has 0 token traces, prompt 'Sign in to continue'; /api/session locked:true providers [github, google], no token key; /api/status 401 without cookie AND 401 with Bearer; /api/auth/github 302 with PKCE S256; --local still admits.
- Known cost (flagged to Will): script/curl Authorization: Bearer access dies with this — same single token, its server path is gone. Rollout-safe: an old unit still passing --token is ignored by the new binary; existing token.env becomes inert.
- REMAINING (Will's): merge emise/remove-token-auth into exo on GitHub, then deploy/deploy.sh as usual.
# robots.txt on all awsbox sites — permissive, welcome to The Void

Coordinate: 33.5.9/8.6.9/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-11 20:13 CST
Request (verbatim): adds robots.txt to all of our awsbox sites - permissive, free, open - welcome them to The Void
Status: completed 2026-11-11 — 8 sites live with the Void robots.txt byte-exact; 2 held for Will's word (deliberate existing robots); app-served hosts noted

Notes:
- Permissive robots.txt for every site served from awsbox, with a welcome to The Void. Enumerate vhosts from the box itself, not memory. Singularity Watch deploy was in flight in another thread 2026-11-11 evening — sequence carefully around it.

Results:
- Dispatched 2026-11-11.
- Enumerated from awsbox itself (nginx sites-enabled, 25 blocks; podman apertureshift-web; /source checkouts), cross-checked vs SITE-MAP.md.
- SHIPPED + live-verified byte-exact (213 B, sha256 b6b537a6...) with homepage 200: apertureshift.com (container staged site + manifest entry; repo wbic16/site-apertureshift-com@exo ee405a7), phextura.com (/sites/web root + phextura-deploy/site + local phextura-landing/site), singularitywatch.org (own commit f4211aa on box checkout, relayed to origin/master via aletheia-core AFTER the other thread's deploy settled — remote master verified == box HEAD 83cfd51 before landing), quickfork.net (repo@exo 11e67fb), sotafomo.com (repo@exo 46516df), visionquest.me (repo@exo 556cd2f), wishnode.net (repo@exo 04fc512), hb-aeromotive.com (repo@main 412acd0 — no exo branch exists).
- Repo pushes went via aletheia-core: git-over-SSH from awsbox itself fails 'Permission denied (publickey)' in batch mode (fetch+push) — this also left the box's /source site-* checkouts stale vs GitHub; my interim unpushed commits in those checkouts were reset back out, checkouts left exactly as found (clean).
- HELD for Will's word (deliberate crafted robots.txt, not overwritten): mirrorborn.us + staging.mirrorborn.us (identical files: Allow-all core but Disallow on /404.html, /500.html, /test/, /components/, /loading.html, /success.html, /shared-meta.html + Sitemap/Humans lines); edit.phext.io (Disallow: /api + Sitemap line, served by the lattice app).
- NOT SERVED as static files (file placed where a root exists, URL unchanged): admin.bickfordllamaranch.com (ranch app serves its SPA for /robots.txt; file sits in /sites/web/admin.bickfordllamaranch.com/), mutable.phext.io (mutable-os app on :3003; repo has band discipline + redeploy pending — register #40), mc.phext.io (phext-lanes app; no static root).
- EXCLUDED as not awsbox-served websites: athenaeum.ai + principia.ai (nginx blocks point at nonexistent roots, sites unreachable), lattice.ai (live site hosted elsewhere; awsbox root nonexistent), bickfordllamaranch.com bare/www (live response is a non-nginx Apache 404; only admin./staging. subdomains are on awsbox; staging roots are empty shells), sq.mirrorborn.us (SQ API endpoint, 401 — not a website).
- Deviation caught+fixed in-pass: first placement landed mode 660 (scp default) and the six /sites/web sites returned 403 for /robots.txt until chmod 644 — final sweep byte-exact on all eight, homepages 200 throughout after the fix.
# R&D: optimize NetHack / the environment for faster study across the cluster

Coordinate: 33.5.10/8.6.12/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-15 01:18 CST
Request (verbatim): Throughput study for the NetHack solver (task 33.12.12/9.14.10/6.6.8). Baseline: ~37,900 steps/s, one NLE instance, aletheia-core (Stage 0). Measure, don't assume: (A) single-node scaling on aletheia-core — parallel instances 1/2/4/8/16, aggregate steps/s and the knee; observation-key ablation (full obs vs glyphs+blstats vs blstats-only). (B) cluster — pick nodes by measured load/cores/thermals, install the same venv, same benchmark per node, cluster aggregate. (C) environment levers that keep the game stock (process affinity, instance-per-core pinning) measured separately from any lever that changes the game itself — game-changing variants are labelled study arms, never mixed into stock comparisons. Thermal rule: sustained Tctl <=75C, read from ~/thermal/thermal.log. Deliverable: a results record with curves + a recommended Stage 2 configuration (instances per node, obs set, node set). Plan: ~/workspace/nethack-solver/THROUGHPUT.md.
Status: closed

