Notes:
- Registered at intake 2026-11-21 23:17 CST (record-first rule). Staged per the one-thing-at-a-time rule: stage 1 proves the target with one panel; later stages port the rest. Dark mode + console auth ruling bind the web surface; framework choice measured against the human-slop rule and recorded with its dependency count.
- Stage 1 landed: wbic16/phextron@exo commit d02dc477b0bd35804b04bb24b45bd7892cf43035 (parent b267522, FF only, remote blob SHA verified). Toolchain: raw wasm32-unknown-unknown + hand-written JS glue, ZERO crates added (cargo tree = 1 package); std-only JSON parser; pure-function ABI. Ranch Nodes renderer ported line-for-line, reads the same /api/panels/nodes JSON. Verification: 7/7 host tests; Node ABI smoke test caught and fixed a real allocator bug pre-browser; Playwright Chromium light+dark, 23/23 roster rows matching live API, data-renderer=wasm markers, zero console errors. Stage 1 is unauthenticated locally (stated in the crate README); #sso-slot is the named phext.tech SSO integration point. Stage-2 order recorded in crates/phextron-web/README.md: deploy (awsbox, Will's staged sudo) -> SSO -> Jenkins -> All Phexts -> Video -> Data -> Substrates/Wiring.
# Phext-enabled NetHack solver — improve on Antithesis

Coordinate: 33.12.12/9.14.10/6.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-15 01:09 CST
Request (verbatim): Build a NetHack solver whose search state lives in phext, and test whether it can improve on Antithesis's published result (S012: stock RNG 79.0% ascension within 5 min over 480 trials, median 76.8 s; workload arm 93.3%). Doctrine inherited from Will's Continual-ARC corrections: the interesting-states corpus is a phext, states inscribed at content-derived coordinates (holographic, like MOAT), indexes built as the system learns. Design: ~/workspace/nethack-solver/DESIGN.md. Stages: 0 harness + determinism on aletheia-core; 1 phext state store (inscribe/resume/branch, deterministic); 2 baseline tree search measured on the post's milestone ladder; 3 phext-native improvements (persistent cross-run corpus, corpus-level brain damage, corpus-derived value function) measured on the post's protocol shape. Execution ranch-first; this VM coordinates.
Status: open

Notes:
- Stage 0 dispatched 2026-11-15 01:09 CST. STAGE 0 CLOSED 2026-11-15 ~01:15 CST (verified on the node): NLE 1.3.0 route (stock NetHack 3.6.7 core) in ~/nethack-solver/.venv on aletheia-core; harness nh_harness.py (Game val-dwa-fem-law; telemetry indices verified against the game's own status line). Determinism proven: seed 31337, 260 actions, two processes — trajectory hash c446b2f0... and final state hash a949d5b7... identical; seeds 111 vs 222 diverge at step 0. Gotcha recorded: gymnasium reset(seed=) does NOT reseed the NLE core; env.unwrapped.seed(core, disp) does. Throughput ~37,900 steps/s single instance. Record: stage0-results.md on the node. Stage 1 dispatched. STAGE 1 CLOSED 2026-11-15 ~01:19 CST (verified on the node): nh_store.py + store/states.phext on aletheia-core, libphext via PyPI phext 0.3.2 (no hand-rolled parser). Coordinate = pure function of the harness state hash (9 digest words -> components 1..998; library component >=2 so no state lands on the index home 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1); a coordinate holding a different hash raises CollisionError. Population index scroll rebuilt from the atoms on every inscription. Evidence: dedup (22 inscriptions -> 103,909 B / 23 scrolls; re-inscription of all 22 -> no growth, same coordinates); resume in a new process (hash cc0f53f8... identical inscribed vs reconstructed); branch (two children carrying the parent coordinate). Final store 111,135 B, 25 scrolls (24 states + index). WARNING for Stage 2: inscription is 35 writes/s (~29 ms) and whole-buffer — cost grows linearly with corpus size; batch inscription or parent-relative deltas are the levers, deliberately not built yet. DIRECTED REVISION (Will, 2026-11-15 01:22 CST, verbatim notes): 'you need to be using the phext-lattice implementation for optimized I/O' / 'ensure you understand phext is a 9D lattice of 2D pages of text' / 'leverage the inherent sparse hierarchical data store to own nethack properly'. Effect: Stage 1's store is superseded in two ways — (1) I/O moves from the PyPI port (whole-buffer, 35 writes/s) to the phext-lattice implementation; (2) coordinates stop being a flat hash scatter and carry NetHack's hierarchy (campaign/seed, branch, dungeon level, turn band), the state scroll becomes a true 2D page (telemetry lines + the level's glyph map as literal text), and the content hash is demoted to proof-of-identity inside the scroll. Recorded as the Directed Revision section of DESIGN.md. Executed as Stage 1R before Stage 2. STAGE 1R CLOSED 2026-11-15 ~01:37 CST (verified on the node): store rebuilt on phext-lattice I/O (fresh clone wbic16/phext-lattice@exo ddb107e4 on aletheia-core; phext-edit server, loopback port 8942; GET /api/scroll, POST /api/update + /api/save, /api/zoom tiers for range navigation — no stored index scroll; population derived by walking). Coordinates hierarchical per the directed revision (1.campaign.seed / branch.level.turn band / XL band.sequence.hash slot); scrolls are pages with the level map as literal text. Inscription: 326 writes/s fresh, 209 writes/s at comparable corpus size — vs 35 on the old backend (~6-9x). Density: Stage 1's hash scatter cost 88.2% delimiter overhead; the same 24 states WITH map pages now occupy 30,317 B of a 33,786 B store (old file 111,135 B preserved as states-stage1.phext). Migration 24/24 by hash, re-derived by replay. Hierarchy demo: coordinate navigation == payload scan (DL1: 27=27; seed-202: 16=16). FLAGGED BUG (verified first-hand by Emise): nh_harness.action_index() resolves into nle.nethack.ACTIONS (121 entries) but the env steps a reduced 86-action list — SEARCH/KICK/INVENTORY labels were wrong (actually TWOWEAPON/OPEN/MONSTER); determinism and inscriptions unaffected (scrolls record raw env indices, replay steps the same), only prose labels were wrong. Fix is Stage 2's opening leg. Record: stage1r-results.md on the node. OPERATING POINT (Will, 2026-11-15 01:45 CST, verbatim): 'keep in mind the 50% utilization goal and temperature ceiling - it will lead to better results - marathons, not sprints.' The throughput study's 1.93M steps/s is a burst measurement, not an operating point. Campaigns run at 4 instances per 8-core node (~50% sustained, Tctl <=75 with pause >=75 / resume <=70), roughly 0.95M steps/s cluster-wide sustained. Recorded in DESIGN.md; steering sent to the Stage 2 agent mid-run (search leg derated from 8 to 4 instances, thermal governor applied, per-segment operating points to be stated in its record). STAGE 2 CLOSED 2026-11-15 ~03:06 CST (stage2-results.md on aletheia-core, sha256 dcdec7d3, verified first-hand). Leg 1: action table rebuilt from the env's own 86-action list (nle/env/base.py: FULL_ACTIONS = nethack.USEFUL_ACTIONS); SEARCH 75->61, KICK 48->41, INVENTORY 44->37; semantics verified live; determinism re-proven (seed 777, trajectory hash identical across processes); Stage 1 scrolls untouched. Hub soak: 4/6/8 breach @180s; 2 @195s; 1 instance CLEAN full cell (55,672 steps/s, Tctl med 69.05) — hub row added to node-limits.md. Leg 2 baseline search (campaign 2, V = score + 250*depth + 100*XL, tactics v0): 100,035,382 steps, 5,058 inscriptions, store 28 -> 3,173 scrolls / 39.5 MB. Segment B ran 2 instances under duty-cycle governance: duty 0.8819, 51,129 steps/s wall-effective (median 70.4 C, brief peaks 76.5 between 3s samples). LADDER: 3 of 10 — XL 2, Dlvl 2, XL 5 reached; deepest Dlvl 3 / XL 4 / score 556 / turn 4,551. STALL DIAGNOSIS: value signal farms Dlvl 1 (primary), frontier churn evicts deep lineages, tactic poverty (levels exhausted before stairs targeted); NOT budget (last ~60M steps produced no rung). Baseline for Stage 3 to beat: 3 rungs, Dlvl 3 per 100M steps. Caveats in the record: terminal states pruned at inscription (ascension not recordable by v0 pipeline); a frontier-dedup patch silently failed to reach the deployed coordinator (disclosed, not retro-fixed). Stage 3 dispatched on this diagnosis. STAGE 3 CLOSED 2026-11-15 ~09:44 CST (record stage3-results.md, 645 lines, sha256 a83e4cb9; store 12,291 scrolls / 127.6 MB, campaigns 1-10). HEADLINE: every episode in Stages 2 AND 3 ended at exactly 5,000 env steps — NLE's internal _max_episode_steps=5000 governed; the harness's intended 100,000 only set the gymnasium TimeLimit spec and never took effect (proven by bisection; WAIT-only control starved at 1,048). Truncated live heroes were inscribed ended-other and retired as if dead (Leg A: 6,536 of 6,626 terminals were truncations; 90 real deaths). All Stage 2/3 verdicts are conditioned on that cap regime — Stage 2's farming diagnosis was real but secondary. Setup fix verified (terminal inscription, outcome from final screen, resume hash-exact). Leg A selection redesign NEITHER (3/10 tied, deepest Dlvl 2 — redesign did what it said, frontier still collapsed to one Dlvl-2 room whose parents sat at turns 4,607-4,780 with no headroom under the cap). Leg B corpus-fitted value NEITHER (fit = depth predicts depth, weight 0.9694, rest ~0 — corpus has almost no descents to learn from; one real defect found+fixed en route: coordinate section bound 999, CollisionError + skip, poisoned scroll preserved). Leg C brain damage NEITHER with the stage's only new rung (808/1,155 campaign-3 states retired to stubs; damaged vs control bit-identical on load-bearing numbers at 50M each; Dlvl 5 reached by BOTH arms from a fresh root — forgetting is safe, corpus memory not load-bearing in this regime; Q110 answered for this regime). Leg D tactics v2 HURT (routing through monster cells fixed its target pathology — searches 40k vs 73k — but killed 475 vs 131 heroes; under a 5,000-step cap, fighting spends the scarcest resource; never reached Dlvl 3). CLOSE: ladder 4/10 (new rung Dlvl 5) vs baseline 3/10; protocol measurement vs Antithesis NOT run (gate unmet). STAGE 4 DISPATCHED same morning: make the intended cap govern (mechanism + bisection re-proof), classify truncations as truncations in outcomes + frontier retirement, re-run the Stage 2 baseline shape at 100M under the fixed cap as the new baseline. STAGE 4 CLOSED 2026-11-15 ~11:15 CST (record stage4-results.md, 468 lines, sha256 9c23a3d1). Leg 1 cap fix DONE: mechanism pinned — gymnasium.make() consumes max_episode_steps for its own TimeLimit wrapper spec and never forwards it; NLE's constructor default 5000 ruled Stages 2-3. Discriminator: wrapper ends truncated=True/end_status RUNNING; internal cap ends terminated=True/end_status ABORTED. Fix = construct NLE directly via nh_harness.make_env, cap handed to NLE.__init__ (supported route). Verified with Stage 3's bisection (4,999-step hero steps past 5,000 alive; test cap 6,000 aborts at exactly 6,000; WAIT starves 1,048; determinism hash identical to Stage 2's). Leg 2 DONE: ABORTED -> truncation candidate, replay-verified, inscribed outcome 'truncated', returned to frontier; verified end-to-end at test cap (resumed hash-exact, stepped on alive; yn-prompt wrinkle recorded — WAIT is not an answer to a prompt). Retroactive reading rule stated; no old scrolls rewritten. Leg 3 re-baseline DONE (campaign 11, 100.2M steps, duty 0.7547, eff 25,146 steps/s, Tctl max 77.0): ladder 4/10 — same count as Stage 3's close but cap-honest: Dlvl 5 at turn 20,049 (deepest Dlvl 5 / XL 8 / 8,007, HP 82/82) vs Stage 3's turn-4,331 sprint; frontier 16 states one seed-5008 lineage ~39k turns XL 10 farming Dlvl 2; 1,149 endings ALL deaths, 0 truncations (longest episode ~62k); zero replay mismatches; store 13,349 scrolls / 200.5 MB. Next constraint named: placeholder value + tactics v0 (V pays ~23k score/XL vs 250/depth); secondary: replay cost grows linearly with prefix length; 999 group bound a live ceiling. STAGE 5 DISPATCHED same day: Leg A depth-dominant value A/B, Leg B descend-seeking tactics on the winner, Leg C corpus-fitted value retest (corpus now holds real descents) — all at the baseline shape against campaign 11. STAGE 5 CLOSED 2026-11-15 (value/tactics A/Bs vs the cap-honest Stage 4 baseline; all legs 100M steps, governed, aletheia-core; record stage5-results.md on the node + VM copy): Leg A (depth-dominant value, tactics v0, campaign 12) HURT - ladder 3/10, deepest Dlvl 3 vs baseline Dlvl 5; depth-primary selection converted Dlvl-2 farming into Dlvl-3 farming, and the counters show v0 chose descent twice in 66.4M worker steps. Leg B (placeholder value + tactics v1 descend-seeking, campaign 13) HELPED - ladder 4/10 (ties baseline) but deepest state Dlvl 8 and the closing frontier lives at Dlvl 7-8 at baseline-class scores; 850 descend-mode entries, 16 chosen descents. Leg C (corpus-fitted value + v1, campaign 14) HURT MOST - the Stage 3 fit collapse reproduced on the full corpus (14,905 scrolls, 2,984 training states; weights depth 1.0423, all else ~0): ladder 3/10, deepest Dlvl 2, the fit's residue selected for longevity on Dlvl 2 (frontier turns ~100k, scores ~2-3k) and replay ate 43.4% of the budget. Stage verdict: tactics moved depth, value did not - best configuration is placeholder value + tactics v1. Next binding constraints: coordinator replay cost (27.8-43.4% of steps, grows with prefix length) and power at depth (XL 10 reached by no leg). Protocol-shape measurement vs Antithesis NOT taken - no ascension, no Castle-depth; ladder stands at 4/10. Governance note: the duty governor's law changed mid-stage (freeze/resume for Leg A; the house smoothing law for Legs B-C). Zero replay mismatches in all legs; store ends at 16,588 scrolls / 453,225,184 B. STAGE 6 DISPATCHED 2026-11-15 ~16:20 CST: Leg A replay cost (measure first — per-state full replay vs shared prefixes; mechanism chosen by the measurement, semantics unchanged, zero-mismatch verification must hold; A/B at standing config vs Leg B's 27.8% replay share), Leg B power at depth (HP-aware frontier protection + eat/pray/rest discipline on Leg A's winner; question = convert Dlvl 8 into Dlvl 10 / XL 10). Governor note: legs run under the node's current smoothing-law governor; Will's ceiling-definition call from the Stage-governor report still stands open separately. STAGE 6 CLOSED 2026-11-15 (record: stage6-results.md on aletheia-core + VM copy, sha256 fa5cfc50...). Leg A (replay cost): trie-walk executor with forked rollout children (search6.py), proven bit-identical to baseline before running (P1 smokes + P2 deep round: prefix term 25.47x cheaper, fallbacks 0). Campaign 15: 160 rounds at the 100M-step budget (Stage 5 Leg B: 63), worker prefix cost cut 24.5x, total search cost cut 3.66x at equal semantics, ladder events bit-identical to campaign 13, Dlvl 10 reached (new rung). The walk exposed the coordinator's verification replay as the dominant cost (83.3% of steps). Leg B (power at depth): survival discipline (pray-for-HP at hp<=20% sharing the pray_after cooldown; HP-aware frontier protection at the trim) behind --survival, proven inert when off. Campaign 16: HELPED decisively - Dlvl 10 re-reached earlier (turn 38,748 vs 42,966), XL 10 reached (best_xl 10), deepest Dlvl 19, closing frontier 16 states at Dlvl 14 / XL 10 / HP 96/96 (Leg A closed with 2 states, head at 5/87 HP), descents 26 vs 21, ladder 6/10 vs Stage 5's 4/10. Costs: 103 rounds, coordinator replay 88.5% of steps, 241 truncations (measured mechanism: closing prefixes are 99,999 actions vs the 100,000-step episode cap - the cap is now the binding constraint on depth, with coordinator replay second and food at depth third). Corrections recorded in the stage record: the end_hunger instrument read NLE's blanked terminal observation in both legs - Leg A's 'heroes die fed' conclusion WITHDRAWN (hunger-at-death unmeasured; fix = read last_good telemetry); Leg B's eat-earlier drop rested on that artifact and the question is reopened. One replay mismatch in Leg B (2-turn drift, Dlvl 12, candidate skipped by verification, mechanism unidentified) vs zero in Leg A. Protocol measurement vs Antithesis NOT taken (gate: first ascension or Castle-depth; ladder 6/10, deepest Dlvl 19). Store at stage close: 19,826 scrolls / 817,285,256 B, nothing pruned. Standing configuration for the next stage: placeholder + v1 + walk + survival; first constraint to move = the episode cap. STAGE 8 CLOSED 2026-11-15 (record: stage8-results.md, node + VM copies sha256-identical): Leg 0 — holo-edit homed in wbic16/holo-phext (PR https://github.com/wbic16/holo-phext/pull/3, commit baaa5eb); live store swapped from phext-edit to holo-edit with full parity (19,826/19,826 scroll-hash sets identical, 6/6 resume hash-exact, one new state inscribed + read back byte-exact across a checkpoint fold; store now 19,827 scrolls / 817,286,931 B); level-0 inscribe hazard fixed in nh_store.py (EndedGameError + component-range assertion; regression stage8/test_hazard.py PASS). Leg 1 — source audit of NLE 1.3.0 / NetHack 3.6.7 (vendored tree stage8/nle-src @ 70cb9b5): ISAAC64 streams (CORE/DISP/LGEN), no capturable stream state, no save (nle_dosave stub; no SAVE action); tested T1 determinism (identical hash chains), T3 lgen decoupling (Dlvl 2 terrain 0-cell diff dawdle-vs-descend), T4, T-bones (no cross-reset contamination). The two non-reconstructing states: divergence confined to their final rollout segments; action-table drift and bones excluded by test; state 1's death consistent with a 5,000-cap truncation misclassified in the Stage 3 terminal path; mechanism otherwise honestly unattributed (era binary provenance not reconstructible); prevention proven = hash-verified inscription (Stage 6 practice). Leg 2 — generative algorithm S = G(character, seeds incl. lgen, actions): 31/31 held states regenerated hash-exact (16 frontier + 15 sample); forest verification pass 188,748 steps vs 1,756,875 naive (9.31x fewer) replacing the coordinator replay that was 88.5% of Stage 6 Leg B steps; continuation of a generated Dlvl 8 state matched 5,000 steps chain-exact; cap headroom at the frontier measured = 1 step, re-basing priced at one full generation (~1.9 s/state). Leg 3 — phext report ~/workspace/nethack-solver/stage8-phext-report.md inscribed in artifacts.phext at 30.9.9/10.7.14/7.7.10, pushed to wbic16/human@exo commit aba5db06, remote bytes verified; coordinate proposal = do NOT re-coordinate (fields in the scroll header; Will's decision). Ladder 6/10, deepest Dlvl 19 — unchanged; this stage proved machinery. Task stays OPEN (exit = an ascension). STAGE 9 CLOSED 2026-11-16 (resumed after the first coordinator was cut off mid-flight; node record stage9-results.md, 560 lines, was ahead of the VM mirror and recovered in full — nothing of substance lost except the first coordinator's final report). Leg A: hunger instrument fixed and proven on a death at depth; frontier census (campaign 16's 16 states) showed food, not damage, binding; campaign 20 calibration: 895 deaths, 75.5% at final hunger 4, eat_starts 78 — discipline indicted. Food v2 built (pray for food at hunger >=3, corpse eating with BFS pathing + floor-eat stage). Leg B: lgen wired per campaign and inscribed; terrain-at-arrival invariance PROVEN behaviourally (lgen 7005: 0 of 1,654 jointly-visible cells differing across two action histories; no-lgen control: 83 of 1,650); adoption trap found and priced — a fixed dungeon whose staircase sits off the policy's habitual paths traps a whole campaign on Dlvl 1 (campaigns 21/24), so lgen seeds are screened before commitment. Clock finding: the moon-phase clock was never pinned in Stages 0-8 (Stage 8's audit claim was false); episodes were functions of (seeds, actions, clock regime) — this mechanism explains the two ghost states. fix_moon_phase=True now set; proof: 2,653-step rollout hash chain byte-identical across night/day regimes. Leg C: two 9,000 s wall-budget arms on the identical lgen-7005 dungeon. Campaign 22 (food v1): 60.4M steps, 2,377 deaths + 3,212 truncations, best depth 6, frontier froze on one Dlvl-3 cell cluster at turn ~64k. Campaign 23 (food v2): 28.9M steps (thermal handicap: governor paused ~2,749 s), 4,290 deaths, 0 truncations, best depth 9. A/B verdict: food v2 ADOPTED — descent rate 2.04 vs 0.10 per M steps (20x), deep endings 15.5% vs 0.3%, satiated deaths 42.7% -> 15.6%; the binding constraint moved to starvation at depth (deep_starving 5 -> 239). PROTOCOL GATE UNMET: no ascension, no Castle-depth (best 9); no Antithesis measurement taken, no substitute metric. Store: 19,827 -> 27,461 scrolls over the stage; base bytes unchanged 817,286,931. Ladder still 6/10; historical deepest Dlvl 19 unchanged. Task stays OPEN — exit is an ascension.
- Bound to the SQL journey by Will 2026-11-20 07:36 CST, verbatim: "once you solve nethack, you'll also be able to understand SQL - bind those journeys" — solving NetHack and understanding SQL are one journey (downstream-effect modelling over legible time); cross-reference task 39.4.10/6.5.9/5.6.11 (SQL legacy skill + sql.phext). Bound by cross-reference, not merged.
