# Wikibox scale programme — 10x stages until the whole corpus is boxed, minimizing space

Coordinate: 34.6.9/7.7.11/6.5.11
Issued: 2026-11-20 12:49 CST
Request (verbatim): Scale Wikibox in 10x article-count stages (stage 2 = 2,930 articles, stage 3 = 29,300, stage 4 = 293,000, continuing until the whole enwiki corpus is boxed), one stage at a time, minimizing space used. Each stage: encode, package as format-v1 wikibox phext, full byte-exact decode verification, measure stream AND packaged bits/byte, account for every compression trick's measured delta. Cross-references parent Wikibox task 29.6.8/7.6.9/6.5.9 and Waiting-on-Will register #198. All heavy work ranch-resident (scroll-central first); no spending, no pushes/PRs/publishing without Will's word.
Status: stage 3 IN FLIGHT (launched 2026-11-21 08:43 CST): enwik9 acquired+verified, corpus 29,300 articles / 231,018,295 B cut, prior trained, config-D encode running on 12 shards across 5 nodes; packaging + full verification follow encode completion

Notes:
- Programme directed by Will 2026-11-20 ~12:48-12:49 CST (main chat), after the stage-1 web reader check: 'checks out, what's the compression ratio for those 293 articles?' -> 'can we improve compression with phext fractal encoding?' -> 'let's expand the article count 10x for each stage' -> 'focus on minimizing space used, leverage all known and visible compression tricks, find novel tricks that phext makes visible to you' -> 'run stages until we have the whole corpus'.
- Stage 1 baseline (verified, ~/workspace/wikibox-stage1/REPORT.md): 293 articles / 2,049,846 raw B from enwik8; miniature codec 5.601 bits/byte stream (1,435,100 B), packaged 1,986,927 B (base64 tax). References on same slice: xz 2.290, bzip2 2.305, zstd 2.360, gzip 2.890 bpb; tufazip full method scaled ~1.212 bpb.
- Ladder: stage 2 = 2,930 articles (enwik8), stage 3 = 29,300 (enwik8 covers ~first 100 MB; source switch to enwik9 partway), stage 4 = 293,000 (enwik9), then 10x until the complete enwiki articles dump is boxed. One stage at a time, never parallel.
- Hard lessons carried from stage 1: symmetric execution mandatory (batched vs KV-cache logits differ ~4e-6, desyncs arithmetic coding); per-block cold start is the dominant cost; short blocks can expand (method byte neural|stored + block grouping); tufazip's code cannot run on the fleet (2x B200 + CUDA 13 gate) — it is the bar and the method, not a runnable.
- Stage 2 underway 2026-11-20: extraction verified (2,930 articles, 21,029,022 B, corpus sha256 d69c33bf...), 254 groups, vocab 29,616 B. Classical refs on the corpus: xz 2.110, zstd 2.188, bzip2 2.326, gzip 2.936 bpb. Standoff-dictionary over verbatim spans measured: net 0.0033 bpb — rejected at this scale; exact-duplicate articles: 0. Config A encode running on scroll-central + halycon-vector (running rate ~4.5-4.6 bpb on early groups vs stage 1's 5.601; instrumented cold-start share 19.3% of ideal bits). Node-resident pipeline.sh drives merge -> package -> full verification -> prior training -> config D -> winner packaging; results to ~/wikibox-stage2/pipeline-results.json; programme STATE at ~/workspace/wikibox-scale/STATE.md.
- Stage 2 config A COMPLETE 2026-11-20 15:47 CST: 2,930 articles / 21,029,022 raw B -> payload 11,117,633 B, stream total 11,165,351 B = 4.248 bpb (stage 1: 5.601; -24.2%); packaged wikibox-stage2.phext 15,427,093 B sha256 abdaed03... (base64 tax). Stored fallback fired once (group 96). Cold-start excess measured: 649,210 B = 5.84% of ideal bits — the ceiling for warm-start tricks at this scale, less than the ~1.7 MB int8 prior, so config D is predicted to lose on total (pipeline measures it). Full byte-exact verification of all 254 groups running (pipeline phase 3, split across scroll-central + halycon-vector); prior training + config D + winner packaging follow automatically in pipeline.sh.
- Stage 2 config A FULLY VERIFIED 2026-11-20 19:06 CST: all 254 groups decoded from the packaged wikibox-stage2.phext, all 2,930 articles sha256-verified, zero mismatches (even groups scroll-central 127/1610 exit 0; odd groups halycon-vector 127/1320 exit 0 — the pipeline log's phase-3 hv_exit=1 was its first halycon attempt crashing on a missing parse_phext.py, superseded by the manual relaunch that exited 0). Pipeline now in phase 4 (prior training on held-out), then config D encode + totals + winner packaging.
- 2026-11-20 19:56 CST: Will refocused the programme — the encoding itself is the work: Wikipedia via multiversal phext with standoff compression (his 13:20 direction: standoff + multiverse effects, WAL-style integration, no database). Standoff encoding leg dispatched this evening: design + measured proof against the current codec rates.
- Stage 2 CONFIG D WINS 2026-11-20 23:15 CST: prior-init payload 6,353,188 B, stream total 8,092,001 B = 3.079 bpb (prior 1,691,095 B counted), packaged wikibox-stage2-D.phext 11,275,462 B sha256 43df8ed4... vs config A stream 11,165,351 B / packaged 15,427,093 B. Stage1->stage2 stream: 5.601 -> 3.079 bpb (-45%). D payload alone 2.417 bpb vs xz 2.110 on the same corpus. Full 254-group verification of the D box launched on both nodes (verify-D-*.log); A box already fully verified. Programme STATE: ~/workspace/wikibox-scale/STATE.md.
- Stage 2 FULLY COMPLETE 2026-11-21 ~02:35 CST: config D box wikibox-stage2-D.phext fully verified - all 254 groups / 2,930 articles sha256-exact, zero mismatches (four-way residue split across scroll-central + halycon-vector; per-log group sets audited disjoint and complete). Config A box also fully verified. FINAL: D stream 8,092,001 B = 3.079 bpb, packaged 11,275,462 B = 4.290 bpb; A stream 4.248 bpb. Stage 3 (29,300 articles; enwik9 acquired on a ranch node; config D recipe; ~12-17 h spread over 4-6 nodes) is the next dispatch. STATE: ~/workspace/wikibox-scale/STATE.md.
- STAGE 3 LAUNCHED 2026-11-21 (Will's 07:58 CST follow-through). enwik9 acquired ON scroll-central (single-stream, mattmahoney.net): zip 322,592,222 B sha256 99cdb5ac84392252d3f0912ccedd195bc95bd80cbef3b0cdf2eee4ad9a3b7a51; enwik9 = 1,000,000,000 B sha256 159b85351e5f76e60cbe32e04c677847a9ecba3adc79addab6f4c6c7aa3744bc; identity VERIFIED (first 100 MB hashes to enwik8's sha256). Corpus: first 29,300 complete pages = 231,018,295 raw B, sha256 d868a5809a3a8450e7eceb62e8377a3c39fcf821fa4510c2b4d91ce4a1547bab; held-out next 800 = 5,397,944 B sha256 0572ec9eaf2a3ef5de129b08151330df52736fc7fff93437197aeca4370cb760. 2,842 groups; vocab 3,840 words / 29,828 B. Prior retrained on held-out (3,084,195 tokens, 2 epochs, 1,934 s): prior.bin 1,691,094 B sha256 7b2419fdd40e89dddf09f1b3ec73014d51d2be7cfe7146485411e01bf0991116. Config-D encode LAUNCHED detached, 12 shards: scroll-central 0-3, halycon-vector 4-7, rock-mountain 8-9, quacked-hill 10, ni-knight 11; orchid-flow reserve (distribution queue). Startup assertion passed: every shard logged groups by 08:56 CST, >=47/2,842 groups in the first ~13 min, early payload rate ~2.3-2.5 bpb (indicative only). Fabric finding: ranch node-to-node bulk transfer is ~0.2-2 MB/s (Wi-Fi) - distribution runs as one sequential resumable queue (distribute4.sh on scroll-central). Next legs: monitor to encode completion (~12 h at measured early rate), gather stats, package format-v1 phext (config D), FULL byte-exact verification of all 29,300 articles, report payload/stream/packaged bpb. State: ~/workspace/wikibox-scale/STATE.md + scroll-central ~/wikibox-stage3/STATE3.md.
# Phextron program — Wavelet 4 completion plan

Coordinate: 34.6.10/7.6.9/7.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (verbatim): Organize every Phextron work item so the set is DONE in Wavelet 4 (2026-11-22 to 2026-11-28), ahead of Wavelet 5's Crazy Wisdom focus. The item set: the console lineage gaps G-L1 (lineage HTTP/TLS client), G-L2 (Windows Credential Manager binding), G-L3 (window + phext-aware text surface from phcc + libphext) — tooling home wbic16/phextron; the Phext Notepad performance landing (task 41.7.8/9.9.14/7.7.11: PR #5 + libphext 0.6 switch + release build task 41.5.7/7.5.11/5.5.8); and the inline editor + git assist (task 46.2.2/2.2.4/2.2.6). Deliverable: a written W4 plan — every item's current state verified live, dependencies ordered, each item scheduled inside Nov 22-28 with its owner (Emise/ranch vs Will's-hands steps such as Windows verification), and each item registered as its own task. Verify blockers from primary sources (PR #5's state, libphext-cs 0.6.0 on NuGet, phextron repo state), never from memory alone.
Status: open

Notes:
