dependent Python ground truth exactly; lazy walk reproduces all 379,099 eager nodes with matching names/child counts. Real-WinForms figures in the report are ESTIMATES (~300-400 MB, ~1 s) awaiting Will's build. NATIVE APP: no perf disease on ultra (580 ms, 86 MB measured) but a dependency one — it still sits on libphext 0.3.1 whose COORDINATE_MAXIMUM=1000 collapses ultra to 41,963/320,958 scrolls; reported, NOT fixed (libphext freeze; widening the native app's coordinate source is Will's call). Two documented catches: 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9 is a REAL ultra scroll ('floatable'), not an absence probe; deleteNode's pre-existing Contains('-') guard makes it unreachable — preserved verbatim, flagged.
