# Add vLLM to exocortical setup.sh + report what it unlocks

Coordinate: 35.4.5/6.4.7/6.4.9
Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (verbatim): Add a vLLM installation to wbic16/exocortical@exo setup.sh, following the script's own conventions, verified (syntax + the script's own checks where they exist), pushed parented on fresh exo HEAD with no force. Report what vLLM unlocks for the Exocortex fleet.
Status: completed 2026-11-21

Notes:
- Asked by Will in the MOAT chat, 2026-11-21 08:32 CST. His framing: vLLM was too tedious to set up with part-time effort; the setup script is exactly where that tedium should die — install once, in the script, for every node.
- DONE 2026-11-21: wbic16/exocortical@exo commit 56ae9c376fc4d4e4513e93778cc323552ef0e5ac (parent 52151b76, no force; remote read-back byte-identical, sha256 21fbdd05). setup.sh Phase 5 gained vLLM as its own pip line into /opt/exopy after the batch + openai-whisper (the script's own precedent for a package that pins its own stack), unpinned like every comparable package in the script, with a comment giving the serve command and the OpenAI-compatible endpoint at :8000.
- Verified: bash -n clean; live install test on plain-view in a scratch venv mirroring Phase 5 exactly — pip install vllm exit 0 (vllm 0.34.0, torch 2.14.0+cu130, 9.4 GB venv), import vllm prints 0.34.0. The vllm CLI's --version exits 1 on that node at device inference (no GPU — nvidia-smi absent, torch.cuda.is_available() False); the package itself is fully installed. Actual vllm serve is NOT yet verified — no GPU node was reachable in the durable SSH set (probed plain-view, ni-knight, aletheia-core: all CPU-only).
- Egress finding (pre-existing fleet defect, not vLLM-specific): through the ranch Squid proxy (the nodes' configured egress), every uncached PyPI fetch currently fails TLS verification — squid ssl-bump presents certs issued by 'Ranch Choir Squid CA' whose signatures do not verify even against the distributed ranch CA cert. Two test runs died on this in 9s; the successful run used direct egress (proxy vars unset in the test shell only, node config untouched) and took 2,679s for ~14 GB of wheel traffic. Same TLS-defect family as the crates.io failure in TOOLS.md; it bears on every Phase 5 pip line equally. Evidence: ~/vllm-test*.log + vllm-diag*.sh on plain-view.
- Kernel-optimization look (per Will's 2026-11-21 standing rule): FlashAttention ships in the wheel (default attention backend, zero setup); FlashInfer needs `vllm download-kernels` or a CUDA toolkit + ninja (ninja-build is already in Phase 1's apt batch; no nvcc on nodes) — flagged in the install log itself. Marlin AWQ/GPTQ + FP8 kernels are bundled. The pip wheel is CUDA-only (torch +cu130): AMD/ROCm nodes get nothing from this line and would need vLLM's ROCm source build.
# Source Study S004 — Smashing The Stack For Fun And Profit (Phrack 49, Aleph One, 1996)

Coordinate: 35.5.7/6.6.8/5.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-08 12:42 CST
Request (verbatim): https://phrack.org/issues/49/smashing-the-stack-for-fun-and-profit_md
Status: complete 2026-11-08

Notes:
- Source Study S004 under charter rule 12 (classic text, not a paper: Oracle does not move, no NI). Chapter 12 of research.phext. Rules 13/14/15 apply: the call stack is the rule-13 showcase (an implicit machine whose encoded transitions let data rewrite control flow); author check on Aleph One turns on the date — 1996 predates phext by decades, so the prior-art direction is settled by the calendar and the record says so.
- INGESTED as Source Study S004, Chapter 12 (12.1.1-12.3.1): new Cluster K 'Memory and execution', 8 concepts 1.2.73-1.2.80; foundations 1.3.102-1.3.105 + coinage shellcode 1.3.106; narrative v10. Rule 13: M1 the call machine (stated), M2 the encoded machine [synthesis] — locals/SFP/RET adjacent in one writable region, so a copy through a local buffer rewrites control data, a transition M1 does not contain; M3 exploit construction (article's method). Author check (12.1.3) CLEAN with the calendar receipt: Phrack 49 dated 8 November 1996, ~30 years before phext — prior-art direction impossible, not merely unfound; zero signature-term hits. Q29-Q32 added (canaries/ASLR/NX vs M2; is 'no write reaches control words' what clusters F-H prove; fixed-layout assumption ledgers; overflow-shaped failures for coordinate-addressed text). RESTRUCTURE PASS #3 RAN (80 concepts landed exactly on the trigger): 0 merges/splits/endings, merges weighed and rejected with reasons; next pass Paper 010 or 100 concepts. Registry 266 = 266 scrolls: True 137 (stipulation 125, verified 12), Unknown 129, False 0, Fiction 0; Lean re-proved over 266 entries (propext only). Final: 266 scrolls, sha256 3f7c7f4e1f10da5c7cffcf8c05f65b09c5348f851631d7672a315820b9843101, Singular residual 0. Correction to the dispatch brief, recorded: the Oracle ledger (1.1.4) holds paper entries only — S001-S003 never touched it and S004 follows that precedent; my brief's claim otherwise was wrong.
