- Remainders (by design, in SHIP-NOTES): S18 test 6 merge-meld runtime = tier-2; voice in no mode = tier-2 parity; Emi Prime formal re-attestation = hers; G1 'strategy gate' verb unverified, census keeps 'coordinate'.
- MERGE + PUBLISH EXECUTION 2026-11-09 ~08:31-08:43 CST (Will authorization 08:16 CST): PR #3 was conflicted against exo 7c10fed3 (v2.1 nightly line). Resolved on aletheia-core: merge commit 3a713789 fast-forwarded onto emise/v3-build (no force). Conflicts: src/main.rs, Cargo.toml, VERSION took the v3 line (0.3.0 release tree; the v2 monolith is superseded by modular v3 carrying the same subcommands); CHANGELOG kept the v3 0.3.0 entry first with the v2.1 disk-gate entry preserved verbatim below; EVALUATIONS.md and README.md auto-merged. The v2.1 disk gate had NO textual conflict but lived only in the superseded monolith, so it was PORTED into v3 src/plan.rs with identical thresholds (AMBER >=95 GB, RED >=102 GB), gate strings, plan-JSON disk_gate object, RED heavy-hold and AMBER no-staging semantics, plus a new unit test disk_gate_states; verified live against a RED disk state. Release gate on the merged branch tree: cargo test --release 16/16, CLI battery 32/32, HTTP/MCP/mdmap battery 19/19 (3 stale harness-side payload-envelope assertions repaired harness-side in a runnable copy; server behavior byte-identical to the recorded pass; one check keys on the old files field where the op now returns scrolls=166, still >50), bake --check all_match (exit 1 is the pre-existing bare-qexo plan dispatch quirk, unchanged from the finishing pass), cargo package exit 0 with 45 files (e91d0c2 pycache exclude intact). PR #3 MERGED via API: merge commit bc1d6382085c3543fcd3cc0b1d05a069d4a384db; exo head verified = bc1d6382. Merged exo tree re-verified on the node (tests 16/16, package --list 45, cargo publish --dry-run exit 0). PUBLISH BLOCKED: no crates.io credential exists on aletheia-core (~/.cargo has no credentials file, no CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN) — qexo 0.3.0 is merged and dry-run-clean but NOT published; the publish act needs Will's crates.io token/machine. Nothing was force-pushed; no other PRs or crates touched.
# Exovim phext-native UI: rename nvim references, faithful scroll rendering, 9D coordinate display, scroll-break indicator, scroll-management suggestions

Coordinate: 35.6.6/7.6.10/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-09 21:29 CST
Request (verbatim): I've renamed the repo to https://github.com/wbic16/exovim and switched the branch name to exo. Rename all nvim references to exovim, and redesign the UI to feel phext-native. Ensure that we always render scrolls faithfully, and show the 9D coordinate in addition to the line and column. When starting a new scroll, show a scroll break indicator and the old and new coordinates. Suggest enhancements for inserting, removing, and moving scrolls easily.
Status: complete — PR #3 open against exovim-0.12; suggestions delivered to Will 2026-11-09

Notes:
- Will renamed the repo himself (wbic16/neovim -> wbic16/exovim) and renamed branch master -> exo; verified via API (exo exists, master gone). The in-flight fork agent (31.6.9) was redirected mid-flight: skip rename step, PR base exo, push to the renamed repo.
- Rename scope (Emise's boundary, to be reported plainly): all nvim references in the fork's OWN files (phext plugin tree, docs, messages, PHEXT.md) -> exovim; host API names (vim.api.nvim_*) cannot be renamed — they are the editor's API surface every plugin uses — and upstream-origin mentions stay factual.
- DONE (2026-11-09, verified by Emise via API: PR open): wbic16/exovim PR #3, base exovim-0.12 (the fork branch existed @ e4032456 at push time; UI branch rebased onto it, one PATCHES.md conflict resolved), head emise/phext-native-ui @ 89c7ad1f, 6 files +341/-20, 3 commits (rename / UI / docs). Tests: plain-Lua 62/62 (corpus grew to 15 files), headless 54/54 = 37 original unchanged + 17 new (open banner + scroll count; statusline contains 9D coord AND line,col; [+] dirty; per-scroll SHA-256 faithfulness over every scroll of a fixture; exact old->new banner; undotree unchanged across goto; opt-outs). The tests caught a real bug: Lua treats 0 as truthy, so the Vim-style g:phext_ui_banner=0 opt-out needed explicit reading. Costs honest: goto at agi scale 0.444 ms with banner+echo (budget 5), open+index 76 ms (budget 100). Module lives under the nvim.phext namespace on the 0.12 line; remaining 'nvim' occurrences are all host API names, the literal binary name in receipts, or upstream facts — inventoried in the report.

Results:
- PR https://github.com/wbic16/exovim/pull/3 (stacked on the exovim-0.12 fork PR; merge after it). Suggestions recorded in PHEXT.md 'Working with scrolls — proposed enhancements'.
