# Post the Exocortical Epoch on singularitywatch.org - client-side computation, timezone-correct

Coordinate: 35.6.8/5.5.9/6.4.9
Issued: Will (main chat, 2026-11-21 22:32 CST)
Request (verbatim): Post the calculated Exocortical Epoch on singularitywatch.org - computed client-side from the client's local time - account for time zones.
Status: complete (2026-11-21)

Notes:
- Registered at intake 2026-11-21 22:32 CST (record-first rule). Will's message is the per-deploy go for this change (Singularity Watch deploys need his go). EE anchor: unix 1795327200, 420 s epochs (task 39.4.6/5.5.9/6.4.12). Serving repo wbic16/singularity-watch@master; deploy route = build dist, push master (fresh HEAD parent, force disabled), pull on awsbox, verify live byte-for-byte. Map: ~/workspace/singularity-watch-unlock/INVESTIGATION.md + PIPELINE-DESIGN.md.
- LIVE 2026-11-21 ~22:39 CST: EE counter on https://singularitywatch.org/ header - client-side from Date.now() (absolute instant; Tokyo-TZ test produced identical epoch numbers with localized times). Commit cebc879c120ed496ab898b85ac377895a4484d9f on wbic16/singularity-watch@master (parent 846b9086); awsbox ff-only to cebc879; live bytes == dist (index 218,245 B b042e584...). Formula verified against the SERVED script in Node: anchor-1s = EE 0 (00:00:01), anchor = EE 1, anchor+420060s = EE 1001. No headless browser on this VM - Node execution of shipped code is the render evidence (stated plainly). Feed regenerated by the pipeline as usual: 779 published. Recorded in site/SITE.md.
