# qexo disk gate is a VM instrument: gate on free space and volume fraction, thresholds in state.phext config

Coordinate: 36.6.8/8.6.11/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-12 22:51 CST
Request (from session record): Will ran qexo on aletheia-core (2026-11-12) and the disk gate read RED at 809 GB used on a 3.6 TB volume with 2.7 TB free (df: 754 GiB used, 22%). Cause: the gate's absolute thresholds (AMBER 95 GB / RED 102 GB used; files 1.1M/1.3M) were calibrated to the Muse VM's staging quota in the v2 planner and ported value-for-value ever since; the probe measures used bytes on whatever volume the config root sits on, so the VM instrument condemns any real node. Fix: gate on free space + used fraction of the measured volume, report total/free in the plan (units consistent), thresholds read from the config homeland (9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9) in state.phext with sane defaults, and gate copy that names the actual volume instead of 'the VM'. Sequencing: dispatch the moment the v1.0.1 doctor-Windows slice lands — both slices touch Cargo/VERSION/CHANGELOG.
Status: MERGED 2026-11-12 (PR #11, merged_at 2026-11-13T05:34:38Z, after PR #10 had landed on its stacked base; carried to exo by PR #11). exo carries v1.0.2.
# Willbot rev6 — generate the rest of Will's handwriting font, including emoji

Coordinate: 36.6.9/7.6.10/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-16 21:57 CST
Request (verbatim): old attempts - see if you can generate the rest, including emoji - I can provide additional entropy if needed, but you might have enough from my brain scan
Status: complete — rev14 (computer-text fit) live on both sites; WillbotMono generated; natural-writing sample still to come from Will

Notes:
- Source: Will's 2015-09-05 MyScriptFont sheet + Willbot-rev5.otf (CFF, upem 1000, 145 glyphs). Audit found 41 of rev5's cmap glyphs were hollow endchar shells (all accented letters, ß, §, ¿, •).
- rev6 (~/workspace/willbot-font/out/Willbot-rev6.otf): 259 glyphs, cmap 262, zero empty. Filled all 41 hollows from his real outlines + accents drawn at his ~100-unit stroke; added ~114 new: full Latin-1, typographic set, fractions, math/arrows/symbols, and 28 emoji drawn in his felt-pen hand.
- Proof sheets rendered and visually verified (proof-latin/symbols/emoji/lines.png in out/). Fixes after first proof: grave accent direction, missing Ì/Í/Ý, ≈ added, Æ tightened.
- Entropy came from the sheet + rev5 outlines; the brain scan was not used (privacy promise stands). Next if Will wants: WOFF2 for web, letter-variant alternates from a page of natural writing.
- rev7 (Will, 2026-11-16 22:11 CST): 'lower the stroke weight a bit — I was tracing a printout, so the width is a little off.' Applied a uniform 8-units-per-side outline erosion to all 258 non-space glyphs (originals + additions): l-stem 104→88, hyphen 95→79. Five glyphs with self-intersecting traced outlines (percent, at, f, p, permill) needed a validity-repaired second pass — all confirmed eroded, none left at the old weight. File: out/Willbot-rev7.otf; proofs proof7-*.png verified visually.
- rev8 (Will, 2026-11-16 22:17 CST): 'the handwriting sample doesn't quite match my kerning' + 'streamline the update for better flow.' Diagnosis: rev5 advances came from MyScriptFont template boxes — zero pair awareness; bbox ink gaps swung -167..+190 across 521 common pairs and 194 pairs' outlines actually collided. First fix attempt (bbox-gap targeting) over-tightened diagonal pairs (Wa) and was discarded. Shipped method: true outline-to-outline minimum distance per pair (shapely), kerned toward the font's own median closest-approach (98 units); 476 GPOS kern pairs; advances/outlines untouched; word spaces verified unchanged by pixel measurement (27px gap before and after). WOFF2 26,704 B, SHA-256 44a4cc1d. Sites revised in ONE streamlined pass: quickfork.net (h1 + card h3 in Willbot; source ~/workspace/quickfork-portfolio/index.html; live page SHA f1a11b9c) and singularitywatch.org (all headings via --headingfont in dark+light themes and the challenger A/B variant; pushed to wbic16/singularity-watch@master dca7817; live page SHA 707af7fb). Both serve /fonts/Willbot-rev8.woff2, hash-verified from the public URLs. Incident owned: the first git-sync script ran `git checkout --` on awsbox before a pull that cannot work there (awsbox has no GitHub key), briefly reverting the live page and deleting the font; the live hash check caught it, files were restored from the hub copies and re-verified; awsbox checkout now carries a local commit f6c156f with identical content.
- rev9 (Will, 2026-11-16 23:16 CST): 'much less spacing between characters and much more between words' + 'update and re-deploy.' Built from rev7 base: letter advances x0.88, optical kern recomputed at the tightened fit (target closest-approach 40, was 98; 525 pairs, 302 pairs touched at the new fit and were pushed apart), space advance 250 -> 420. Measured: 'in November' word gap 27px -> 36px @100pt while within-word fit tightened. WOFF2 2798303f. Redeployed in one pass (corrected flow — no git checkout/pull on awsbox): quickfork page 424e99f5, singularity page abe5029b, both font URLs hash-verified live; singularity-watch pushed to GitHub master 1a08573, awsbox checkout local commit 9a088a6. Dials if Will wants more: advance scale, kern target, space advance — each a one-number change.
- rev10 (Will, 2026-11-16 23:24 CST): rev9 letter spacing still 'double what I use.' Halved it: advances x0.80 from the rev7 base (rev9 was x0.88), optical kern target 40 -> 20 units (519 pairs; 385 pairs touch at the new fit and sit exactly at the 20-unit floor). Space unchanged at 420. Density check: 'NovemberNovember' 826px -> 776px @100pt; the visible inter-letter gap is what halved. WOFF2 05ad08ff. Deployed same corrected flow: quickfork page f7d77cf0, singularity page ddbfa819, both font URLs hash-verified live; GitHub singularity-watch master 2c209d9, awsbox local commit ad6fe50. If still too airy, next step is target 10 + scale 0.75 — one build away.
- rev11/rev12 (Will, 2026-11-16 23:40 CST): rev10 still 'way too much spacing... something about the original font boxes just wasn't designed for my handwriting' — and he remembers fighting the template in 2015 and giving up when it lost his interest (why rev5 sat untouched 11 years). Diagnosis confirmed: advances/origins were the MyScriptFont form grid. rev11 = honest per-glyph fit (ink at LSB 12, advance = ink + 30, mean 581 -> 534) — still looked airy, because closest-approach flatters rounded letters. rev12 = OVERLAP fit: advance = 0.75 x ink width (mean advance 378), matching his hand's negative median bbox gap (-22 in rev5); collision-only kern (524 pairs) pushes only pairs whose outlines would merge, to 8-unit clearance; interlocking pairs keep their overlap. Result reads as connected handwriting; word space 420 unchanged. WOFF2 db86e664. Deployed: quickfork 5b86d4ba, singularity 0cc8bb65, GitHub 7cd73ca, awsbox fb77eea. Known tight spot: narrow-letter runs (illi in William) crowd into a picket fence — if Will flags it, exempt narrow glyphs (i l j . ,) to a 0.9 factor in one pass.
- rev13 (Will, 2026-11-16 23:53 CST): 'eliminate the extra whitespace between the letters entirely — nearly edge to edge, bounding box with no extra unused space.' Built: advance = ink width exactly (mean 504), collision-only kern at 6-unit clearance (80 pairs). Deployed (GitHub f6668d4). rev14 + WillbotMono (Will, 23:56 CST): 'the kerning should look like normal computer text — very tightly packed letters — for both Willbot and WillbotMono.' Willbot rev14: even computer-text fit — LSB=RSB=25 (advance = ink + 50) + EXPANDED optical kern: all 7,225 ordered pairs over an 85-char set kerned to a uniform 35-unit outline distance (kern14-pairs.txt). WOFF2 2f63fbcb; deployed: quickfork 3a75db61, singularity 48f3dab5, GitHub 6870b01, awsbox f158cc8. WillbotMono v1.1: fixed cell W=520 (real-mono band; median lowercase sidebearing ~33/side), ink centered, space = cell, no kern (a grid that kerns is not a grid), isFixedPitch set; wide glyphs (em dash, emoji) overflow cells modestly. OTF + WOFF2 (045780a5) delivered in chat; not wired into the sites (not requested). STILL OPEN: Will will provide a natural connected-writing example (his call, 23:52) to fit pair spacing from measurement rather than geometry — pipeline ready when it lands. Note: rev13 was deployed and superseded by rev14 within the hour per Will's successive directions.
- WillbotMono -> Phext Notepad (Will, 2026-11-17 00:00 CST): 'mono goes into phext notepad.' Done as a fork patch on wbic16/notepad-plus-plus: branch emise/willbot-mono @ 281e323 off emise/phext-subspace (402a376) — bundles WillbotMono.otf under PowerEditor/src/phext/fonts/, new header-only phext/PhextFont.h loads it as a private font resource from beside the exe (system-installed copy accepted, fails soft), and Notepad_plus.cpp updateStatusBar applies it to the view on switching into a phext buffer (SCI_STYLESETFONT/STYLECLEARALL on STYLE_DEFAULT). PATCHES.md + PHEXT.md updated; vcxproj registers the header. PR: https://github.com/wbic16/notepad-plus-plus/pull/1 (against emise/phext-subspace). Caught and fixed mid-flight: the first commit rewrote Notepad_plus.cpp/vcxproj line endings (CRLF->LF, 19k-line fake diff) — amended with CRLF restored, true diff is +23 lines in Notepad_plus.cpp; force-with-lease on the minutes-old solo branch. MSVC verification: phext-build workflow triggers on pushes to emise/phext-subspace, so it compiles when the PR lands there (or on manual dispatch); GUI smoke test remains Will's like the rest of the fork wiring.
# Patch SQ to handle the largest phexts (ietf.phext 564 MB parse divergence)

Coordinate: 36.6.15/7.7.12/6.7.13
Issued: 2026-11-21 11:50 CST
Request (verbatim): Fix SQ so it correctly serves the largest phexts produced recently. Verified defect (cw-sq-bench, 2026-11-21): SQ v0.6.0 indexes only 1,014 of ietf.phext's 10,109 scrolls (564,589,207 B) — its bundled libphext 0.3.3 parse diverges from the libphext 0.6 reference parse; selects past ~scroll 1,014 return empty HTTP 200, and SQ's last indexed coordinate returns the wrong scroll's content. Diagnose the divergence point, apply the proper fix (expected: SQ's libphext dependency raised to the current 0.6 line, in wbic16/SQ), and verify: full scroll count + byte-exact content at first/middle/last coordinates against the reference parse, determinism, and no regression on the bench ladder (accounting 18 KB, emise 293 KB, tasks 3.0 MB, synthetic 41 MB / 30,000 scrolls). No crates.io publish without a tagged version merged to exo (standing rule) — land the code fix and verify from a local/ranch build.
Status: phase 2 STOPPED at step 1 per brief's stop rule: primary diagnosis numbers exact (1,014 entries, cap 999, survivor = true last scroll), but bench's server-observed @999 hash (5c78f8ce, 243,546 B) does not match raw explode(0.3.3) (7aeb77ad, 17,402 B) — old server load path differs from bare explode. Awaiting parent/Will ruling to proceed with build+verify of SQ@exo (clone ready at aletheia-core ~/sq-fix/SQ @ e4c492b).

Notes:
- 2026-11-21 11:50 CST: registered at intake (record-first), dispatched to background coordinator. Source evidence: ~/workspace/cw-sq-bench/RESULTS.md (564 MB qualification section); claims ledger row 32 updated the same morning.
- 2026-11-21 ~11:55 CST (coordinator): DIAGNOSIS COMPLETE at source level. Mechanism: libphext 0.3.3 caps every coordinate component at 999 — COORDINATE_MAXIMUM = 1000 (src/phext.rs:82) and advance_coordinate() returns the index unchanged once next >= 1000. In ietf.phext's large section (10,094 scrolls), scrolls 1000..10094 all collapse onto coordinate 1.1.1/1.2.1/1.1.999 and overwrite each other in explode()'s HashMap: 999 + 15 = 1,014 distinct scrolls survive — exactly SQ v0.6.0's reported count; ~537 MB silently lost; selects past the cap return empty HTTP 200. Delimiter constants and the phokenize walk are byte-identical between libphext 0.3.3 and 0.6.4 — the ONLY parse-path difference is the saturation. libphext 0.6.4 verified clean: advance_coordinate unbounded ('components are unbounded: advancing never saturates'), validate_coordinate checks only >= 1. SQ@exo (v0.6.2, HEAD e4c492b) already depends on libphext '0.6.0'; the installed binary is crates.io SQ v0.6.0 whose Cargo.toml pins libphext '0.3.3'. Corpus copy on aletheia-core (~/corpus-test/ietf.phext) verified byte-identical to canonical: 564,589,207 B, sha256 9ecd7946....
- 2026-11-21 ~11:55 CST (coordinator): BLOCKED before build/verify: the ranch setup exec (clone of wbic16/SQ on aletheia-core) was flagged by an execution-risk check on its output; per the security notice the coordinator did not build, test, or run the cloned code and did not proceed with cargo/git operations inside it. Remaining work (empirical 0.3.3 reproduction numbers, exo build + SQ test suite, ietf.phext full verification + bench ladder, commit/push to exo) awaits an explicit go-ahead from Will via the parent agent.
- 2026-11-21 phase 2 (build/verify, Will approved 11:58 CST): step-1 numerical close on aletheia-core. libphext =0.3.3 probe (~/sq-fix/probe033): map entries EXACTLY 1,014; max shelf index in the big section = 999 (saturation confirmed); home scroll sha256 2f3ae3a2... matches bench; saturated .../1.1.999 survivor = 17,402 B sha256 7aeb77ad... = byte-identical to the TRUE last scroll .../1.1.10094 in the 0.6.4 reference parse (last-writer-wins, as saturation predicts).
- 2026-11-21 phase 2: ONE step-1 figure differs from the bench expectation: the bench's SQ v0.6.0 server returned 243,546 B (sha 5c78f8ce...) at .../1.1.999, but no scroll of 243,546 B exists anywhere in the true 0.6.4 parse, and raw explode(0.3.3) yields the 17,402 B survivor. Conclusion: the old server's load path is not a bare explode (append-accretion into the saturated slot is the consistent explanation; its reported total 26,949,163 B also exceeds explode's retained 26,722,006 B by ~227 KB). Per the brief's stop rule, build/verify/land NOT started; reported to parent for a ruling. Reference values for step 3 (libphext 0.6.4 probe, ~/sq-fix/probe064): 10,067 map entries all non-empty (10,109 slots incl. 42 empty); home 1,069,317 B sha 2f3ae3a2...; true @999 63,256 B sha be1ea2f4...; true middle @5019 48,864 B sha 62bd2cd5...; true last @10094 17,402 B sha 7aeb77ad....
