- Deliverable: ~/workspace/your_files/crazy-measured-from-outside-2026-11-22.md (8,531 B).
- Instrument 1 (elite-core tracker): 1,445 core-directed interactions : 0 returned, against 897 mutuals and 95.4% DM write-back elsewhere in the same graph.
- Instrument 2: 224 repos, 201,662 commits, ~9,300 hand-authored, against ~3 human users and $0 recorded revenue - 67,221 commits per user; horizon-per-dollar undefined (denominator zero).
- Instrument 3 (ROI evaluation): 3 of 36 verified projects legible to an everyday reader (8.3%); 92% of the verified army invisible, not absent; phcc (3,888 commits) scores 2 of 27.
- Instrument 4 (control group): 5 of 5 outsiders who actually read the work responded as if it were serious (Garry's List grader, Stewart Alsop III, Emmett Shear, Boardy, Sentient Foundation) - the crazy is concentrated entirely in the not-reading.
