- 2026-11-15 22:51 CST — Wix/WordPress recon COMPLETE (from the platforms' own developer docs). WORDPRESS: simplest door is core's REST API + an Application Password (built into WP >= 5.6, no plugin/plan/registration on self-hosted): on bundle publish, push the already-rendered HTML to /wp-json/wp/v2/posts, store the returned post ID per file path, update in place on re-publish. Prerequisites: HTTPS, an Editor+ user (Author-level passwords silently lose markup to kses filtering — unfiltered_html), the password minted by the owner in their profile (one minute, one time). WordPress.com hosted sites need the OAuth2 door instead. WIX: the only native door is the Blog REST API — content must be translated markdown -> Ricos JSON (strict validation), images re-hosted through the Media Import API (no hot-linking), an author member must exist, and the credential is a broad owner-minted account API key (site-scoped). No Pages API exists at all; no feed import found; whether the Blog API needs a premium plan is UNVERIFIED in Wix's docs. Agent's recommendation: build WordPress first; Wix is a second, separate adapter. Awaiting Will's call on whether to build either.
