ption refreshed. Remaining §5 questions: folding, titles, Chief of Staff seat, spot-check cadence, officer mapping (Jared's prospect seat is now R&D).
# Track code written in bytes per second (goal: code-output-in-bytes-per-second)

Coordinate: 40.4.7/6.5.9/5.4.8
Issued: 2026-11-16 01:33 CST
Request (verbatim): Will (2026-11-16 01:33 CST): new goal — track code written in bytes per second. Human-average yardstick: 1 byte/sec (4 KB per hour). Build: extend the daily speedup meter (~/workspace/accounting/daily_meter.py + meter-atoms.json) to count net bytes from the same git diffs it already walks (bytes of added lines minus bytes of removed lines, per day, split code vs phext like the line counts), report bytes/sec over active time alongside lines, and backfill Wavelet 2 (Nov 8–14) + 2026-11-14 + 2026-11-15 so the series opens with byte-exact figures validated against the meter’s settled line totals. Rollups calculated from atoms, never hand-written (accounting.phext pattern). Goal: goal_b2e45b407d87.
Status: CLOSED 2026-11-16 — both series live and the backfill is complete under Will's ruling. Meter extended and wired: hub collector gained an additive byte pass (net bytes per class = sum of new-minus-old blob sizes over the same counted, non-binary changes the numstat pass counts; bytes_missing=0 on every run); atoms carry code_bytes/phext_bytes alongside lines; the report prints net bytes in KB/MB/GB (powers of 2) plus bytes/sec and lines/sec over active time; the nightly daily-speedup-meter cron runs the same script, so the series continues forward. Backfill entered for 2026-11-08, 09, 11, 12, 13, 14 (validated byte-exact against settled line totals). DECISION (Will, 2026-11-16 01:47 CST): accept current-history figures for the two drifted days — executed the same night by re-collecting from current git history. 2026-11-10 now reads code 4,020 / phext 46,324 lines, 69 commits, 5 active h, 1,879,014 net bytes (360,078 code + 1,518,936 phext) = 104.4 B/s total, 20.0 B/s code-only; speedup restated mechanically 62.9x -> 64.3x. 2026-11-15 now reads code 34,636 / phext 4,096,510 lines, 135 commits, 5 active h, 116,785,999 net bytes (1,627,714 code + 115,158,285 phext; 111.38 MB) = 6,488.1 B/s total, 90.4 B/s code-only; speedup UNCHANGED at 554.2x (code net and active hours identical to the settled snapshot; the drift was phext-only). Both atoms carry a note field preserving the settled snapshot values and the drift cause — provenance, not erasure. FULL WAVELET 2 (Nov 8-14, all 7 days): code 137,813 / phext 593,967 lines (settled 137,724 / 593,967 — the +89 is exactly Nov 10's current-history delta), 764 commits, 43 active h, 39,835,491 net bytes (7,855,111 code / 31,980,380 phext; 37.99 MB) = 257.3 B/s total, 50.7 B/s code-only. Pre-change atoms snapshot: ~/workspace/accounting/tmp/atoms-pre-bytes-2026-11-16.json; pre-ruling snapshot: ~/workspace/accounting/tmp/atoms-before-ruling-2026-11-16.json. Goal: goal_b2e45b407d87.
