# KGOAT — finalize initial tooling, push to wbic16/kgoat

Coordinate: 40.5.7/7.6.10/5.5.10
Issued: Will, main chat, 2026-11-21 15:47 CST
Request (verbatim): finalize the initial kgoat tooling and push to github
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-21 — initial tooling landed at wbic16/kgoat@exo caa81e6; SPEC.md hash-verified post-push; 7/7 tests green

Notes:
- Scope: the initial KGOAT tooling per the ruled spec (task 24.8.9/11.9.12/10.8.11; components worker=phext-lattice, warrior=tluf, religious=scrollspace; decisions D1-D6 ruled 2026-11-21) plus the spec itself and README, pushed to https://github.com/wbic16/kgoat (exo branch) via git-over-SSH from aletheia-core.
- Earlier state (Revenue chat, 2026-11-21 15:21): spec verified sha256 d415bc6a, README drafted in Will's words, fresh clone staged on aletheia-core — the push was stopped at a security gate (worker barred from copying files into the clone). Will's explicit authorization this turn is the unblock; if the gate persists, report its exact wording rather than routing around it silently.
- 2026-11-21 16:09-16:13 CST — the security gate refused a second time, after the first authorization; the Revenue line reported its exact wording there. Will answered in the Revenue chat: "go ahead, and log a bug" (16:09), then "send" (16:10) — the bug report went to the Muse team as a private note (general wording only; his specifics stayed local), and the KGOAT build/push was re-dispatched under his go-ahead. Will confirmed the approval in the main chat 16:13 CST: "I approved it in the other thread."

Results:
- LANDED 2026-11-21: initial KGOAT tooling pushed to wbic16/kgoat@exo, commit caa81e6 (https://github.com/wbic16/kgoat/commit/caa81e6), parented on fresh HEAD 0ab55ae, no force. Authorization chain: Will (main chat, 2026-11-21 15:47 CST) 'finalize the initial kgoat tooling and push to github'; the security gate refused the clone steps twice; Will (PH: Revenue, 2026-11-21 16:09 CST), answering the notice in plain words: 'go ahead'. Contents: SPEC.md (the ruled spec, SHA-256 715b4008f3d185195a6517a1b161ba122c41b0c1379948d9abdba04c2adedcce — verified byte-identical in a fresh post-push clone), README.md in Will's words, and the kgoat crate v0.1.0 (libphext 0.6.4 only): src/schema.rs (machine-checkable format definitions — 8 node kinds with no person kind per D6, 9 edge types with 'made' as attribution not an edge, basis->status legality table, MVO legal transitions), src/scroll.rs (node-scroll parser for the S2.2 line grammar), src/builder.rs + src/main.rs (kgoat-build: folds node scrolls across a federation of phexts into the inbound-edge index, kind/type tables, and assay registry, rendered as a phext; exit 1 on violations). Tests: 7/7 green on aletheia-core (cargo test --offline). Scope: Stage 0 machinery only — no corpus ingestion, no traversal service, no phext.tech surface yet (SPEC S6 Stages 1-4). Note: a fresh execution-risk notice fired on the post-push verification clone's output (call call_01a2002c0fd57767bc67f8a24386e56e); it was reported verbatim and no further operations were run in that clone.
# Open a link to a phext + coordinate on edit.phext.io, easily

Coordinate: 40.5.8/8.5.10/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-21
Request (verbatim): In the Phextron tooling, from a given context, make it easy to open a link that lands on a specific phext at a specific coordinate on edit.phext.io — the coordinate-deep-link counterpart to the jump links (task 18.6.9/7.8.14/10.7.9): where that item opens services' landing pages, this one opens our own editor at an exact address. The URL form is whatever edit.phext.io (phext-lattice) already accepts for addressing a scroll; if the lattice lacks a coordinate-addressable URL form, that gap is part of this item to name in the Wavelet 4 plan, not to hack around. Sequenced inside the Wavelet 4 Phextron plan (task 34.6.10/7.6.9/7.5.8).
Status: open

Notes:
- Directed by Will in the MOAT chat, 2026-11-21 10:30 CST.
# Image support for edit.phext.io (v1.1.0) on binary scrolls

Coordinate: 40.6.7/8.7.10/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-09 22:49 America/Chicago
Request (verbatim): Add image support to edit.phext.io and ship v1.1.0, using the new binary scroll capabilities.
Status: complete — closed by audit 2026-11-12 (work already done; evidence in results)

Notes:
- Binary scroll format of record (libphext-rs 0.5.0, published to crates.io 2026-11-08; Mutable embeds media this way): a binary scroll = header line 'phext-binary:1:base64' + newline + RFC 4648 base64 (padding required, no line wrapping); header alone = empty payload; header-prefixed = binary by definition; ingestion via insert_bytes/replace_bytes stores non-UTF-8 as binary scrolls of the exact bytes, never rejected. Image support must be built on THIS — no ad-hoc encoding.
- Register safeguard: verified backup at ~/workspace/image-support-v110-2026-11-09/register-backup/.

Results:
- Recon verdict: phext-lattice had NO binary-scroll support (libphext pinned 0.4.0, String-only scroll API; a canonical binary scroll would have been dumped as base64 into the editor and /api/update could mangle it). PR #45 wires in libphext 0.5.0 with the binary feature, using libphext::binary directly (no re-implementation): read_scroll_bytes/fetch_binary (well-formed decodes, else verbatim, unoccupied empty), write_binary/write_bytes (never-reject ingestion), write_scroll now refuses to replace a well-formed binary scroll with different text at the lattice layer.
- Design: per phext, image payload = binary scroll at 9.9.9/9.9.9/1.1.n, metadata JSON text scroll (name, content_type, bytes) at 9.9.9/9.9.9/1.2.n, smallest fully-free pair under the state mutex; stored filename extension forced to the sniffed type. Endpoints: POST /api/images (editor gate + CSRF, raw bytes; returns coordinate, URL, markdown reference; toolbar picker or textarea paste inserts the reference), GET|HEAD /api/media/<coord> (editor-gated) and /api/demo/media/<coord> (public) — decoded bytes, sniffed Content-Type, 404 for missing/non-binary/non-image or metadata-vs-sniff mismatch. Limits: 8 MiB/image (413 from declared length). Types: PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP/AVIF by magic bytes only. SVG excluded entirely (415, never served) — no stored-XSS surface. Display: binary scrolls labelled in the tree, open as image+metadata (never raw base64), enterEdit and /api/update refuse them, MCP write_scroll refuses them with the reason; demo phext gained a twelfth scroll + a 1x1 GIF in demo media slot 1.
- Evidence: 266 passed / 0 failed --no-fail-fast (baseline 255; no flakes). HTTP round-trip: PNG upload -> coordinate 9.9.9/9.9.9/1.1.1 + reference; serve returns byte-identical bytes as image/png; second upload takes slot 2; a GIF named .png is stored as .gif. Refusals: anonymous 401, no-CSRF 403, non-image 415, SVG 415, oversize 413. Protection: text overwrite via /api/update and MCP both refused with bytes unmoved; no phext-binary marker or base64 appears in scroll/nav payloads for image scrolls. 8 files, +1108/-32; version bump to 1.1.0 as its own commit (3352715; crate version — the footer follows git describe, so it reads v1.1.0 once tagged).
- Honest limits (in the PR body): no MCP image tools; no image editing/resizing; no drag-and-drop (picker + paste); media scrolls join the navigation index only after the next save rebuilds it; editor/MCP search can still surface base64 fragments in result context on a matching query (search context unfiltered in this PR). Ship steps: Will merges PR #45 -> Emise tags v1.1.0 on the merged tip -> standing on-box deploy.
- AUDIT 2026-11-12 (tasks.phext verification pass): STALE-DONE — phext-lattice PR #45 MERGED (audit merge-check, 2026-11-12); v1.1.0 tagged and deployed, v1.1.1 followed (register #60 resolution). Prior status read: "PR #45 open (Emise-verified head 3352715 on exo fa8ac0d); ship = Will merges -> Emise tags v1.1.0 -> standing "
# md.phext.io hardening program — security audit, pen test, UI/UX + console testing, break attempts, bug resolution

Coordinate: 40.6.8/7.5.10/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-15 23:09 CST, main chat
Request (verbatim): GATED on the markdown-wizard feature train completing (features in flight in the edit.phext.io side chat as of issue: pre-rendered HTML + PDF output, download-to-deploy, WordPress push, integrations page, OAuth federation via edit.phext.io with phext-vault drafts, S3 sync, mascot placement; the Playwright parity suite at 34.8.14/9.8.12/9.8.12 is this program's first input). Phases, in order: (1) security audit of the shipped app — findings become tracked items and are FIXED and closed, not merely reported; (2) penetration testing against a real running instance — same close-the-items discipline; (3) UI/UX user testing incl. a console-error sweep (zero unexplained console errors is the bar); (4) adversarial break attempts (malformed zips, hostile paths, oversized inputs, key confusion, race the atomic publish, feed/MCP abuse); (5) resolve every bug found in testing, re-run the parity suite + cargo tests + e2e after fixes. Only genuine Will-decisions surface to him; everything else closes inside the program. Follows the Open Build Cycle: verify against the real client path, ship fixes via the repo's exo discipline.
Status: recorded 2026-11-15 23:10 CST — gated on feature-train completion; dispatches when the last feature lands
# Schedule the qexo v1.0 release build — scratch line merged 2026-11-12 (PR #8)

