Request (verbatim): Will's standing rule (2026-11-12): every merge into Rust tooling queues a release task in the same session. Trigger: the qexo distributed-builds change (v1.7.0) merged by Will 2026-11-15 02:09-02:10 CST — wbic16/quarterexo PR #26 (https://github.com/wbic16/quarterexo/pull/26, merge commit 5e8fa235e1) and wbic16/qexo PR #5 (https://github.com/wbic16/qexo/pull/5, merge commit 03f996199b); the companion tree change wbic16/exocortical PR #6 (https://github.com/wbic16/exocortical/pull/6, merge commit 52151b76fa) merged in the same pass. Release legs: (a) tag v1.7.0 from the merged exo tree of wbic16/quarterexo and mirror the tag to wbic16/qexo, the twin home; (b) release build on a ranch node, aletheia-core first; (c) crates.io publish ONLY from the tagged, merged-to-exo tree, if a publish is part of this release — never publish from an unmerged branch or an untagged tree; (d) fleet normalization: nodes replace the staged ~/qexo-v170 binaries via `qexo update` so the distributed-builds command becomes permanent fleet-wide.
Status: v1.8.0 SHIP PREPARED AND STAGED 2026-11-17 (re-scoped from the held v1.7.1-line release; dispatch core aboard) — PRs quarterexo #37 / qexo #7 MERGED 2026-11-18 (GitHub-verified 2026-11-22, W2: qexo PR #7 merge commit 6f549730 = current exo head; quarterexo PR #37 merge-check 204); tags, crates.io publish, and fleet rollout remain Will-timed; rollout closing proof still waits on the section 10.4 credential leg (Will's awsbox steps).

Notes:
- Parent work: distributed-builds task 25.5.7/7.6.9/6.5.9 (closed 2026-11-15 ~02:05 CST), whose Stage 4 rollout staged v1.7.0 per node as ~/qexo-v170 pending exactly this release. Once leg (d) lands, the staged binaries and the --branch emise/distributed-builds workaround from Stage 4 are retired.
- UNHOLD TRIGGER FIRED (2026-11-17): slice 3 merged to quarterexo@exo (7d3363a) and register@exo (4d00296) — the register integration the v1.7.x rollout was held for is in. Release packaging still follows the slice order (version bump is slice 8); no unilateral fleet rollout — Will times the rollout.
- SLICE 8 EXECUTED THE RE-SCOPED SHIP'S PREPARATION (2026-11-17): the release is v1.8.0 — the dispatch core (slices 1-7, incl. the register integration this task was held for) at a new-minor stamp on both repos. Packaged + gated + staged on aletheia-core at ~/qexo-build-v1.8.0/fleet-build/ (SHA256SUMS; Linux/exe/Android/APK — launcher v3's first APK, versionCode 5). Gates: cargo 159/159 both trees, package --list 39, publish --dry-run clean, all slice packs green, upgrade exercise 20/20 from v1.6.1-born and v1.7.1-born states. PRs awaiting Will's merges: https://github.com/wbic16/quarterexo/pull/37 and https://github.com/wbic16/qexo/pull/7. Remaining legs are Will-timed: (a) v1.8.0 tags on the merged exo trees (post-merge script prepared, tree-hash verified against the gated trees), (c) crates.io publish, (d) fleet rollout via the signed channel — whose closing proof (a fleet node draining the real register) still requires the section 10.4 credential leg on awsbox. The staged v1.7.1 binaries and the Stage-4 --branch workaround retire when leg (d) lands. Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/dispatch-slice8/BUILD-RECORD.md.
- Gate cleared 2026-11-17: slice 8 (v1.8.0) merged to both exo branches (see task 26.5.9 note). Release leg is now the live step: publish v1.8.0 + signer-first fleet rollout, fix /source/exocortical checkout to exo 52151b7, mirror tags to twin wbic16/qexo.
- 2026-11-22 RECONCILED (qexo production programme, W2): Status corrected: the slice-8 PRs this record said 'await Will's merges' are both merged (see 26.5.9/7.6.11/5.5.10 reconciliation note, same date). The staged/Will-timed release clauses were and remain accurate. Evidence: ~/workspace/qexo-production/W2-RECONCILE.md.
