Coordinate: 40.16.11/20.9.27/7.10.10
Issued: 2026-11-17 05:29 CST
Request (verbatim): Clone https://github.com/huggingface/pybot (a ~640k-line pure-Python rule-based chatbot written by a swarm of 1,000+ agents) on a ranch node, census it, and apply the Computronium treatment: function-level de-duplication measurement plus an actual compaction (canonical function pool + standoff skeletons). Report how far the tree collapses and how the ratio compares with the Chromium census.
Status: complete — measured 2026-11-17; see result

Notes:
- Will sent the repo link 2026-11-17 05:27 CST with no text; Emise read it and offered the census; Will: 'yes, clone, compact, and measure: see if we can do better' (05:29 CST).
- Repo claims (README, unverified until census): ~640k lines of bot code in 528 files + ~550k lines of tests; knowledge base 317k lines of facts-as-data; memory store 109k; arbiter picks among module proposals per turn; SmolTalkBench win rate 26% after 5,000+ swarm versions.
- Placement: fair draw (Will, 2026-11-16) among eligible nodes drew orchid-flow; rock-mountain (SMOL resident), ashfall-haven (Exo), quacked-hill (Corus), aletheia-core (coordinator) excluded from the draw.
- Emise's pre-measurement bet (regex/lookup code would collapse hard under dedup) was WRONG — owned to Will in the delivery message; the swarm tree is bespoke at function grain.
