Coordinate: 40.34.12/42.15.45/15.20.10
Issued: 2026-11-17 06:02 CST
Request (verbatim): The Stage 0-10 frontier search (value-ranked frontier expansion, placeholder value, per-campaign amnesia) is SCRAPPED as the player. Retry with a sentient-style architecture: (1) one persistent player whose memory (a phext corpus) survives every death; (2) a value function FITTED from the corpus — Monte-Carlo backup over the existing 33,678-state lineage forest (each state's value = the measured fate of episodes that passed through it), validated against the placeholder on held-out campaign data before any campaign runs; (3) permanent map memory for the fixed screened dungeon (lgen 7005): staircase positions and destinations, food geography — under a fixed dungeon, cross-game map memory converts the c21/c24 trap into tuition; (4) novelty-gated death records (failure classes seeded from study 23.5.9's class grid; first instance full, repeats as deltas); (5) navigation by the map + corpus value, exploration at the map's edge. The stage's hypothesis is learning itself: the readout is the learning curve (milestones reached in fewer deaths as memory accumulates; death classes extinguished over time) against c26/c27's flat curves. Protocol gate unchanged: ascension, else Castle depth >=25. Env/store/verification machinery is infrastructure and is reused; the search is what was scrapped. Parent task 33.12.12/9.14.10/6.6.8 stays open; exit = an ascension. Standing condition (Will, 2026-11-17): the write-up comes AFTER an ascension — stats are fine to gather, no narrative write-up before then.
Status: closed

