Request (verbatim): https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.38214
Status: complete 2026-11-07

Notes:
- Paper 006 for the R&D tracker: 'Skeleton Coding: Program Structure as a Specification for Agents' (Golatkar, Achille, Zabounidis, Sobal, Ding, Ray, Buck, Van den Broeck, Fazel, Perona, Xia, Soatto), arXiv:2610.38214 [cs.SE], submitted 28 Oct 2026. Chapter 10 of research.phext. First ingestion under charter rules 13 (state machine pass) and 14 (MVO classification + Lean re-proof).
- INGESTED as Chapter 10 (10.1.1-10.3.1): 8 new concepts 1.2.57-1.2.64 (cluster I 'Specification as control'), 1 revision (1.2.14), 5 foundations 1.3.87-1.3.91, narrative v8. NI = 8.5/64 ≈ 0.13, NOT axis-opening (a bridge paper); Oracle ~35% (25-45%), up from ~25%. Q20-Q23 added. State machines M1-M4 stated by the paper, M5-M6 inferred [synthesis]. MVO Pass #2 ran (64 concepts ≥ 60 trigger): no merges/splits/retirements. Registry 221 = 221 scrolls: True 116 (stipulation 108, verified 8), Unknown 105 (attributed 88, synthesis 10, open 6, estimate 1), False 0, Fiction 0; Lean instance re-proved over 221 entries, axioms propext/Quot.sound only. research.phext 221 scrolls, sha256 824917aeef7789827d6283ee3ad221a2c9f232aae266bc2cf3604a5bdac39ac3, Singular residual 0.
