# Ship Phext Notepad updates — perf stack + libphext v0.6 switch

Coordinate: 41.7.8/9.9.14/7.7.11
Issued: 2026-11-15 10:53 CST
Request (verbatim): Will's direction (2026-11-15 10:53 CST, edit.phext.io chat): ship the wbic16/phext-notepad update stack, especially the performance enhancements (emise/perf-sparse-load) and the switch to libphext v0.6. Stack per the 2026-11-08 review: PR #4 (cursor/native-phext-notepad-ad0b, native FLTK app) -> emise/perf-sparse-load -> PR #5 (emise/ultra-open-fix, libphext-cs 0.5.0 from NuGet) and emise/edit-sync -> emise/desktop-sso. Live check 2026-11-15: all branch heads match the 2026-11-08 record except ultra-open-fix, advanced to f8c45eb651 by the libphext-cs commits; exo at 4ffc24cb99; PRs #4/#5 open; perf/edit-sync/desktop-sso have no PRs. Plan: verify stack + tests on the ranch, open the missing PRs, merge in stack order, then cut the libphext 0.6 switch (Rust libphext 0.6.0; check libphext-cs 0.6 availability) off the merged exo, test, PR, merge.
Status: stack shipped 2026-11-15 — PR #4 (native app), PR #6 (perf pass), PR #7 (edit-sync), PR #8 (desktop-sso) merged to exo in order; exo head 4590f024; merged branches cursor/native-phext-notepad-ad0b, emise/edit-sync, emise/desktop-sso deleted per Will's 2026-11-15 stale-branch rule; emise/perf-sparse-load kept as PR #5's base. Post-merge exo test verification dispatched. REMAINING: PR #5 (ultra-open-fix) held until libphext-cs 0.6.0 publishes to NuGet (ports push, 2026-11-15); the libphext v0.6 switch rides with PR #5's landing because the native 0.3.1 -> 0.5.0 adaptation lives on that branch — at landing, bump both pins to 0.6.0 (csproj + Cargo), resolve the known 3-file native conflict mechanically (keep the higher pin, keep all module lines, regenerate the lockfile), retest the full tree on the ranch, then merge. Post-merge verification (2026-11-15, aletheia-core): exo @ 4590f024 cargo test --workspace 33 passed, 0 failed, zero warnings; libphext pin on merged exo confirmed 0.3.1 (the 0.5.0 adaptation is only in PR #5, as expected; the 33 vs 47 test difference is ultra's own seal/binary tests, which land with PR #5 — no regression).

Notes:
- RENEWED by Will, 2026-11-21 10:25 CST: 'finish Phext Notepad performance enhancements' — with added scope recorded on task 46.2.2/2.2.4/2.2.6 (inline editor for inspecting managed phexts; git assist). Will approved moving the perf branch forward on 2026-11-20 (Windows check + merge). The remaining perf leg is PR #5 (ultra-open-fix), held on libphext-cs 0.6.0 reaching NuGet; current state of that blocker is to be verified live as part of the Wavelet 4 Phextron plan (task 34.6.10/7.6.9/7.5.8).
# Script the proof-tool install in libphext-rs + wire into exocortical setup.sh

Coordinate: 41.8.7/10.9.12/8.8.12
Issued: 2026-11-07 01:17 CST
Request (verbatim): please add a script to libphext-rs so that we can get those tools installed; also incorporate them into setup.sh in exocortical
Status: complete 2026-11-07 — script committed on provable-0.4.1, Phase 11 live in exocortical

Notes:
- Parent task 47.11.7/12.13.16/12.11.16. Recipe lessons to encode: opam install ./src (the ./ is load-bearing; bare 'src' silently no-ops), charon-ml deps via opam install ./charon, aeneas make SERIALLY (parallel MAKEFLAGS races dune's _build lock), charon built with RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN from its rust-toolchain file (nightly-2026-09-17, host target only), Lean version read from aeneas/backends/lean/lean-toolchain (v4.35.0), set -euo pipefail throughout.
- Closed 2026-11-07. scripts/install-proof-tools.sh committed on provable-0.4.1 (cd18d83; published to the remote branch in the PR #7 stack, mode 100755 verified) and exocortical setup.sh gained Phase 11 running it from its /source/libphext-rs clone (published to wbic16/exocortical exo as 34452c9c). The script codifies the recipe verified manually on aletheia-core; not yet run end-to-end from a clean machine.
# PXE service — MAC registration and control page (current OS, IP, hostname)

Coordinate: 41.9.11/9.9.13/9.9.15
Issued: Will, 2026-11-17 21:05 CST (web, PH: Evolution chat)
Request (verbatim): Specify the phccbox PXE service (task 25.6.7/7.6.9/7.5.9): machines register by MAC address; a control page lists each registered machine's current OS, IP, and hostname.
Status: recorded — PXE service specification; build rides with the phccbox programme

Notes:
- Recorded in the finish-phcc GOAL.md design rulings.
- Emise's note: the MAC registry is also the table the install-time pruner keys on — MAC identifies the machine, the registry says what it runs and where it is.
# phcc phext capability parity with libphext-rs (C developer library)

Coordinate: 41.10.7/11.11.14/11.10.15
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): make sure phcc has every capability libphext-rs has, so developers can quickly handle phext data
Status: COMPLETE + PUBLISHED (0.5.0) — wbic16/phcc main == exo == 53a15166 (7bd02706 F45 source + 53a15166 phext refresh, on f65e68cc). Publisher verification from a fresh clone: phcc.phext sha256 9cd6bd60…, seal 59799edd…; unpack 613/613 SHA-verified; make test ALL PASSED; parity suite 163,987 checks / 0 failures under gcc with PHEXT_WITH_XZ and 163,987 / 0 under the tree's own phcc; conformance spot 332/333, diverge set exactly [a_pp_018], 0 oracle splits; static cells 3/3 (23 IRELATIVE in .rela.plt in first LOAD, static Lua byte-identical, static phccbox byte-identical, awk 42). Prior 0.4.1 state: COMPLETE + PUSHED @ 8b56ea22.

Notes:
- Phase A parity matrix: ~/workspace/phcc-libphext/PARITY.md (also committed as phext/PARITY.md). 77 capabilities audited from libphext-rs v0.4.1 source: 26 constants, 7 types, 17 Coordinate-surface items, 27 free functions - 77 with C counterparts, 0 gaps.
- Divergences of record: D-2 strict parse returns PHEXT_EFORMAT/PHEXT_ENUMBER where Rust TryFrom panics; D-3 C API byte-oriented, no UTF-8 validation; D-4 map sorted (implode identical); D-5 summary display truncation; D-6 lenient parse wraps like Rust release.
- Phase B: new top-level phext/ dir in a copy of the phcc tree on base 395f5d63 (F1) - phext.h (380 lines), phext.c (1,921 lines, incl. scalar XXH3-128 port), README, tests. Additive only; tcc.h/tccpp.c preprocessor counters untouched - wiring them to the library is the named F3-candidate follow-on, not done.
- Phase C: ported libphext-rs tests (49 test_lib + 8 test_phokenize + 1 regressions = 58 functions, same vectors): 163,831 checks, 0 failures under gcc AND under the freshly built phcc itself on aletheia-core (dogfood; phcc make test also passes). Differential fuzz vs Rust reference driver on libphext-rs 0.4.1: 40,000 cases, 2 seeds, 24 op classes, 0 divergences on defined behaviour (339 Rust panics total, all the D-2 parse class). Fuzz harness kept outside the repo at ~/workspace/phcc-libphext/fuzz/.
- Phase D: PATCHES.md gained per-file rows + entry F2. LOCAL commit 66ef47108f6580995a654a32e4ecb990b837420d on top of 395f5d63 (9 files, +4,674). NOT PUSHED - parent sequences the push (remote main has since advanced via the consolidation and pack/unpack passes, so the push will need a rebase/merge decision by the parent).
- 0.5.0 move (2026-11-08, PATCHES.md F45): re-audited against the PUBLISHED crates.io libphext 0.5.0 package (crate SHA-256 c8f8df75..., index-verified; not a git branch). Delta = 16 capabilities (binary module: 10 functions + header constant; seal module: 4 functions + SEAL_PRESET) plus one core behaviour change found by the fuzz: lenient to_coordinate now saturates at u64::MAX (0.4.1 wrapped). Totals: 93 capabilities, 93 with C counterparts, 0 gaps. New divergences D-7 (cargo feature gating mapped to build-time PHEXT_WITH_XZ for the seal; binary always compiled, base64 self-contained) and D-8 (seal io error vocabulary -> PHEXT_EINVAL/PHEXT_ENOSEAL). D-2 now only the EFORMAT/ENUMBER spelling split (0.5.0 TryFrom returns Err; fuzz op-20 panics: 0). Work on rock-mountain, base f65e68cc (cloned at D9 tip 611b763e; the h8 receipt-port commit landed during the run and was fast-forwarded to before work began). LOCAL commits 7bd02706 (F45 source) + 53a15166 (phext refresh) — coordinator publishes.

Results:
- libphext-rs 0.4.1 parity inside phcc: 77/77 capabilities with C counterparts, 0 gaps (phext/PARITY.md).
- Conformance: 163,831 checks, 0 failures under gcc; 163,831 checks, 0 failures under phcc itself (dogfood).
- Differential fuzz: 40,000 cases, 0 divergences on defined behaviour.
- Local commit ready to push: 66ef47108f6580995a654a32e4ecb990b837420d (on top of 395f5d63).
- libphext-rs 0.5.0 parity: 93/93 capabilities with C counterparts, 0 gaps (phext/PARITY.md sections 5-7 + 0.5.0 outcome).
- Conformance: 163,955 checks plain / 163,987 with PHEXT_WITH_XZ, 0 failures under gcc AND under phcc itself (dogfood). Differential fuzz vs the published 0.5.0: 20,000 regression cases (ops 0-23) + 40,000 new cases (ops 24-38, binary payloads + seal cross-checks), 0 divergences, 0 Rust panics. Seal byte-identical to Rust's; C unseal of the shipped phcc.phext.xz reproduces phcc.phext byte-identically (the repo seal is the refresh tooling's preset 9-extreme stream, same format).
- Tree receipts on the final tree: make test ALL TESTS PASSED; conformance spot 332/333 (diverge set exactly [a_pp_018]); static gate cells 3/3. Phext refresh census: 613 manifest rows, 0 mismatches; scroll-diff vs base = exactly the 6 intended scrolls; WP receipt scroll (1.1.1/10.2.7/1.2.1) byte-identical, untouched.
- 0.5.0 move PUBLISHED 2026-11-08: wbic16/phcc main == exo == 53a15166; fresh-clone verification all green (phext hash, unpack 613/613, make test, parity 163,987/0 gcc+XZ and phcc, conformance 332/333, static cells 3/3).
# Make SQ and phext-shell handle the teixml 0.3 test outputs well

Coordinate: 41.10.8/10.10.14/12.9.13
Issued: 2026-11-14
Request (verbatim): TEI XML

https://teibyexample.org/exist/tools/software.htm
https://www.tei-c.org/tools/

We're going to provide users with a first-class upgrade from TEI-XML to Phextura. Using multiversal phext and standoff properties, encode all salient points of TEI-XML. Generate a fast Rust-based migrator called teixml-to-mutable.

Source: https://github.com/wbic16/teixml-to-mutable
Publish Target: crates.io
Output Formats: raw phext (0.1), mutable (0.2), phextura (0.3)

The goal is to help Ian populate content for Mutable OS at phext speed. Ask me any clarifying questions needed.
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-14: SQ gap was deployment staleness only (node had Oct sq 0.6.0/libphext 0.3.3); sq 0.6.1 installed - counts exact (142,619/386,175/8,144), 1,800 sampled REST reads byte-identical incl. previously-capped coordinates. phext-shell 0.6.0 reads all three artifacts byte-identical (base 0.22s/128 MiB, standoff 0.91s/~694 MiB, image 1.92s/~1.49 GiB peak). One real defect found+fixed: REPL spun forever on stdin EOF - branch emise/shell-corpus-scale @ 343ebfe, PR https://github.com/wbic16/phext-shell/pull/6 open for Will; queue a phext-shell release task when it merges.

Notes:
- Will's words: 'make SQ and phext-shell handle the test outputs well' (2026-11-14 03:32 CST), spoken on merging teixml PR #3 + phextura PR #1.
- Record: ~/workspace/teixml-to-mutable-work/SQ-SHELL-E2E.md. Measured behavior noted, not changed: phext-shell 'lp' on the VFS image prints a ~533 MB transcript (libphext create_summary takes content to first break; VFS chunks are single-line 64 KiB base64).
- phext-shell PR #6 (EOF fix) also MERGED by Will 2026-11-14 (merged_at 10:09:45Z; main now 0adb19c). Release build queued as task 46.7.8/9.7.14/7.7.10.
# Slice 5: value-stack state machine (design machine #2, tccgen.c)

Coordinate: 42.4.6/5.5.11/7.5.11
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): continue (Will, 2026-11-07, alongside the libphext-rs PR direction)
Status: COMPLETE + PUBLISHED: Slice 5 output (6029562c…) merged with the hardened receipts into the canonical phext 646144c7… and pushed as wbic16/phcc 7573c4b8 (main=exo). Gate v5 on the merged file: machine #2 PASS, binding CURRENT; whole file byte-reproducible.

Notes:
- Base note: built on the consolidated canonical phext (61638c14...) per brief; the receipts-port copy (cebcd917...) is a sibling lineage on the same base - merging the two additive scroll sets is the parent's sequencing call.

Results:
- Machine scroll at Design 1.1.1/3.2.3/1.1.2: 8 states / 25 events / 73 transitions / 9 invariants, derived from tccgen.c in the consolidated phext; 7 interpretation notes marked (N3: I3 rests mostly on mechanism + enumerated call-site discipline; N6: expr_cond parks its then-value off-stack).
- Static: tools/check_vstack.py PASS, 0 violations; 25/25 event functions resolve to Vol 3 def members of tccgen.c. First runs caught a checker regex defect (ev_gv2 dropped) and real scroll errors (vcheck_cmp materializes via gv(RC_INT), not gvtst_set) - scroll corrected to the code.
- Dynamic (ranch, phcc @ 8b56ea22): authored 26/26 PASS (24 model tests: model == phcc == gcc, traces legal vs the scroll; O01/O02 oracle-only phcc == gcc); tests2 corpus 24/24 match .expect. Trace tests at Tests 1.1.1/5.2.3/1.1.229-254.
- Regressions: 5 filed at Regressions 1.1.1/6.2.3/1.1.1-5, all Changelog-sourced (0.9.22:204 value stack full -> I1; 0.9.13:320 + 0.9.7:411 long long register spill -> I7; 0.9.10:359 lvalue type saved -> I7; 0.9.7:412 ?: register spill -> expr_cond save_regs).
- Gate v5.0.0: Slice 1-4 sections reproduce byte-identically on the base (baseline + machine-#2-absent block only); verdict at Meta 1.1.1/1.2.10/1.12.1 (sha 786fc893...), register at Sec 13, binding CURRENT; verdict reproduces byte-identically.
- Exit test PASS: vcheck_cmp() removed from vsetc in a scratch ranch copy -> exactly the 4 CMP-burying tests diverged (V06: 0 vs 1; V08: 1 vs 0; V09: 0 vs 10; V10: garbage vs 0 1 0 1), 22 others held; violated transition CMP --ev_check_cmp [...]--> REG named. V10 reclassified as burying by the exit test itself.
- Output: ~/workspace/phcc-slice5/phcc.phext, 49,197,656 B, SHA-256 6029562c5e84fc2b9feec6299d089e4c8945df3d0e428884e8620f61fd0b1b3a; additive proof: 52,781 base scrolls 0 missing / 0 changed, exactly 34 added. Report: ~/workspace/phcc-slice5/REPORT.md.
# Sort the long-term deployment process for mutable.phext.io

Coordinate: 42.4.7/5.5.10/4.4.9
Issued: 2026-11-09 20:02 CST
Request (verbatim): let's get the long-term deployment process for https://mutable.phext.io/ sorted out - I want to deploy from https://github.com/wbic16/mutable-os, but have the deployment runner automatically sync from upstream at https://github.com/argimenes/mutable-os. Make any adjustments necessary - and also open a PR to merge the phext support (only) into upstream - keep the SSO process as a set of patches we apply during deployment.
Status: complete — purity PURE, CI/CD built + dry-run-verified, upstream PR prepared but blocked on credentials

Notes:
- Existing discipline: mutable-upstream-sync skill (two-band stack; phext band upstream-bound; SSO band never upstream; nightly trial sync exists; promotion is per-sync approved, standing ratification PENDING — the runner must stop at an approval gate, no unattended go-live).
- Will ratified unattended go-live (2026-11-09 20:04 CST): 'unattended go-live for mutable.phext.io is fine - we will be watching his upstream repo for updates and automatically deploying them as a continuous CI/CD process.' The approval gate is removed; verification itself is the gate (failed build/tests/conflict/purity blocks the deploy and reports). Amendment sent to the dispatched worker; skill + MEMORY updates follow in this session.
- Result (2026-11-09 20:08 CST): Part A PURE (3 independent checks over the 154-file band diff; standing script check-band-purity.sh in the sync-pipeline). Part B BLOCKED: no duplicate PR exists; VM token gets 403 on argimenes/mutable-os (fine-grained repo selection doesn't cover it); aletheia-core's gh token is expired. PR title/body staged on aletheia-core /tmp/pr-title.txt + /tmp/pr-body.md. Unblock is Will's: extend the token's repo access, re-auth gh on aletheia-core, or open from the web UI. Part C: promote-and-deploy.sh (5 stages) + deploy-pipeline.conf + cron mutable-cicd-deploy ~04:44 CST daily; dry run exit 0, nothing deployed. SSO-at-deploy-time realized via env-gating (sso-auth.ts inert without box-only secrets) — flagged for Will's confirmation. One unproven link: sudo -n -u ubuntu from wbic16's key-only session may not be policy-granted (exit 44 if not; one-time sudoers drop-in fixes it).

Results:
- deployment-process.md in the mutable goal's files/; promote-and-deploy.sh + check-band-purity.sh + deploy-pipeline.conf in hidden_files/sync-pipeline/; cron mutable-cicd-deploy (~04:44 CST)
