# qexo v1.0.4 Windows link fix: per-platform volume probe (statvfs / GetDiskFreeSpaceExW)

Coordinate: 42.7.8/7.7.10/7.7.12
Issued: 2026-11-12 23:41 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-12 23:41 CST), building exo@1b819c2 (v1.0.3) on Windows: 'unresolved external symbol statvfs'. Diagnosis: probe_disk in src/core.rs declared POSIX statvfs unconditionally; Windows has no such symbol, so the build failed at link time — invisible to the v1.0.1 gates, which ran cargo check (never links) for the Windows targets. Fix: volume_at() split per platform — statvfs on unix (semantics unchanged), GetDiskFreeSpaceExW on Windows mapped into the same Volume terms, None elsewhere; the gate set gains a full Windows link.
Status: MERGED 2026-11-12 by Will (PR #13; exo head 560e97e0). v1.0.4 on exo. PR #14 rebase onto it directed by Will the same evening.

Results:
- Gates (aletheia-core): cargo test 37/37 (36 baseline + win32 mapping test); release build OK; wiring-check OK; cargo check --tests PASS windows-gnu + windows-msvc; FULL LINK cargo build --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu produced qexo.exe (PE32+, imports GetDiskFreeSpaceExW, no statvfs reference); unix battery: bare qexo on incident volume GREEN, 755 GiB of 3,663 GiB, matches df. Extern audit: statvfs was the only unconditional unix extern in src/. Record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/statvfsfix/BUILD-RECORD.md
# tluf.org paper submissions + a unified paper addressing scheme

Coordinate: 42.9.6/12.6.15/5.8.10
Issued: 2026-11-15 17:51 CST
Request (verbatim): Two deliverables. (1) A paper addressing scheme that unifies every source tluf meets, built as a profile of phextura's Layer-2 scheme (px2:) from ~/workspace/phextura-design/LAYER2.md - NOT a fresh invention: extend the work-ref registry with the schemes the tracker has actually filed from (arxiv, doi, hexagon, vixra, url for bare-web resources with no repository ID, tluf for native deposits), canonicalization + edition-pin rules, worked examples from the real corpus (arXiv 2611.14552; the Lightspeed URL of Paper 022; hexagon:2611.00496v1; the ciphergoth.org PDF of fringe F001). Spec at ~/workspace/oracle-service/ADDRESSING.md; gaps in L2-as-designed recorded as gaps in the spec. Wired into the Assay record as a dated addendum pointer in REQUIREMENTS.md (no renumbering) and a note in BUILD-PLAN.md. (2) The submission feature on tluf.org: a submit page in the site's existing design (extend the t-l-u-f-banner artifact and re-export; a standalone page in the same visual language is the fallback) whose form derives and displays the canonical px2 address live as a locator is pasted; a minimal backend service for awsbox (Python stdlib, runs as wbic16 on loopback, one file per submission in mailbox pattern under ~/tluf-submissions/, size-capped, no auth - submission is open, assessment and merge stay gated house acts). Stage everything hash-verified with docroot modes normalized (644 files / 755 dirs - the publish lesson); the nginx proxy block for /api/submit goes into the deploy kit as an updated install script for Will's root run; verify the service end-to-end on its loopback port before handoff. Inscribe ADDRESSING.md in artifacts.phext per the inscription skill.
Status: open - built 2026-11-15; waiting on Will: root run of install-submit.sh on awsbox, then public end-to-end verification

