Coordinate: 46.5.6/5.5.10/5.5.11
Issued: 2026-11-21 07:58 CST
Request (verbatim): follow through on those issues (phccbox/phcc status items)
Status: closed — both defects fixed, verified, PR #1 merged by Will 2026-11-21

Notes:
- 2026-11-21 07:58 CST: created under Will's follow-through directive. Defect 1: phcc-windows-i386 Jenkins job fails on unresolved _SetUnhandledExceptionFilter (i386 PE import resolution vs stdcall-decorated name) — a genuine phcc defect found 2026-11-20 during the Jenkins build-out (task 29.6.8/6.5.9/5.5.8). Defect 2: tccasm.c:964 uses tolower without <ctype.h> (hard error under NDK clang 17; Android builds carry a workaround flag — the proper fix removes the need for it). Proper fixes, not patches.
- 2026-11-21: BOTH FIXES DONE on branch emise/phcc-i386-stdcall-fix (parented on exo 2f7583db), PR https://github.com/wbic16/phcc/pull/1 (commits 49208085 ctype, f77ea7d4 tccelf guard). Defect 1 root cause: the fork's F28 ELF versioned-symbol handling in tcc_load_object_file (tccelf.c) split undefined names at '@' and registered the base name as a name@VER reference; on i386 PE '@N' is stdcall decoration, so the win32 CRT's _SetUnhandledExceptionFilter@4 was registered undecorated and tccpe.c's stdcall-stripping import lookup (which needs the '@') failed. tccpe.c/tcccoff.c/kernel32.def/crt1.c are byte-identical to upstream and upstream links fine — isolated by diff + instrumented pe_check_symbols. Fix: #ifndef TCC_TARGET_PE guard on the F28 branch (+10 lines). Defect 2: #include <ctype.h> in tccasm.c (+1). Verified on aletheia-core: native make test ALL TESTS PASSED; Jenkins i386 job replicated step-for-step — hello links, PE32 (was: unresolved reference); x86_64-win32 Wine exit 42; ELF versioned-ref probe (foo@VER1 -> foo@@VER1) still binds and runs; zero implicit-declaration warnings. Jenkins phcc-windows-i386 still shows build #1 FAILURE (2026-11-20) — it polls exo and rebuilds on change, so it should go green on the first build after the PR merges; not merged by Emise. Wine cannot run the 32-bit exe on the hub (wine64 only). Android job's -Wno-implicit-function-declaration shim no longer needed for this defect (wasm/emcc side unaudited). Report: ~/workspace/phcc-fixes/REPORT.md.
- 2026-11-21 08:16 CST: PR https://github.com/wbic16/phcc/pull/1 MERGED by Will (verified live via GitHub API: state closed, merged_at 2026-11-21T14:16:26Z). Jenkins phcc-windows-i386 job polls exo every 5 min and rebuilds on change — expected green on its first post-merge build; confirm at next Jenkins pass. Task closed.
